\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 In this chapter, in response to a question by Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 gives his conclusions concerning how the Supreme Personality of Godhead, although the Supersoul, friend and protector of everyone, killed the Daityas, the demons, for th
e sake of Indra, the King of heaven. In his statements, he totally refutes the arguments of people in general who accuse the Supreme Lord of partiality. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 proves that because the body of the conditioned soul is infected by the three qualitie
s of nature, dualities arise such as enmity and friendship, attachment and detachment. For the Supreme Personality of Godhead, however, there are no such dualities. Even eternal time cannot control the activities of the Lord. Eternal time is created by th
e Lord, and it acts under His control. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, therefore, is always transcendental to the influence of the modes of nature, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4,}{\insrsid30033 
 the Lord's external energy, which acts in creation and annihilation. Thus all the demons killed by the Supreme Lord attain salvation immediately.
\par The second question raised by Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja concerns how \'c7i\'e7up\'e4la, although inimical toward K\'e5\'f1\'eba from his very childhood and always blaspheming K\'e5\'f1\'eba, attained salvation in oneness when K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a killed him. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 explains that because of their offenses at the feet of devotees, two attendants of the Lord in Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha named Jaya and Vijaya became Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a in Satya-yuga, R\'e4va\'eb
a and Kumbhakar\'eba in the next }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yuga,}{\insrsid30033  Tret\'e4-yuga, and \'c7i\'e7up\'e4la and Dantavakra at the end of Dv\'e4
para-yuga. Because of their fruitive acts, Jaya and Vijaya agreed to become the Lord's enemies, and when killed in that mentality, they attained salvation in oneness. Thus even if one thinks of the Supreme Personality o
f Godhead in envy, he attains salvation. What then is to be said of devotees who always engage in the Lord's service with love and faith?
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.1.1
