\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  are reactions of these modes, not of the Supreme Lord's partiality. \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9, in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bh\'e4
gavata-sandarbha,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  has clearly said:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sattv\'e4dayo na sant\'e9\'e7e\line yatra ca pr\'e4k\'e5t\'e4 gu\'eb\'e4\'f9\line sa \'e7
uddha\'f9 sarva-\'e7uddhebhya\'f9\line pum\'e4n \'e4dhya\'f9 pras\'e9datu
\par hl\'e4din\'e9 sandhin\'e9 samvit\line tvayy ek\'e4 sarva-sa\'e0sthitau\line hl\'e4da-t\'e4pa-kar\'e9 mi\'e7r\'e4\line tvayi no gu\'eba-varjite
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 According to this statement of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bh\'e4gavata-sandarbha,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the Supreme Lord, being always transcendental to the material qualities, is never affected by the influence of these qualities. This same characteristic is also present in the living being, but because he is conditioned by material nature, e
ven the pleasure potency of the Lord is manifested in the conditioned soul as troublesome. In the material world the pleasure enjoyed by the conditioned soul is followed by many painful conditions. For instance, we have seen that in the two great wars, wh
ich were conducted by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 rajo-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 both parties were actually ruined. The German people declared war against the English to ruin them, but the result was that both parties were ruined. Although the Allies were apparently victorious, at least
 on paper, actually neither of them were victorious. Therefore it should be concluded that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is not partial to anyone. Everyone works under the influence of various modes of material nature, and when the various modes are 
prominent, the demigods or demons appear victorious under the influence of these modes.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
Everyone enjoys the fruits of his qualitative activities. This is also confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (14.11-13):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-dv\'e4re\'f1u dehe 'smin\line prak\'e4\'e7a upaj\'e4yate\line j\'ef\'e4na\'e0 yad\'e4
 tad\'e4 vidy\'e4d\line viv\'e5ddha\'e0 sattvam ity uta
\par lobha\'f9 prav\'e5ttir \'e4rambha\'f9\line karma\'eb\'e4m a\'e7ama\'f9 sp\'e5h\'e4\line rajasy et\'e4ni j\'e4yante\line viv\'e5ddhe bharatar\'f1abha
\par aprak\'e4\'e7o 'prav\'e5tti\'e7 ca\line pram\'e4do moha eva ca\line tamasy et\'e4ni j\'e4yante\line viv\'e5ddhe kuru-nandana
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "The manifestations of the modes of goodness
 can be experienced when all the gates of the body are illumined by knowledge.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 "O chief of the Bh\'e4
ratas, when there is an increase in the mode of passion, the symptoms of great attachment, uncontrollable desire, hankering, and intense endeavor develop.
\par "O son of Kuru, when there is an increase in the mode of ignorance, madness, illusion, inertia and darkness are manifested."
\par The Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is present in everyone's heart, simply gives the results of the increase in the various qualities, but He is impartial. He supervises victory and loss, but He does not take part in them.
\par The various modes of material nature do not work all at once. The interactions of these modes are exactly like seasonal changes. Sometimes there is an increment of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 rajo-gu\'eba,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  sometimes of }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and sometimes }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Generally the demigods are surcharged with }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba,}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and therefore when the demons and the demigods fight, the demigods are victorious because of the prominence of their }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  qualities
. However, this is not the partiality of the Supreme Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.1.9
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 9
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid30033 \b\v\f75\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 JYaaeiTaraidirva>aaiTa Sa\'baaTaa\'e0 ivivCYaTae )\line 
ivdNTYaaTMaaNaMaaTMaSQa& MaiQaTva k-vYaae_NTaTa" )) 9 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 jyotir-\'e4dir iv\'e4bh\'e4ti
\par sa\'ecgh\'e4t\'e4n na vivicyate
\par vidanty \'e4tm\'e4nam \'e4tma-stha\'e0
\par mathitv\'e4 kavayo 'ntata\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 jyoti\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash fire; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4di\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash and other elements; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iva}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash just as; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4bh\'e4ti}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash appear; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa\'ecgh\'e4t\'e4t}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash from the bodies of demigods and others; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vivicyate}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash are distinguished; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vidanti}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 
\emdash perceive; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4nam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the Supersoul; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4tma-stham}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash situated in the heart; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mathitv\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by discerning; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kavaya\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash expert thinkers; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 antata
\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash within.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
The all-pervading Personality of Godhead exists within the heart of every living being, and an expert thinker can perceive how He is present there to a large or small extent. Ju
st as one can understand the supply of fire in wood, the water in a waterpot, or the sky within a pot, one can understand whether a living entity is a demon or a demigod by understanding that living entity's devotional performances. A thoughtful man can u
nderstand how much a person is favored by the Supreme Lord by seeing his actions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (10.41) the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yad yad vibh\'fctimat sattva\'e0\line \'e7r\'e9mad \'fcrjitam eva v\'e4\line tat tad ev\'e4
vagaccha tva\'e0\line mama tejo-'\'e0\'e7a-sambhavam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Know that all beautiful, gl
orious and mighty creations spring from but a spark of My splendor." We have the practical experience of seeing that one person is able to do very wonderful things whereas another cannot do those same things and cannot even do things that require only a l
ittle common sense. Therefore, how much a devotee has been favored by the Supreme Personality of Godhead can be tested by the activities the devotee has performed. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (10.10) the Lord also says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 satata-yukt\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line bhajat\'e4\'e0 pr\'e9ti-p\'fcrvakam\line dad
\'e4mi buddhi-yoga\'e0 ta\'e0\line yena m\'e4m upay\'e4nti te}{\cs1998\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"To those who are constantly devoted and who worship Me with love, I give the understanding by which they can come to Me." This is very practical. A teacher instructs the student if the student is capable of taki
ng more and more instructions. Otherwise, in spite of being instructed by the teacher, the student cannot make strides in his understanding. This has nothing to do with partiality. When K\'e5\'f1\'eba says }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 te\'f1\'e4\'e0
 satata-yukt\'e4n\'e4\'e0 bhajat\'e4\'e0 pr\'e9ti-p\'fcrvakam/ dad\'e4mi buddhi-yoga\'e0 tam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  this indicates that K\'e5\'f1\'eba is prepared to give }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 to everyone, but one must be capable of receiving it. That is the secret. Thus when a person exhibits wonderful devotional activities, a thoughtful man understands that K\'e5\'f1\'eba has been more favorable to this devotee.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
This is not difficult to understand, but envious persons do not accept that K\'e5\'f1\'eba has bestowed His favor upon a particular devotee in accordance with his advanced position. Such foolish persons become envious and try to minim
ize an advanced devotee's activities. That is not Vai\'f1\'ebavism. A Vai\'f1\'ebava should appreciate the service rendered to the Lord by other Vai\'f1\'ebavas. Therefore a Vai\'f1\'ebava is described in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh
\'e4gavatam}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nirmatsara.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Vai\'f1\'ebavas are never envious of other Vai\'f1\'eb
avas or of anyone else, and therefore they are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nirmatsar\'e4\'eb\'e4\'e0 sat\'e4m.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 As }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  informs us, one can understand how one is saturated with }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba.}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  In the examples given herewith, fire represents the mode of goodness. 
One can understand the constitution of a container for wood, petrol or other inflammable substances by the quantity of the fire. Similarly, water represents }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 rajo-gu\'eba,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 the mode of passion. A small skin and the vast Atlantic Ocean both contain water, and by
 seeing the quantity of water in a container one can understand the size of the container. The sky represents the mode of ignorance. The sky is present in a small earthen pot and also in outer space. Thus by proper judgment one can see who is a }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 devat\'e4,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or demigod, and who is an }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asura,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Yak\'f1a or R\'e4k\'f1asa according to the quantities of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 
sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  One cannot judge whether a person is a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 devat\'e4,}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  an }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asura}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or a R\'e4k\'f1asa by seeing him, but a sane man can understand this by the activities suc
h a person performs. A general description is given in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 the Padma Pur\'e4\'eba:}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 vi\'f1\'ebu-bhakta\'f9 sm\'e5to daiva \'e4suras tad-viparyaya\'f9.}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  A devotee of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is a demigod, whereas an }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asura}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or Yak\'f1a is just the opposite. An }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asura}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is not a devotee of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu; instead, for his sense gratification he is a devotee of the demigods, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bh\'fctas, pretas}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 and so on. Thus one can judge who is a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 devat\'e4,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  who is a R\'e4k\'f1asa and who is an }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asura}{\insrsid30033  by how they conduct their activities.
\par The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4nam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  in this verse means }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 param\'e4tm\'e4nam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The Param\'e4tm\'e4
, or Supersoul, is situated in the core of everyone's heart (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 antata\'f9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (18.61). }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0 h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7vara,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 the Supreme Personality of Godhead, being situated in everyone's heart, gives directions to everyone in terms of one's capabilities in taking the instructions. The instructions of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  are open to everyone, but some people understand them properly, whereas others understand them so improperly that they cannot even believe in the existence of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, although reading K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a's book. Although the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 G\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  says }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7r\'e9-bhagav\'e4n uv\'e4ca,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  indicating that K\'e5\'f1\'eba spoke, they cannot understand K\'e5
\'f1\'eba. This is due to their misfortune or incapability, which is caused by }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 rajo-gu\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 the modes of passion and ignorance. It is because of these modes that they cannot even understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba, whereas an advanced devotee like Arjuna understands Him and glorifies Him, saying, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 para\'e0 brahma para\'e0 dh\'e4
ma pavitra\'e0 parama\'e0 bhav\'e4n:}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\insrsid30033 "You are the Supreme Brahman, the supreme abode and purifier." K\'e5\'f1\'eba is open to everyone, but one needs the capability to understand Him.
\par By external features one cannot understand who is favored by K\'e5\'f1\'eba and who is not. According to one's attitude, K\'e5\'f1\'eba becomes one's direct adviser, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba becomes unknown. This is not K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a's partiality; it is His response to one's ability to understand Him. According to one's receptiveness\emdash whether one be a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 devat\'e4, asura,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Yak\'f1a or R\'e4k\'f1asa\emdash K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a's quality is proportionately exhibited. This proportionate exhibition of K\'e5\'f1\'eba's power is misunderstood by less intelligent men to be K\'e5\'f1\'eba's partiality, but actually it is no such thing. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is equal to everyone, and according to one's ability to receive the favor of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, one advances in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kura gives a practical example in this connection. In the sky there are many luminaries. At night, even in darkness, the moon is extremely brilliant and can be directly perceived. The sun is also extremely b
rilliant. When covered by clouds, however, these luminaries are not distinctly visible. Similarly, the more one advances in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 the more his brilliance is exhibited by devotional service, but the more one is covered by }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 rajo-gu\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  the
 less visible his brilliance, for he is covered by these qualities. The visibility of one's qualities does not depend on the partiality of the Supreme Personality of Godhead; it is due to various coverings in different proportions. Thus one can understand
 how far he has advanced in terms of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and how much he is covered by }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 rajo-gu\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.1.10
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 10
