\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash this; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tat}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of that (body); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vadh\'e4t}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
from the annihilation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pr\'e4\'ebin\'e4m}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the living beings; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vadha\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash annihilation; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tath\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash similarly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yasya}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of whom; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kaivaly\'e4t}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash because of being absolute, one without a second; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 abhim\'e4na\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash false conception; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 akhila-\'e4tmana\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the Supersoul of all living entities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 parasya}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dama-kartu\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the supreme controller; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hi}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash certainly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hi\'e0s\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash harm; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kena}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash how; }
{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 asya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash His; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kalpyate}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash is performed.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 Because of the bodily con
ception of life, the conditioned soul thinks that when the body is annihilated the living being is annihilated. Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is the supreme controller, the Supersoul of all living entities. Because He has no material body
, He has no false conception of "I and mine." It is therefore incorrect to think that He feels pleasure or pain when blasphemed or offered prayers. This is impossible for Him. Thus He has no enemy and no friend. When He chastises the demons it is for thei
r good, and when He accepts the prayers of the devotees it is for their good. He is affected neither by prayers nor by blasphemy.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
Because of being covered by material bodies, the conditioned souls, including even greatly learned scholars and falsely
 educated professors, all think that as soon as the body is finished, everything is finished. This is due to their bodily conception of life. K\'e5\'f1\'eba has no such bodily conception, nor is His body different from His self. Therefore, since K\'e5\'f1
\'eba has no material conception of life, how can He be affected by material prayers and accusations? K\'e5\'f1\'eba's body is described herewith as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kaivalya,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 nondifferent from Himself. Since everyone has a material bodily conception of life, if K\'e5\'f1\'eba had such a conception what would be the difference between K\'e5\'f1\'eba and the conditioned soul? K\'e5\'f1\'eba's instructions in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  are accepted as final because He does not possess a material body. As soon as one has a material body he has four deficiencies, but since K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a does not possess a material body, He has no deficiencies. He is always spiritually conscious and blissful. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c9\'e7vara\'f9 parama\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9:}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  His form is eternal, blissful knowledge. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9, \'e4nanda-cinmaya-rasa}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kaivalya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  are the same.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 K\'e5\'f1\'eba can expand Himself as Param\'e4tm\'e4
 in the core of everyone's heart. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (13.3) this is confirmed. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid12728211 K\'f1etra}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'efa
\'e0 c\'e4pi m\'e4\'e0 viddhi sama-k\'f1etre\'f1u bh\'e4rata:}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  the Lord is the Param\'e4tm\'e4\emdash the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 or Superself of all individual souls. Therefore it must natu
rally be concluded that He has no defective bodily conceptions. Although situated in everyone's body, He has no bodily conception of life. He is always free from such conceptions, and thus He cannot be affected by anything in relation to the material body
 of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'e9va.
\par }{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (16.19):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 t\'e4n aha\'e0 dvi\'f1ata\'f9 kr\'fcr\'e4n\line sa\'e0s\'e4re\'f1u nar\'e4dham\'e4n\line k
\'f1ip\'e4my ajasram a\'e7ubh\'e4n\line \'e4sur\'e9\'f1v eva yoni\'f1u
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"Those who are envious and mischievous, who are the lowest among men, are cast by Me into the ocean of material exist
ence, into various demoniac species of life." Whenever the Lord punishes persons like demons, however, such punishment is meant for the good of the conditioned soul. The conditioned soul, being envious of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, may accuse Him
, saying, "K\'e5\'f1\'eba is bad, K\'e5\'f1\'eba is a thief" and so on, but K\'e5\'f1\'eba, being kind to all living entities, does not consider such accusations. Instead, He takes account of the conditioned soul's chanting of "K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1
\'eba" so many times. He sometimes punishes such demons for one life by putting them in a lower species, but then, when they have stopped accusing Him, they are liberated in the next life because of chanting K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a's name constantly. Blaspheming the Supreme Lord or His devotee is not at all good for the conditioned soul, but K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, being very kind, punishes the conditioned soul in one life for such sinful activities and then takes him back home, back to Godhead. The vivid example for this is V\'e5tr\'e4sura, who was formerly Citraketu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, a great devotee. 
Because he derided Lord \'c7iva, the foremost of all devotees, he had to accept the body of a demon called V\'e5tra, but then he was taken back to Godhead. Thus when K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a punishes a demon or conditioned soul, He stops that soul's habit of blaspheming Him, and when the soul becomes completely pure, the Lord takes him back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.1.26
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 26
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid30033 \b\v\f75\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TaSMaa\'dcEraNaubNDaeNa iNav\'8c\'84\'84re<a >aYaeNa va )\line \'f2
ehaTk-aMaeNa va YauHJYaaTa(-k-Qai\'c4\'e0e+aTae Pa*Qak(- )) 26 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 tasm\'e4d vair\'e4nubandhena
\par nirvaire\'eba bhayena v\'e4
\par sneh\'e4t k\'e4mena v\'e4 yu\'efjy\'e4t
\par katha\'efcin nek\'f1ate p\'e5thak
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tasm\'e4t}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash therefore; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vaira-anubandhena}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by constant enmity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 nirvaire\'eba}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by devotion; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhayena}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by fear; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 v\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash or; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sneh\'e4t}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash from affection; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e4mena}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by lusty desires; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 v\'e4}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash or; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yu\'efjy\'e4t}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash one should concentrate; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 katha\'efcit}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash somehow or other; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9k\'f1ate}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
sees; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 p\'e5thak}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash something else.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
Therefore by enmity or by devotional service, by fear, by affection or by lusty desire\emdash by all of these or any one of them\emdash if a conditioned soul somehow or other concentrates his mind up
on the Lord, the result is the same, for the Lord, because of His blissful position, is never affected by enmity or friendship.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 From this verse one should not conclude that because K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is unaffected by favorable prayers or unfavorable blasphemy one should therefore blaspheme the Supreme Lord. This is not the regulative principle. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhakti-yoga}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4nuk\'fclyena k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4nu\'e7\'e9lanam:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  one should serve K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a very favorably. This is the real injunction. Here it is said that although an enemy thinks of K\'e5\'f1\'eba unfavorably, the Lord is unaffected by such anti-devotional service. Thus He offers His benedictions even to \'c7i\'e7up\'e4
la and similarly inimical conditioned souls. This does not mean, however, that one should be inimical toward the Lord. The stress is given to the favorable execution of devotional service, not purposeful blasphemy of the Lord. It is said:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nind\'e4\'e0 bhagavata\'f9 \'e7\'e5\'ebva\'e0s\line tat-parasya janasya v\'e4\line tato n
