\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 One who hears blasphemy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead
 or His devotees should immediately take action or should leave. Otherwise he will be put into hellish life perpetually. There are many such injunctions. Therefore as a regulative principle one should not be unfavorable toward the Lord but always favorabl
y inclined toward Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 \'c7i\'e7up\'e4
la's achievement of oneness with the Supreme Lord was different because Jaya and Vijaya, from the very beginning of their material existence, were ordained to treat the Supreme Lord as an enemy for three lives and then return ho
me, back to Godhead. Jaya and Vijaya inwardly knew that K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but they purposely became His enemies to be delivered from material life. From the very beginning of their lives they thought of Lord K\'e5\'f1
\'eba as an enemy, and even though blaspheming Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, they chanted the holy name of K\'e5\'f1\'eba constantly along with their inimical thoughts. Thus they were purified because of chanting the holy name of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. It is to be understood that even a blasphemer can be freed from sin
ful activities by chanting the holy name of the Lord. Certainly, therefore, freedom is assured for a devotee who is always favorable to the service of the Lord. This will be clear from the following verse. By rapt attention fixed upon K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, one is purified, and thus one is delivered from material life.
\par \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura has very nicely explained the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhayena,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  which means "by fear." When the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 gop\'e9s}{\insrsid30033  went to K\'e5
\'f1\'eba in the dead of night, they certainly feared chastisement by their relatives\emdash their husbands, brothers and fathers\emdash but nonetheless, not caring for their relatives, they went to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. There was certainly fear, but this fear could not check their devotional service to K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par One should not mistakenly think that Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba must be worshiped by an inimical attitude like that of \'c7i\'e7up\'e4la. The injunction is }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4nuk\'fclyasya graha\'eba\'e0 pr\'e4tik\'fclyasya varjanam:}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  one should give up unfavorable activities and accept only favorable conditions in devotional service. Generally, if one blasphemes the Supreme Personality of Godhead he is punished. As the Lord says in }{
\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (16.19):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 t\'e4n aha\'e0 dvi\'f1ata\'f9 kr\'fcr\'e4n\line sa\'e0s\'e4re\'f1u nar\'e4dham\'e4n\line k
\'f1ip\'e4my ajasram a\'e7ubh\'e4n\line \'e4sur\'e9\'f1v eva yoni\'f1u
