of Him (the Supreme Personality of Godhead); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tyakta-svabh\'e4vasya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash who has given up His natural position (of being equal to everyone); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gh\'e5
\'ebe\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash most abominable; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash under the influence of the illusory energy; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
vana-okasa\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash behaving exactly like an animal in the jungle; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhajantam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash unto the devotee engaged in devotional service; }
{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhajam\'e4nasya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash being worshiped; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 b\'e4lasya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash a child; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iva}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash like; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 asthira-\'e4tmana\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash who is always restless and changing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mat}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash my; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcla}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by the trident; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhinna}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
separated; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gr\'e9vasya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash whose neck; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bh\'fcri\'eb\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash profuse; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
rudhire\'eba}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by blood; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vai}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 as\'e5k-priyam}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash who was fond of blood; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tarpayi\'f1ye}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash I shall please; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhr\'e4taram}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash brother; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 me}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash my; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gata-vyatha\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
becoming peaceful myself.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 The Supreme Personality of Godhead has given up His natural tendency 
of equality toward the demons and demigods. Although He is the Supreme Person, now, influenced by m\'e4y\'e4
, He has assumed the form of a boar to please His devotees, the demigods, just as a restless child leans toward someone. I shall therefore sever Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u's head from His trunk by my trident, and with the profuse blood from His body I shall please my brother Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a, who was so fond of sucking blood. Thus shall I too be peaceful.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid16528151 The defect of the demoniac mentality is expressed in this verse ve
ry clearly.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu thought that Vi\'f1\'ebu also becomes partial, like a child whose mind is not steady or resolute. The Lord can change His mind at any time, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu thought, and therefore His words and activities are like those of children. Actual
ly, because the demons are ordinary human beings, their minds change, and being materially conditioned, they think that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is conditioned also. As the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (9.11), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 avaj\'e4nanti m\'e4\'e0 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4 m\'e4nu\'f1\'e9\'e0 tanum \'e4\'e7ritam:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 "Fools deride Me when I descend in a human form."
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 Demons always think that Vi\'f1\'eb
u can be killed. Therefore, being absorbed in thoughts of Vi\'f1\'ebu's form to kill Him, at least they have the opportunity to think of Vi\'f1\'ebu unfavorably. Although they are not devotees, their thinking of Vi\'f1\'eb
u is effective, and thus they generally attain }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 s\'e4yujya-mukti.}{\insrsid30033  Because the demons consider the Supreme Lord an ordinary living being, they think that they can kill Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u as one might kill an ordinary person. Another fact disclosed herein is that demons are very much fond of sucking blood. Indeed, all of them are meat-eaters and bloodsuckers.
\par Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu accused the Supreme Lord of having a restless mind like that of a small child who can be induced to do anything if simply offered some cakes and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 l\'e4\'f2\'f2us.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 Indirectly, this indicates the true position of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who says in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (9.26):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 patra\'e0 pu\'f1pa\'e0 phala\'e0 toya\'e0\line yo me bhakty\'e4 prayacchati\line tad aha
\'e0 bhakty-upah\'e5tam\line a\'e7n\'e4mi prayat\'e4tmana\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "If
 one offers Me with love and devotion a leaf, a flower, fruit or water, I will accept it." The Lord accepts the offerings of devotees because of their transcendental love. Because they are in love with the Supreme Lord, they do not eat anything without of
fering it first to the Lord. The Lord does not hanker for a small leaf or flower; He has enough to eat. Indeed, He is feeding all living entities. Nonetheless, because He is very merciful and is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakta-vatsala,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  very favorable to the devotees, He certainly eats whatever they offer Him with love and devotion. This quality should not be misjudged to be childish. The highest quality of the Supreme Lord is that He is }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakta-vatsala;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  in other words, He is always extremely pleased with His devotees. As for the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 when used in reference to the dealings of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and His devotees, this word means "affection." The actions of the Lord to favor His devotees are not disqualifications but signs of His natural affection.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 As for }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 rudhira,}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or the blood of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, since there is no possibility of severing Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's head from His body, there is no question of blood. But the garland that decorates Vi\'f1\'eb
u's body is as red as blood. When the demons achieve }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4yujya-mukti}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and leave behind their sinful activities, they are blessed by Vi\'f1\'eb
u's garland, which is red like blood. After attaining }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4yujya-mukti,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  the demons are sometimes promoted to the Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha world, where they receive the reward of the Lord's garland }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pras\'e4da.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.2.9
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 9
