uZYaiNTa ivZ<auPa[a<aa idvaEk-Sa" )) 9 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 tasmin k\'fc\'f6e 'hite na\'f1\'f6e
\par k\'e5tta-m\'fcle vanas-patau
\par vi\'f6ap\'e4 iva \'e7u\'f1yanti
\par vi\'f1\'ebu-pr\'e4\'eb\'e4 divaukasa\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tasmin}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash when He; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'fc\'f6e}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the most deceitful; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ahite}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash enemy; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na\'f1\'f6e}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash is finished; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e5tta-m\'fcle}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash having its roots cut off; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vanas-patau}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash a tree; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vi\'f6ap\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the branches and leaves; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iva}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash like; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7u\'f1yanti}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash dry up; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vi\'f1\'ebu-pr\'e4\'eb\'e4\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash whose life is Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 diva-okasa\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the demigods.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 When the root of a tree is cut and the tr
ee falls down, its branches and twigs automatically dry up. Similarly, when I have killed this diplomatic Vi\'f1\'ebu, the demigods, for whom Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is the life and soul, will lose the source of their life and wither away.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s3008\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14425756 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 The difference between the 
demigods and the demons is here explained. The demigods always follow the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, whereas the demons simply plan to disturb or kill Him. Nevertheless, sometimes the demons very much appreciate the full dependenc
e of the demigods upon the mercy of the Lord. This is indirect glorification of the demigods by the demons.
