u, go down to the planet earth, which is flourishing due to brahminical culture and a k\'f1atriya government. These people engage in austerity, sacrifice, Vedic study, regulative vows, and charity. Destroy all the people thus engaged!
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu's main purpose was to disturb the demigods. He planned first to kill Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu so that with Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's death the demigods would automatically weaken and die. Another of his plans was to disturb
 the residents of the planet earth. The peace and prosperity of the residents of earth, and all the other planets, were maintained by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  The Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (4.13), }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 c\'e4tur-var\'ebya\'e0 may\'e4 s\'e5\'f1\'f6a\'e0 gu\'eba-karma-vibh\'e4ga\'e7a\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  "Acco
rding to the three modes of material nature and the work ascribed to them, the four divisions of human society were created by Me." On all the planets there are different types of residents, but the Lord recommends, referring especially to the planet eart
h, which is inhabited by human beings, that society be divided into four }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 var\'ebas-br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdra.
}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  Before the advent of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba on this earth, it is understood that the earth was managed by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  The duty of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  is to cultivate }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7ama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (peacefulness), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (self-control), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
titik\'f1\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (tolerance), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 satyam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (truthfulness), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7aucam}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (cleanliness) and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4rjavam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (simplicity), and then to advise the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriya}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  kings how to rule the country or planet. Following the instructions of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 should engage the populace in austerity, sacrifices, Vedic study and adherence to the rules and regulations established by Vedic principles. They should also arrange for charity to be given to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas, sanny
\'e4s\'e9s}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and temples. This is the godly arrangement of brahminical culture.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 People are inclined to offer }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'ef
a}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  because unless sacrifices are offered there will be insufficient rain (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'ef\'e4d bhavati parjanya\'f9}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
), which will hamper agricultural activities (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 parjany\'e4d anna-sambhava\'f9}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). By introducing brahminical culture, therefore, a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1
atriya}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  government should engage people in performing }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  studying the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vedas}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and giving charity. Thus the people will receive their necessities for life very easily, and there will be no disturbances in society. In this regard, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (3.12):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 i\'f1\'f6\'e4n bhog\'e4n hi vo dev\'e4\line d\'e4syante yaj\'efa-bh\'e4vit\'e4\'f9\line 
tair datt\'e4n aprad\'e4yaibhyo\line yo bhu\'eckte stena eva sa\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "In charge of the various necessities of life, the demigods, being satisfied b
y the performance of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  [sacrifice], supply all necessities to man. But he who enjoys these gifts, without offering them to the demigods in return, is certainly a thief."
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
The demigods are authorized supplying agents who act on behalf of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'ebu. Therefore, they must be satisfied by the performance of prescribed }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efas.}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Vedas,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  there are different kinds of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efas}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 prescribed for different kinds of demigods, but all are ultimately offered to the Supreme Personality of
 Godhead. For one who cannot understand what the Personality of Godhead is, sacrifice to the demigods is recommended. According to the different material qualities of the persons concerned, different types of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efas}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  are recommended in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Vedas.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Worship of different demigods is also on the same basis\emdash 
namely, according to different qualities. For example, the meat-eaters are recommended to worship the goddess K\'e4l\'e9, the ghastly form of material nature, and before the goddess the sacrifice of animals is recomm
ended. But for those in the mode of goodness, the transcendental worship of Vi\'f1\'ebu is recommended. Ultimately, all }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efas}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 are meant for gradual promotion to the transcendental position. For ordinary men, at least five }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efas,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 pa\'efca-mah\'e4yaj\'efa,}{\insrsid30033  are n
ecessary.
\par One should know, however, that all the necessities of life that human society requires are supplied by the demigod agents of the Lord. No one can manufacture anything. Consider, for example, all the eatables of human society. These eatables inclu
de grains, fruits, vegetables, milk and sugar for persons in the mode of goodness, and also eatables for the nonvegetarians, such as meats, none of which can be manufactured by men. Then again, take for example, heat, light, water and air, which are also 
necessities of life\emdash 
none of them can be manufactured by human society. Without the Supreme Lord, there can be no profuse sunlight, moonlight, rainfall or breeze, without which no one can live. Obviously, our life is dependent on supplies from the Lord. Even
 for our manufacturing enterprises, we require so many raw materials like metal, sulphur, mercury, manganese and so many essentials\emdash 
all of which are supplied by the agents of the Lord, with the purpose that we should make proper use of them to keep ourselv
es fit and healthy for the purpose of self-realization, leading to the ultimate goal of life, namely, liberation from the material struggle for existence. This aim of life is attained by performance of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efas.}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  If we forget the purpose of human life and sim
ply take supplies from the agents of the Lord for sense gratification and become more and more entangled in material existence, which is not the purpose of creation, certainly we become thieves, and therefore we are punished by the laws of material nature
. A society of thieves can never be happy, for they have no aim in life. The gross materialist thieves have no ultimate goal of life. They are simply directed to sense gratification; nor do they have knowledge of how to perform }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 
yaj\'efas.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Lord Caitanya, however, inaugurated the easiest performance of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  namely the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa,}{\insrsid30033 
 which can be performed by anyone in the world who accepts the principles of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu planned to kill the inhabitants of earth so that }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  would stop and the demigods, being disturbed, would die automatically when Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efe\'e7vara,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  was killed. These were the demoniac plans of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, who was expert in such activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.2.11
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 11
