\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vi\'f1\'ebu\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu, the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dvija}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas;}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kriy\'e4-m\'fcla\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash whose root is the performance of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
yaj\'efa}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  and the ritualistic ceremonies mentioned in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 Vedas;}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash personified }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  (Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who is known as the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa-puru\'f1a}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 ); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dharma-maya\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash full of religious principles; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pum\'e4n}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the Supreme Person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 deva-\'e5\'f1i}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the demigods and great }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e5\'f1is}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  like Vy\'e4sadeva and N\'e4rada; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pit\'e5}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the forefathers; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash and of all other living entities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dharmasya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the religious principles; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ca}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash also; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 par\'e4ya\'ebam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the shelter.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 The basic principle of brahminical culture is to satisfy Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, the personification of sacrificial and ritualistic ceremonies. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is the personified reservoir of all religious principles, and He is the shelter of all the demigods, the great pit\'e4s, and the people in general. When the br\'e4hma\'eb
as are killed, no one will exist to encourage the k\'f1atriyas to perform yaj\'efas, and thus the demigods, not being appeased by yaj\'efa, will automatically die.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 Since Vi\'f1\'ebu is the central point of brahminical culture, Hira
\'ebyaka\'e7ipu's plan was to kill Vi\'f1\'ebu, for if Vi\'f1\'ebu were killed, naturally the brahminical culture would also be lost. With brahminical culture lost, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  would no longer be performed, and for want of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the regular distribution of rainfall would cease (}{
