}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash with no material tinge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sarva-ga\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash qualified to go anywhere in the material or spiritual worlds; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sarva-vit}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash full of knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 para\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash transcendental to material conditions; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dhatte}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash accepts; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 asau}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4,}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  or living being; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4tmana\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the self; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 li\'ecgam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 
\emdash a body; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e4yay\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by the material energy; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vis\'e5jan}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash creating; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gu\'eb\'e4n}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash various material qualities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 The spirit soul, the l
iving entity, has no death, for he is eternal and inexhaustible. Being free from material contamination, he can go anywhere in the material or spiritual worlds. He is fully aware and completely different from the material body, but because of being misled
 
by misuse of his slight independence, he is obliged to accept subtle and gross bodies created by the material energy and thus be subjected to so-called material happiness and distress. Therefore, no one should lament for the passing of the spirit soul fro
m the body.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu very intelligently described the position of the soul. The soul is never the body, but is always completely different from the body. Being eternal and inexhaustible, the soul has no death, but when the same pure soul desire
s to enjoy the material world independently, he is placed under the conditions of material nature and must therefore accept a certain type of body and suffer the pains and pleasures thereof. This is also described by K\'e5\'f1\'eba in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (13.22). }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 K\'e4ra\'eba\'e0 gu\'eba-sa\'ecgo 'sya sad-asad-yoni janmasu:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 the living entity is born in different families or species of life because of being infected by the modes of material nature. When conditioned by material nature, the living entity must accept a certain type of body,
 which is offered by nature under the direction of the Supreme Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati\line 
bhr\'e4mayan sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni\line yantr\'e4r\'fc\'f2h\'e4ni m\'e4yay\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "The Supreme Lord is situated in everyone's heart, O Arjuna, and is directing the wanderings o
f all living entities, who are seated as on a machine, made of the material energy." (Bg. 18.61) The body is just like a machine, and according to the living entity's }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 he is offered a particular type of machine to move here and there under the control of material nature. This continues until he surrenders to the Supreme Personality of Godhead (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4m eva ye prapadyante m\'e4y\'e4m et
\'e4\'e0 taranti te}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Until he surrenders, the conditioned soul is carried from life to life by the arrangement of material nature.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.2.23
