e daytime it is customary for his funeral ceremony to be performed before the sun sets, regardless of whether he is burned or buried, and if he dies at night the funeral must be completed before the next sunrise. Apparently the queens continued lamenting 
f
or the dead body, the lump of matter, and would not allow it to be taken away for burning. This illustrates the strong grip of illusion among foolish persons who consider the body the self. Women are generally considered less intelligent. Because of ignor
ance only, the queens thought of the dead body as their husband and somehow or other thought that if the body were kept their husband would remain with them. Such a conception of the self is certainly for }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 go-khara}{
\cs2996\fs28\cf9\insrsid10813782\charrsid11368625 \emdash }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 cows and asses. We have actually seen that 
sometimes when a cow's calf has died the milkman cheats the cow by presenting before her the dead body of her calf. Thus the cow, who would not otherwise allow milking, licks the dead body of the calf and allows herself to be milked. This substantiates th
e description of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stra}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 that a foolish man in the bodily concept of life is like a cow. Not only do foolish men and women consider the body the self, but we have even seen that the dead body of a so-called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  was kept for days by his disciples, who thought that their }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  was in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sam\'e4dhi.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  When decomposition began and a bad smell unfortunately began to overwhelm the yogic power, the disciples allowed the dead body of the so-called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  to be burned. Thus the bodily concept of life is extremely strong amo
ng foolish persons, who are compared to cows and asses. Nowadays, great scientists are trying to freeze dead bodies so that in the future these frozen bodies may again be brought to life. The incident narrated by Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu from history must have taken place millions of years ago because Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu lived millions of years ago and was even then quoting from history. Thus the incident occurred before Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu's lifetime, but the same ignorance in the bodily concept of life is still prevalent, not only among laymen but even among scientists who think they will be able to revive frozen corpses.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
