all-pervading; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sajjate}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash mix; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tath\'e4}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash similarly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pum\'e4n}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the living entity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sarva-gu\'eba-\'e4\'e7raya\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash although now the shelter of the modes of material nature; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 para\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash transcendental to material contamination.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
As fire, although situated in wood, is perceived to be different from the wood, as air, although situated within the mouth and nostrils, is perceived to be separate, and as the sky, although all-pervading, never mixes with 
anything, so the living entity, although now encaged within the material body, of which it is the source, is separate from it.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the Supreme Personality of Godhead has explained that the material energy and spiritual energy both emanate from Him. The material energy is described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 me bhinn\'e4 prak
\'e5tir a\'f1\'f6adh\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the eight separated energies of the Lord. But although the eight gross and subtle material energies\emdash namely, earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intelligence and false ego
\emdash are stated to be }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhinn\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 separate from the Lord, actually they are not. As fire appears separate from wood and as the air flowing through the nostrils and mouth of the body appear separate from the body, so the Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, app
ears separate from the living being but is actually separate and not separate simultaneously. This is the philosophy of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acintya-bhed\'e4bheda-tattva}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  propounded by \'c7r\'e9
 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu. According to the reactions of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the living being appears separate 
from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but actually he is very intimately related with the Lord. Consequently, even though we now seem neglected by the Lord, He is actually always alert to our activities. Under all circumstances, therefore, we should si
mply depend on the supremacy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and thus revive our intimate relationship with Him. We must depend upon the authority and control of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.2.44
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 44
