\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
As long as the spirit soul is covered by the subtle body, consisting of the mind, intelligence and false ego, he is bound to the results of his fruitive activ
ities. Because of this covering, the spirit soul is connected with the material energy and must accordingly suffer material conditions and reversals, continually, life after life.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 The living entity is bound by the subtle body, consisting of the min
d, intelligence and false ego. At the time of death, therefore, the position of the mind becomes the cause for the next body. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (8.6), }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ya\'e0 ya\'e0 v\'e4pi smaran bh\'e4va\'e0 tyajaty ante kalevaram:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  at the time of death the mind sets the cri
teria for the spirit soul's being carried to another type of body. If a living being resists the dictation of the mind and engages the mind in the loving service of the Lord, the mind cannot degrade him. The duty of all human beings, therefore, is to keep
 the mind always engaged at the lotus feet of the Lord (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa vai mana\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pad\'e4ravindayo\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). When the mind is engaged at the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the intelligence is purified, and then the intelligence gets inspiration from the Supersoul (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dad\'e4mi buddhi-yoga\'e0 tam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
). Thus the living entity makes progress toward liberation from material bondage. The individual living soul is subject to the laws of fruitive activity, but the Supersoul, Param\'e4tm\'e4
, is not affected by the fruitive activities of the individual soul. As confirmed in the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Upani\'f1ad,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the Param\'e4tm\'e4 and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j
\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  who are likened to two birds, are sitting in the body. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 is enjoying or suffering by eating the fruits of the bodily activities, but the Param\'e4tm\'e4, who is free from such bondage, witnesses and sanctions the activities of the individual soul as the individual soul desires.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.2.48
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 48
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid30033 \b\v\f75\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 ivTaQaai>aiNaveXaae_Ya& Yad( Gau<aeZvQaRd*Gvc" )\line 
YaQaa MaNaaerQa" SvPan" SavRMaEiNd]Yak&- Ma*za )) 48 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 vitath\'e4bhinive\'e7o 'ya\'e0
\par yad gu\'ebe\'f1v artha-d\'e5g-vaca\'f9
\par yath\'e4 manoratha\'f9 svapna\'f9
\par sarvam aindriyaka\'e0 m\'e5\'f1\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vitatha}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash fruitless; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 abhinive\'e7a\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the conception; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ayam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash this; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yat}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash which; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gu\'ebe\'f1u}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash in the modes of material nature; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 artha}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash as a fact; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 d\'e5k-vaca\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the seeing and talking of; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yath\'e4}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash just as; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 manoratha\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash a mental concoction (daydream); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 svapna\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash a dream; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sarvam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash everything; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 aindriyakam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
produced by the senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e5\'f1\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash false.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
It is fruitless to see and talk of the material modes of nature and their resultant so-called happiness and distress as if 
they were factual. When the mind wanders during the day and a man begins to think himself extremely important, or when he dreams at night and sees a beautiful woman enjoying with him, these are merely false dreams. Similarly, the happiness and distress ca
used by the material senses should be understood to be meaningless.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
The happiness and distress derived from the activities of the material senses are not actual happiness and distress. Therefore }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 speaks of happiness that is transcendental to the material conception of life (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sukham \'e4tyantika\'e0 yat tad buddhi-gr\'e4hyam at\'e9ndriyam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
). When our senses are purified of material contamination, they become }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 at\'e9ndriya,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  transcendental senses, and when the transcendental senses are engaged in the service
 of the master of the senses, H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7
a, one can derive real transcendental pleasure. Whatever distress or happiness we manufacture by mental concoction through the subtle mind has no reality, but is simply a mental concoction. One should therefore not imag
ine so-called happiness through mental concoction. Rather, the best course is to engage the mind in the service of the Lord, H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a, and thus feel real blissful life.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 There is a Vedic statement }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ap\'e4
ma-somam am\'e5t\'e4 abh\'fcma apsarobhir vihar\'e4ma.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  With reference to such a conception, one wants to go to the heavenly planets to enjoy with the young girls there and drink }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 soma-rasa.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Such imaginary pleasure, however, has no value. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (7.23), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 antavat tu phala\'e0 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 tad bhavaty alpa-medhas\'e4m:}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 "Men of small intelligence worship the demigods, and their fruits are limited and temporary." Even if by fruitive activity or worship of the demigods one is elevated to the higher planetary systems for sense enjoyment, his situation is condemned in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 antavat,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 perishable. The happiness one enjoys in this way is like the pleasure of embracing a young woman in a dream; for some time it may be pleasing, but actually the basic principle is false. The mental concoctions of happiness and distress i
n this material world are compared to dreams because of their falseness. All thoughts of obtaining happiness by using the material senses have a false background and therefore have no meaning.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.2.49
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 49
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
