In this material world, the conception of self-preservation is the first law of nature. According to this conception, one should be interested in his personal safety and should then consider society, friendship, love, nationality, communit
y and so on, which have all developed because of the bodily conception of life and a lack of knowledge of the spirit soul. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 aj\'ef\'e4na.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 As long as human society is in darkness and ignorance, men will continue to make huge arrangements in the bodily conception of life. This is described by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bharam.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  In the materialistic conception, modern civilization makes enormous arrangements for huge roads, houses, mills and factories, and this is man's conception of the advancement of civili
zation. People do not know, however, that at any time they themselves may be kicked out of the scene and forced to accept bodies that have nothing to do with these enormous houses, palaces, roads and automobiles. Therefore when Arjuna was thinking in term
s of his bodily relationships with his kinsmen, K\'e5\'f1\'eba immediately chastised him, saying, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kutas tv\'e4 ka\'e7malam ida\'e0 vi\'f1ame samupasthitam an\'e4rya ju\'f1\'f6am:}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  "This bodily conception of life is befitting the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 an\'e4ryas,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the non-\'c4ryans, who are not advanced in knowledge." An \'c4
ryan civilization is a civilization advanced in spiritual knowledge. Not merely by stamping oneself an \'c4ryan does one become an \'c4ryan. To keep oneself in the deepest darkness concerning spiritual knowledge and at the same time claim to be an \'c4
ryan is a non-\'c4ryan position. In this connection, \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya quotes as follows from the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Brahma-vaivarta Pur\'e4\'eba:
\par }\pard\plain \s865\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ka \'e4tm\'e4 ka\'f9 para iti deh\'e4dy-apek\'f1ay\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 na hi deh\'e4dir \'e4tm\'e4 sy\'e4n\line na ca \'e7atrur ud\'e9rita\'f9\line ato daihika-v
\'e5ddhau v\'e4\line k\'f1aye v\'e4 ki\'e0 prayojanam
\par yas tu deha-gato j\'e9va\'f9\line sa hi n\'e4\'e7a\'e0 na gacchati\line tata\'f9 \'e7atru-viv\'e5ddhau ca\line sva-n\'e4\'e7e \'e7ocana\'e0 kuta\'f9
\par deh\'e4di-vyatiriktau tu\line j\'e9ve\'e7au pratij\'e4nat\'e4\line ata \'e4tma-viv\'e5ddhis tu\line v\'e4sudeve rati\'f9 sthir\'e4\line \'e7atru-n\'e4\'e7as tath\'e4j\'ef\'e4na-\line n\'e4\'e7o n\'e4nya\'f9 katha\'efcana
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The purport is that as long as we are in t
his human form of body, our duty is to understand the soul within the body. The body is not the self; we are different from the body, and therefore there is no question of friends, enemies or responsibilities in terms of the bodily conception of life. One
 
should not be very anxious about the body's changing from childhood to boyhood, from boyhood to old age and then to apparent annihilation. Rather, one should be very seriously concerned about the soul within the body and how to release the soul from the m
a
terial clutches. The living entity within the body is never annihilated; therefore one should surely know that whether one has many friends or many enemies, his friends cannot help him, and his enemies cannot do him any harm. One should know that he is a 
spirit soul (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 aha\'e0 brahm\'e4smi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
) and that the constitutional position of the soul is unaffected by the changes of the body. In all circumstances, everyone, as a spirit soul, must be a devotee of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and should not be concerned with bodily relationships, 
whether with friends or with enemies. One should know that neither we ourselves nor our enemies in the bodily conception of life are ever killed.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.2.61
