{\cs3000\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid16347101  The demoniac king Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu wanted to be unconquerable and free from old age and dwindling of the body. He wanted to gain all the yogic perfections like a\'ebim\'e4 and laghim\'e4
, to be deathless, and to be the only king of the entire universe, including Brahmaloka.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 Such are the goals of the austerities performed by demons. Hira\'eb
yaka\'e7ipu wanted to receive a benediction from Lord Brahm\'e4 so that in the future he would be able to conquer Lord Brahm\'e4's abode. Similarly, another demon received a benediction from Lord \'c7iva but later wanted to kill Lord \'c7
iva through that same benediction. Thus self-interested persons, by demoniac austerity, want to kill even their benedictors, whereas the Vai\'f1\'ebava wants to remain an ever-existing servant of the Lord and never to occupy the post of the Lord. Through 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4yujya-mukti,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  which is generally demanded by }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asuras,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
