In the material world, a servant is provided for by the master but is always planning how to 
capture the master's post. There have been many instances of this in history. Especially in India during the Mohammedan rule, many servants, by plans and devices, took over the posts of their masters. It is learned from Caitanya literature that one big Za
mindar, Subuddhi R\'e4
ya, kept a Mohammedan boy as a servant. Of course, he treated the boy as his own child, and sometimes, when the boy would steal something, the master would chastise him by striking him with a cane. There was a mark on the boy's back from 
this chastisement. Later, after that boy had by crooked means become Hussain Shah, Nawab of Bengal, one day his wife saw the mark on his back and inquired about it. The Nawab replied that in his childhood he had been a servant of Subuddhi R\'e4
ya, who had punished him because of some mischievous activities. Upon hearing this, the Nawab's wife immediately became agitated and requested her husband to kill Subuddhi R\'e4ya. Nawab Hussain Shah, of course, was very grateful to Subuddhi R\'e4
ya and therefore refused to kill him, but when his wife requested him to turn Subuddhi R\'e4ya into a Mohammedan, the Nawab agreed. Taking some water from his waterpot, he sprinkled it upon Subuddhi R\'e4ya and declared that Subuddhi R\'e4
ya had now become a Mohammedan. The point is that this Nawab had been an ordinary menial servant of Subuddhi R\'e4
ya but was somehow or other able to occupy the supreme post of Nawab of Bengal. This is the material world. Everyone is trying to become master through various devices, although everyone is servant of 
his senses. Following this system, a living entity, although servant of his senses, tries to become master of the whole universe. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was a typical example of this, and Brahm\'e4 was informed by the demigods of his intentions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.3.13
