he help of skin, marrow, bone, blood and so on, because it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asa\'ecgo'ya\'e0 puru\'f1a\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 \emdash 
the living entity has nothing to do with the material covering. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu performed a severe type of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tapasya,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 austerity, for many long years. Indeed, it is said that he performed the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tapasya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 for one hundred heavenly years. Since one day of the demigods equals six of our months, certainly this was a very long time. By nature's own way, his body had been almost consumed by earthworms, ants and other parasites, and therefore even Brahm\'e4
 was at first unable to see him. Later, however, Brahm\'e4 could ascertain where Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was, and Brahm\'e4 was struck with wonder to see Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu's extraordinary power to execute }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tapasya.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  Anyone would conclude that Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was dead because his body was covered in so many ways, but Lord Brahm\'e4, the supreme living being in this universe, could understand that Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu was alive but covered by material elements.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 It is also to be noted that although Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu performed this austerity for a long, long time, he was nonetheless known as a Daitya and R\'e4k\'f1asa. It will be seen from verses to follow that even great saintly persons could not perform such a severe type of austerity. Why then was he called a R
\'e4k\'f1asa and Daitya? It is because whatever he did was for his own sense gratification. His son Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was only five years old, and so what could Prahl\'e4
da do? Yet simply by performing a little devotional service according to the instructions of N\'e4rada Muni, Prahl\'e4da became so dear to the Lord that the Lord came to save him, whereas Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu, in spite of all his austerities, was killed. This is the difference between devotional service and all other methods of perfection. One who performs severe austerities for sense gr
atification is fearful to the entire world, whereas a devotee who performs even a slight amount of devotional service is a friend to everyone (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 suh\'e5da\'e0 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). Since the Lord is the well-wisher of every living entity and since a devotee assumes the
 qualities of the Lord, a devotee also acts for everyone's good fortune by performing devotional service. Thus although Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu performed such a severe austerity, he remained a Daitya and a R\'e4k\'f1asa, whereas Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, although born of the same Daitya father, became the most exalted devotee and was personally protected by the Supreme Lord. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhakti}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is therefore called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarvop\'e4dhi-vinirmuktam,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  indicating that a devotee is freed from all material designations, and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnyam,}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  situated in a transcendental position, free from all material desires.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.3.17
