Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (9.23-24):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ye 'py anya-devat\'e4-bhakt\'e4\line yajante \'e7raddhay\'e4nvit\'e4\'f9\line te 'pi m\'e4
m eva kaunteya\line yajanty avidhi-p\'fcrvakam
\par aha\'e0 hi sarva-yaj\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line bhokt\'e4 ca prabhur eva ca\line na tu m\'e4m abhij\'e4nanti\line tattven\'e4ta\'e7 cyavanti te
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Whatever a man may sacrifice to other gods, O son of Kunt\'e9
, is really meant for Me alone, but it is offered without true understanding. I am the only enjoyer and the only object of sacrifice. Those who do not recognize My true transcendental nature fall down."
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 In effect, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a says, "Persons engaged in the worship of demigods are not very intelligent, although such worship is indirectly offered to Me." For example, when a man pours water on the leaves and branch
es of a tree without pouring water on the root, he does so without sufficient knowledge or without observing regulative principles. The process of watering a tree is to pour water on the root. Similarly, the process of rendering service to different parts
 
of the body is to supply food to the stomach. The demigods are, so to speak, different officers and directors in the government of the Supreme Lord. One has to follow the laws made by the government, not by the officers or directors. Similarly, everyone i
s
 to offer his worship to the Supreme Lord only. That will automatically satisfy the different officers and directors of the Lord. The officers and directors are engaged as representatives of the government, and to offer some bribe to the officers and dire
ctors is illegal. This is stated in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 avidhi-p\'fcrvakam.}{\insrsid30033  In other words, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a does not approve the unnecessary worship of the demigods.
\par In }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  it is clearly stated that there are many types of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  performances recommended in the Ve
dic literatures, but actually all of them are meant for satisfying the Supreme Lord. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Yaj\'efa}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means Vi\'f1\'ebu. In the Third Chapter of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  it is clearly stated that one should work only for satisfying Yaj\'efa, or Vi\'f1\'ebu. The perfectional form of human civilization, known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{\insrsid30033 
 is specifically meant for satisfying Vi\'f1\'ebu. Therefore, K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, "I am the enjoyer of all sacrifices because I am the supreme master." However, less intelligent persons, without knowing this fact, worship demigods fo
r temporary benefit. Therefore they fall down to material existence and do not achieve the desired goal of life. If, however, anyone has any material desire to be fulfilled, he had better pray for it to the Supreme Lord (although that is not pure devotion
), and he will thus achieve the desired result.
\par Although Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu offered his obeisances unto Lord Brahm\'e4, he was strongly inimical toward Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. This is the symptom of an }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asura.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Asuras}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  worship the demigods as being separate from the Lord, not kno
wing that all the demigods are powerful because of being servants of the Lord. If the Supreme Lord were to withdraw the powers of the demigods, the demigods would no longer be able to offer benedictions to their worshipers. The difference between a devote
e and a nondevotee, or }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asura,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is that a devotee knows that Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is the Supreme Personality of Godhead and that everyone derives power from Him. Without worshiping the demigods for particular powers, a devotee worships Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, knowing that if he de
sires a particular power he can get that power while acting as Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's devotee. Therefore in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stra}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\i\insrsid5139582\charrsid5139582 (Bh\'e4g.}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  2.3.10) it is recommended:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ak\'e4ma\'f9 sarva-k\'e4mo v\'e4\line mok\'f1a-k\'e4ma ud\'e4ra-dh\'e9\'f9\line t\'e9vre
\'eba bhakti-yogena\line yajeta puru\'f1a\'e0 param
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "A person who has broader i
ntelligence, whether he be full of material desires, free from material desires, or desiring liberation, must by all means worship the supreme whole, the Personality of Godhead." Even if a person has material desires, instead of worshiping the demigods he
 should pray to the Supreme Lord so that his connection with the Supreme Lord will be established and he will be saved from becoming a demon or a nondevotee. In this regard, \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya gives the following quotation from the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Brahma-tarka:
