\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  begins by declaring that the Absolute Person is the original source of all creation (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 janm\'e4dy asya yata\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
). One may ask whether Lord Brahm\'e4 is the Supreme Absolute Person. No, the Supreme Absolute Person is K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Brahm\'e4 receives his mind, intelligence, materials and everything else from K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, and then he becomes the secondary creator, the engineer of this universe. In this regard we may note that the creation does not take place accidentally, because o
f the explosion of a chunk. Such nonsensical theories are not accepted by Vedic students. The first created living being is Brahm\'e4, who is endowed with perfect knowledge and intelligence by the Lord. As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r
\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, tene brahma h\'e5d\'e4 ya \'e4di-kavaye:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 although Brahm\'e4
 is the first created being, he is not independent, for he receives help from the Supreme Personality of Godhead through his heart. There is no one but Brahm\'e4 at the time of creation, and therefore he receives his intelligence direct
ly from the Lord through the heart. This has been discussed in the beginning of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 Lord Brahm\'e4
 is described in this verse as the original cause of the cosmic manifestation, and this applies to his position in the material world. There are many, many such controllers, all of whom are created by the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'eb
u. This is illustrated by an incident described in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  When the Brahm\'e4 of this particular universe was invited by K\'e5\'f1\'eba to Dv\'e4rak\'e4
, he thought that he was the only Brahm\'e4. Therefore when K\'e5\'f1\'eba inquired from His servant which Brahm\'e4 was at the door to visit, Lord Brahm\'e4 was surprised. He replied that of course Lord Brahm\'e4, the father of the four Kum\'e4
ras, was waiting at the door. Later, Lord Brahm\'e4 asked K\'e5\'f1\'eba why He had inquired which Brahm\'e4 had come. He was then informed that there are millions of other Brahm\'e4s because there are millions of universes. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a then called all the Brahm\'e4s, who immediately came to visit Him. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 catur-mukha}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Brahm\'e4, the four-headed Brahm\'e4
 of this universe, thought himself a very insignificant creature in the presence of so many Brahm\'e4s with so many heads. Thus although there is a Brahm\'e4 who is the engineer of each universe, K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the original source of all of them.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.3.29
