\insrsid10039258 CHAPTER FOUR\line }{\insrsid30033 Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu Terrorizes the Universe
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.4 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 This chapter fully describes how Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu obtained power from Lord Brahm\'e4
 and misused it by harassing all the living entities within this universe.
\par By severe austerities, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu satisfied Lord Brahm\'e4
 and obtained the benedictions he desired. After he received these benedictions, his body, which had been almost entirely consumed, was revived with full beauty and a luster like gold. Nonetheless, he continued to be envious of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, unable to forget Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's having killed his brother. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu conquered everyone in the ten directions and the three worlds and brought all living entities, both demigods and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asuras,}{\insrsid30033 
 under his control. Becoming the master of all places, including the residence of Indra, whom he had driven out, he began enjoying life in great luxury and thus became mad. All the demigods but Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva came under his control and began serving him, but despite all his material power he was dissatisfied because he was always puffed up, proud of transgressing the Vedic regulations. All the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\insrsid30033 
 were dissatisfied with him, and they cursed him with determination. Eventually, all the living entities within the universe, represented by the demigods and sages, prayed to the Supreme Lord for relief from Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu's rule.
\par Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu informed the demigods that they and the other living entities would be saved from the fearful conditions created by Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu. Since Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was the oppressor of all the demigods, the followers of the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Vedas,}{\insrsid30033  the cows, the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\insrsid30033  and the religious, saintly persons, and since he was envious of the Supreme Lord, he would naturally be killed very soon. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu's last exploit would be to torment his own son Prahl\'e4da, who was a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 mah\'e4-bh\'e4gavata,}{\insrsid30033  an exalted Vai\'f1\'eb
ava. Then his life would end. When the demigods were thus reassured by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, everyone was satisfied, knowing that the miseries inflicted upon them by Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu would come to an end.
\par Finally, N\'e4rada Muni describes the characteristics of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the son of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, and describes how his father envied his own qualified son. In this way the chapter ends.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.4.1
