The steps of King Indra's residence were made of coral, the floor was bedecked with invaluable emeralds, the walls were of crystal, and the columns of vaid\'fcrya stone. The wonderful canopies were beautifully decorated, the
 seats were bedecked with rubies, and the silk bedding, as white as foam, was decorated with pearls. The ladies of the palace, who were blessed with beautiful teeth and the most wonderfully beautiful faces, walked here and there in the palace, their ankle
 bells tinkling melodiously, and saw their own beautiful reflections in the gems. The demigods, however, being very much oppressed, had to bow down and offer obeisances at the feet of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu, who chastised the demigods very severely and for no reason. Thus Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu lived in the palace and severely ruled everyone.
