a. Without the grace of the spiritual master, one cannot make any advancement."
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d-dharitvena samasta-\'e7\'e4strair\line uktas tath\'e4 bh\'e4
vyata eva sadbhi\'f9\line kintu prabhor ya\'f9 priya eva tasya\line vande guro\'f9 \'e7r\'e9-cara\'eb\'e4ravindam}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"The spiritual master is to be honored as much as the Supreme Lord because he is the most confidential servitor of the Lord. This is acknowledged in all revealed scriptures and followed by all authorities. Therefore I 
offer my respectful obeisances unto the lotus feet of such a spiritual master, who is a bona fide representative of \'c7r\'e9 Hari [K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a]." The spiritual master, the servant of God, is engaged in the most confidential service of the Lord, namely delivering all the conditioned souls from the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 in which one thinks, "This person is my enemy, and that one is my friend." Actually the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the friend of all living entities, and all living entities are eternal servants of th
e Supreme Lord. Oneness is possible through this understanding, not through artificially thinking that every one of us is God or equal to God. The true understanding is that God is the supreme master and that all of us are servants of the Supreme Lord and
 are therefore on the same platform. This had already been taught to Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja by his spiritual master, N\'e4rada, but Prahl\'e4da was nonetheless surprised by how a bewildered soul thinks one person his enemy and another his friend.

\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 As long as one adhere
s to the philosophy of duality, thinking one person a friend and another an enemy, he should be understood to be in the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9
 philosopher who thinks that all living entities are God and are therefore one is also mistaken. No one is equal to God. The servant cannot be equal to the master. According to the Vai\'f1\'eb
ava philosophy, the master is one, and the servants are also one, but the distinction between the master and servant must continue even in the liberated stage. In the condition
ed stage we think that some living beings are our friends whereas others are enemies, and thus we are in duality. In the liberated stage, however, the conception is that God is the master and that all living entities, being servants of God, are one.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.5.12
