ja's teachers and demoniac father asked him how his intelligence had been polluted, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja said, "As far as I am concerned, my intelligence has not been polluted. Rather, by the grace of my spiritual master and by the grace of my Lord, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, I have now learned that no one is my enemy and no one is my friend. We ar
e all actually eternal servants of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, but under the influence of the external energy we think that we are separately situated from the Supreme Personality of Godhead as friends and enemies of one another. This mistaken idea has now been corrected, and 
therefore, unlike ordinary human beings, I no longer think that I am God and that others are my friends and enemies. Now I am rightly thinking that everyone is an eternal servant of God and that our duty is to serve the supreme master, for then we shall s
tand on the platform of oneness as servants."
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 Demons think of everyone as a friend or enemy, but Vai
\'f1\'ebavas say that since everyone is a servant of the Lord, everyone is on the same platform. Therefore a Vai\'f1\'ebava treats other living entities neither as friends nor as enemies, but instead tries to spread K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, teaching everyone that we are all one as servants of the Supreme Lord but are uselessly wasting our valuable lives by creating nations, communities and other groups of friends and enemies. Everyone should come to the platform of K\'e5\'f1
\'eba consciousness and thus feel oneness as a servant of the Lord. Although there are 8,400,000 species of life, a Vai\'f1\'ebava feels this oneness. The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c9\'e7opani\'f1ad}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  advises, }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ekatvam anupa\'e7yata\'f9.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  A devotee should see the 
Supreme Personality of Godhead to be situated in everyone's heart and should also see every living entity as an eternal servant of the Lord. This vision is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ekatvam,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 oneness. Although there is a relationship of master and servant, both master and servant are one because of their spiritual identity. This is also }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ekatvam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Thus the conception of }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ekatvam}{\insrsid30033  for the Vai\'f1\'ebava is different from that of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9.
\par Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu asked Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja how he had become antagonistic to his family. When a family member is killed by an enemy, all the members of the family would naturally be inimical to the murderer, but Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu saw that Prahl\'e4da had become friendly with the murderer. Therefore he asked, "Who has created this kind of intelligence in you? Hav
e you developed this consciousness by yourself? Since you are a small boy, someone must have induced you to think this way." Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja wanted to reply that an attitude favorable toward Vi\'f1\'eb
u can develop only when the Lord is favorable (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sa yad\'e4nuvrata\'f9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). As stated in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the friend of everyone (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 suh\'e5da\'e0 sama-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0 j\'ef\'e4tv\'e4 m\'e4\'e0 \'e7\'e4ntim \'e5cchati}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
). The Lord is never an enemy to any of the millions of living entities, but is always a friend to everyone. This is true understanding. If one thinks that the Lord is an enemy, his intelligence is }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 pa\'e7u-buddhi,}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  the intelligence of an animal. He falsely thinks, "I am different from my enemy, and my enemy is different from me. The enemy has done this, and therefore my duty is to kill him." This mi
sconception is described in this verse as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bheda-gat\'e4sat\'e9.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The actual fact is that everyone is a servant of the Lord, as confirmed in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 j\'e9vera 'svar\'fcpa' haya-k\'e5\'f1\'ebera 'nitya-d\'e4sa}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 '}{\insrsid30033 ). As servants of the Lord, we ar
e one, and there can be no questions of enmity or friendship. If one actually understands that every one of us is a servant of the Lord, where is the question of enemy or friend?
\par Everyone should be friendly for the service of the Lord. Everyone should praise another's service to the Lord and not be proud of his own service. This is the way of Vai\'f1\'ebava thinking, Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha thinking. There may be rivalries and apparent competition between servants in performing service, but in the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha planets the service of another servant is appreciated, not condemned. This is Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha competition. There is no question of enmity between servants. Everyone should be allowed to render service to the Lord to the best of his ability, and everyone should appreciate the service of others. Such are the activities of Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha. Since everyone is a servant, everyone is on the same platform and is allowed to serve the Lord according to his ability. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (15.15), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 
sarvasya c\'e4ha\'e0 h\'e5di sannivi\'f1\'f6o matta\'f9 sm\'e5tir j\'ef\'e4nam apohana\'e0 ca:}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 the Lord is situated in everyone's heart, giving dictation according to the attitude of the servant. However, the Lord gives different dictation to the nondevotees and devotees. The nondevotees challenge the authority of the Supreme Lo
rd, and therefore the Lord dictates in such a way that the nondevotees forget the Lord's service, life after life, and are punished by the laws of nature. But when a devotee very sincerely wants to render service to the Lord, the Lord dictates in a differ
ent way. As the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (10.10):
