\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means "semen." The sons of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya were }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  by birthright, but an actual }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  is one who possesses the brahminical qualities. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  \'d1a
\'eb\'f2a and Amarka, being seminal sons of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, did not actually possess real brahminical qualifications, for they engaged as servants of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu. An actual }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  is very much satisfied to see anyone, not to speak of his disciple, become a devotee of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Such }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  are meant to satisfy the supreme master. A }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 is strictly prohibited from becoming a servant of anyone else, for that is the business of dogs and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdras.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  A dog must satisfy his master, but a }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  does not have to satisfy anyone; he is simply meant to satisfy K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4nuk\'fclyena k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4nu\'e7\'e9
lanam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). That is the real qualification of a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  Because \'d1a\'eb\'f2a and Amarka were seminal }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and had become servants of such a master as Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, they unnecessarily wanted to chastise Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
