\'e0 gr\'e4hay\'e4m \'e4sa}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  are important. The words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 gr\'e4hay\'e4m \'e4sa}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  literally mean that they tried to induce Prahl
\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja to accept the paths of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma, artha}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e4ma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 (religion, economic development and sense gratification). People are generally preoccupied with these three concerns, without interest in the path of liberation. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, the father of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, was simply interested in gold and sense enjoyment. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 hira\'ebya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means "gold," and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ka\'e7ipu}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  refers to soft cushions and bedding on which people enjoy sense gratification. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prahl\'e4da,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 however, refers to one who is always joyful in understanding Brahman (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Prahl\'e4da}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prasann\'e4tm\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  always joyful. Prahl\'e4
da was always joyful in worshiping the Lord, but in accordance with the instructions of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu, the teachers were interested in teaching him about material things. Materialistic persons think that the path of religion is meant for improving their material conditions. The materialist goes to a temple to worship many varieties of demigods just to
 receive some benediction to improve his material life. He goes to a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4dhu}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  or so-called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sv\'e4m\'e9}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  to take advantage of an easy method for achieving material opulence. In the name of religion, the so-called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4dhus}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 try to satisfy the senses of the materialists by
 showing them shortcuts to material opulence. Sometimes they give some talisman or blessing. Sometimes they attract materialistic persons by producing gold. Then they declare themselves God, and foolish materialists are attracted to them for economic deve
l
opment. As a result of this process of cheating, others are reluctant to accept a religious process, and instead they advise people in general to work for material advancement. This is going on all over the world. Not only now but since time immemorial, n
o one is interested in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mok\'f1a,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  liberation. There are four principles\emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 (religion), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 artha}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (economic development), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e4ma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (sense gratification) and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mok\'f1a}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (liberation). People accept religion to become materially opulent. And why should one be materially opulent? For sense gratification. Thus people prefer these three 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4rgas,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the three paths of materialistic life. No one is interested in liberation, and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhagavad-bhakti,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  devotional service to the Lord, is above even liberation. Therefore the process of devotional service, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, is extremely difficult to understand. This will be explained later by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. The teachers \'d1a\'eb\'f2a and Amarka tried to induce Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja to accept the materialistic way of life, but actually their attempt was a failure.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.5.19
