I consider; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 adh\'e9tam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash learning; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 uttamam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash topmost.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja said: Hearing and chanting about the transcendental holy name, form, qualities, paraphernalia and pastimes of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, remembering them, serving the lotus feet of the Lord, offering the Lord respectful worship with sixteen t
ypes of paraphernalia, offering prayers to the Lord, becoming His servant, considering the Lord one's best friend, and surrendering everything unto Him (in other words, serving Him with the body, mind and words)\emdash 
these nine processes are accepted as pure devotional service. One who has dedicated his life to the service of K\'e5\'f1\'eba through these nine methods should be understood to be the most learned person, for he has acquired complete knowledge.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 When Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was asked by his father to say so
mething from whatever he had learned, he considered that what he had learned from his spiritual master was the best of all teachings whereas what he had learned about diplomacy from his material teachers, \'d1a\'eb\'f2a and Amarka, was useless. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhakti\'f9 pare\'e7\'e4nubhavo viraktir anyatra ca}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  }{\cs3010\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5139582\charrsid5139582 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 11.2.42). This is the symptom of pure devotional service. A pure devotee is interested only in devotional service, not in material affairs. To execute devotional service, one should always engage in hearing and chanting about K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu. The process of temple worship is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 arcana.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  How to perform }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 arcana}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 will be explained herein. One should have complete faith in the words of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who says that He is the great well-wishing friend of everyone (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 suh\'e5da\'e0 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). A devotee considers K\'e5\'f1\'eba the only friend. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sakhyam.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Pu\'e0s\'e4
rpit\'e4 vi\'f1\'ebau.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pu\'e0s\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 means "by all living entities." There are no distinctions permitting only a man or only a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  to offer devotional service to the Lord. Everyone can
 do so. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (9.32), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 striyo vai\'e7y\'e4s tath\'e4 \'e7\'fcdr\'e4s te 'pi y\'e4nti par\'e4\'e0 gatim:}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  although women, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vai\'e7yas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdras}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  are considered less intelligent, they also can become devotees and return home, back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 After performing sacrifi
ces, sometimes a person engaged in fruitive activity customarily offers the results to Vi\'f1\'ebu. But here it is said, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhagavaty addh\'e4:}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  one must directly offer everything to Vi\'f1\'eb
u. This is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (not merely }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ny\'e4sa}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). A }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 trida\'eb\'f2i-sanny\'e4s\'e9}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  carries three }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 da\'eb\'f2as,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  signifying }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 kaya-mano-v\'e4kya}{\insrsid1313702\charrsid11471083 \emdash }{\insrsid30033 
body, mind and words. All of these should be offered to Vi\'f1\'ebu, and then one can begin devotional service. Fruitive workers first perform some pious activities and then formally or officially offer the results to Vi\'f1\'ebu. The
 real devotee, however, first offers his surrender to K\'e5\'f1\'eba with his body, mind and words and then uses his body, mind and words for the service of K\'e5\'f1\'eba as K\'e5\'f1\'eba desires.
\par \'c7r\'e9la Bhaktisiddh\'e4nta Sarasvat\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura gives the following explanation in his }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Tathya.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7rava\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 refers to giving aural reception to the holy name and descriptions of the Lord's form, qualities, entourage and pastimes as explained in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 and similar authorized scriptures. After aurally receiving such messages, one should memorize these vibrations and repeat them (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'e9rtanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Smara\'ebam}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means trying to understand more and more about the Supreme Lord, and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 means engaging oneself in serving the lotus feet of the Lord according to the time and circumstances. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Arcanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu as one does in the temple, and }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 vandanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means offering respectful obeisances. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Man-man\'e4 bhava mad-bhakto mad-y\'e4j\'e9 m\'e4\'e0 namaskuru.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 
Vandanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 namaskuru}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 \emdash offering obeisances or offering prayers. Thinking oneself to be }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 nitya-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-d\'e4sa,}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  everlastingly a servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 d\'e4syam,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sakhyam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means being a well-wisher of K
\'e5\'f1\'eba. K\'e5\'f1\'eba wants everyone to surrender unto Him because everyone is constitutionally His servant. Therefore, as a sincere friend of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, one should preach this philosophy, requesting everyone to surrender unto K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c4tma-nivedanam}{\insrsid30033  means offering K\'e5\'f1\'eba everything, including one's body, mind, intelligence and whatever one may possess.
\par One's sincere endeavor to perform these nine processes of devotional service is technically called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhakti.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 addh\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 means "directly" One should not be like the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 karm\'e9s,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  who perform pious activities and then formally offer the results to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. That is }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a.}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  One should not aspire for the results of his pious activities, but should dedicate oneself fully and then act piously. In other words, one should act for the satisfaction of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, not for the satisfaction of his own senses. That is the meaning of the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 addh\'e4,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  "directly."
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnya\'e0\line j\'ef\'e4na-karm\'e4dy-an\'e4v\'e5tam\line 
\'e4nuk\'fclyena k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4nu-\line \'e7\'e9lana\'e0 bhaktir uttam\'e4}{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "One should render transcendental loving service to the Supreme Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a favorably and without desire for material profit or gain through fruitive activities or philosophical speculation. That is called pure devotional service." One should simply satisfy K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, without being influenced by fruitive knowledge or fruitive activity.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Gop\'e4la-t\'e4pan\'e9 Upani
\'f1ad}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  says that the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhakti}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means engagement in the devotional service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, not of anyone else. This }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Upani\'f1ad}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  describes that }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhakti}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 is the offering of devotional service unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead. To perform devotional service, one should be relieved of the bodily conception of life and a
spirations to be happy through elevation to the higher planetary systems. In other words, work performed simply for the satisfaction of the Supreme Lord, without any desire for material benefits, is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhakti.}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhakti}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is also called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ni\'f1karma,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or freedom from the results of fruitive activity. }
{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhakti}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ni\'f1karma}{\insrsid30033  are on the same platform, although devotional service and fruitive activity appear almost the same.
\par The nine different processes enunciated by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who learned them from N\'e4rada Muni,
 may not all be required for the execution of devotional service; if a devotee performs only one of these nine without deviation, he can attain the mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Sometimes it is found that when one performs one of the proces
ses, other processes are mixed with it. That is not improper for a devotee. When a devotee executes any one of the nine processes (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 nava-lak\'f1a\'eb\'e4}{\insrsid30033 
), this is sufficient; the other eight processes are included. Now let us discuss these nine different processes.
\par (1) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7rava\'ebam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Hearing of the holy name of the Lord (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7rava\'ebam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) is the beginning of devotional service. Although any one of the nine processes is sufficient, in chronological order the hearing of the holy name of the Lord is the beginning. Indeed, it is essential. As enunciated by Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ceto-darpa\'eba-m\'e4rjanam:}{\cs1998\insrsid30033  }{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
by chanting the holy name of the Lord, one is cleansed of the material conception of life, which is due to the dirty modes of material nature. When the dirt is cleansed from the c
ore of one's heart, one can realize the form of the Supreme Personality of Godhead\emdash }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 parama\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 Thus by hearing the holy name of the Lord, one comes to the platform of understanding the personal form of the Lord. After re
alizing the Lord's form, one can realize the transcendental qualities of the Lord, and when one can understand His transcendental qualities one can understand the Lord's associates. In this way a devotee advances further and further toward complete unders
tanding of the Lord as he awakens in realization of the Lord's holy name, transcendental form and qualities, His paraphernalia, and everything pertaining to Him. Therefore the chronological process is }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana
\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9.}{\insrsid30033  This same process of chronolog
ical understanding holds true in chanting and remembering. When the chanting of the holy name, form, qualities and paraphernalia is heard from the mouth of a pure devotee, his hearing and chanting are very pleasing. \'c7r\'e9la San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 has forbidden us to hear the chanting of an artificial devotee or nondevotee.
\par Hearing from the text of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is considered the most important process of hearing. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 is full of transcendental chanting of the holy name, and therefore the chanting and hearing of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 are transcendentally full of mellows. The transcendental holy name of the Lord may be heard and chanted accordingly to the attraction of the devotee. One may chant the holy name of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or one may chant the holy name of Lord R\'e4ma or }{
\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 r\'e4m\'e4di-m\'fcrti\'f1u kal\'e4-niyamena ti\'f1\'f6han}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
). The Lord has innumerable forms and names, and devotees may meditate upon a particular form and chant the holy name according to his attraction. The best course is to hear of the holy name,
 form and so on from a pure devotee of the same standard as oneself. In other words, one who is attached to K\'e5\'f1\'eba should chant and hear from other pure devotees who are also attached to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. The same principle applies for devotees attracted by Lord R\'e4ma, Lord N\'e5si\'e0ha and other forms of the Lord. Because K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the ultimate form of the Lord (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'e5\'f1\'ebas tu bhagav\'e4n svayam}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ), it is best to hear about Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba's name, form and pastimes from a realized devotee who is particularly attracted by the form of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  great devotees like \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 have specifically described Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a's holy name, form and qualities. Unless one hears about the holy name, form and qualities of the Lord, one cannot clearly understand the other processes of devotional service. Therefore \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu recommends that one chant the holy name of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Para\'e0 vijayate \'e7r\'e9-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-sa\'eck\'e9rtanam.}{\insrsid30033 
 If one is fortunate enough to hear from the mouth of realized devotees, he is very easily successful on the path of devotional service. Therefore hearing of the holy name, form and qualities of the Lord is essential.
\par In }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (1.5.11) there is this verse:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tad-v\'e4g-visargo janat\'e4gha-viplavo\line yasmin prati-\'e7lokam abaddhavaty api\line n
\'e4m\'e4ny anantasya ya\'e7o-'\'eckit\'e4ni yat\line \'e7\'e5\'ebvanti g\'e4yanti g\'e5\'ebanti s\'e4dhava\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"Verses describing the name, form and qualities of Anantadeva, the unlimited Supreme Lord, are able to vanquish all the sinful reactions of the entire world. Therefore even if such verses are improperly compose
d, devotees hear them, describe them and accept them as bona fide and authorized." In this connection, \'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9
 has remarked that a pure devotee takes advantage of another pure devotee by trying to hear from him about the holy name, form and qualities of the Lord. If there is no such opportunity, he alone chants and hears the Lord's holy name.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 (2) }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 K\'e9rtanam.}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The hearing of the holy name has been described above. Now let us try to understand the chanting of the holy name, which is the second item in the
 consecutive order. It is recommended that such chanting be performed very loudly. In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  N\'e4
rada Muni says that without shame he began traveling all over the world, chanting the holy name of the Lord. Similarly, \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu has advised:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 t\'e5\'eb\'e4d api sun\'e9cena\line taror api sahi\'f1\'ebun\'e4\line am\'e4nin\'e4 m\'e4
nadena\line k\'e9rtan\'e9ya\'f9 sad\'e4 hari\'f9}{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
A devotee can very peacefully chant the holy name of the Lord by behaving more humbly than the grass, being tolerant like a tree and offering respects to everyone, witho
ut expecting honor from anyone else. Such qualifications make it easier to chant the holy name of the Lord. The process of transcendental chanting can be easily performed by anyone. Even if one is physically unfit, classified lower than others, devoid of 
m
aterial qualifications or not at all elevated in terms of pious activities, the chanting of the holy name is beneficial. An aristocratic birth, an advanced education, beautiful bodily features, wealth and similar results of pious activities are all unnece
s
sary for advancement in spiritual life, for one can very easily advance simply by chanting the holy name. It is understood from the authoritative source of Vedic literature that especially in this age, Kali-yuga, people are generally short-living, extreme
l
y bad in their habits, and inclined to accept methods of devotional service that are not bona fide. Moreover, they are always disturbed by material conditions, and they are mostly unfortunate. Under the circumstances, the performance of other processes, s
uch as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa, d\'e4na, tapa\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kriy\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash sacrifices, charity and so on\emdash 
are not at all possible. Therefore it is recommended:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 harer n\'e4ma harer n\'e4ma\line harer n\'e4maiva kevalam\line kalau n\'e4sty eva n\'e4
sty eva\line n\'e4sty eva gatir anyath\'e4}{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "In this age of quarrel and hypocrisy the 
only means of deliverance is chanting of the holy name of the Lord. There is no other way. There is no other way. There is no other way." Simply by chanting the holy name of the Lord, one advances perfectly in spiritual life. This is the best process for 
success in life. In other ages, the chanting of the holy name is equally powerful, but especially in this age, Kali-yuga, it is most powerful. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 K\'e9rtan\'e4d eva k\'e5\'f1\'ebasya mukta-sa\'ecga\'f9 para\'e0 vrajet: }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 simply by chanting the holy name of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, one is liberated and r
eturns home, back to Godhead. Therefore, even if one is able to perform other processes of devotional service, one must adopt the chanting of the holy name as the principal method of advancing in spiritual life. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yaj\'efai
\'f9 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-pr\'e4yair yajanti hi sumedhasa\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 those who are very sharp in their intelligence should adopt this process of chanting the holy names of the Lord. One should not, however, manufacture different types of chanting. One should adhere seriously to the chanting of the holy name as recomme
nded in the scriptures: Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
While chanting the holy name of the Lord, one should be careful to avoid ten offenses. From Sanat-kum\'e4ra it is understood that even if a per
son is a severe offender in many ways, he is freed from offensive life if he takes shelter of the Lord's holy name. Indeed, even if a human being is no better than a two-legged animal, he will be liberated if he takes shelter of the holy name of the Lord.
 One should therefore be very careful not to commit offenses at the lotus feet of the Lord's holy name. The offenses are described as follows: (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to blaspheme a devotee, especially a devotee engaged in broadcasting the glories of the holy name, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 b}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to consider the name of Lord \'c7
iva or any other demigod to be equally as powerful as the holy name of the Supreme Personality of Godhead (no one is equal to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, nor is anyone superior to Him), (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 c}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to disobey the instructions of the spiritual master, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 d}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to blaspheme the Vedic literatures and literatures compiled in pursuance of the Vedic literatures, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 e}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to comment that the glories of the holy name of the Lord are exaggerated, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 f}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to interpret the holy name in a deviant way, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to commit sinful activities on the strength of chanting the holy name, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 h}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to compare the chanting of the holy name to pious activities, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 i}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to instruct the glories of the holy name to a person who has no understanding of the chanting of the holy name, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 j}{\insrsid30033 ) not
 to awaken in transcendental attachment for the chanting of the holy name, even after hearing all these scriptural injunctions.
\par There is no way to atone for any of these offenses. It is therefore recommended that an offender at the feet of the holy name co
ntinue to chant the holy name twenty-four hours a day. Constant chanting of the holy name will make one free of offenses, and then he will gradually be elevated to the transcendental platform on which he can chant the pure holy name and thus become a love
r of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par It is recommended that even if one commits offenses, one should continue chanting the holy name. In other words, the chanting of the holy name makes one offenseless. In the book }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 N\'e4ma-kaumud\'e9}{\insrsid30033 
 it is recommended that if one is an offender at the lotus feet of a Vai\'f1\'ebava, he should submit to that Vai\'f1\'eb
ava and be excused; similarly, if one is an offender in chanting the holy name, he should submit to the holy name and thus be freed from his offenses. In this connection there is the following statement, spoken by Dak\'f1a to Lord \'c7
iva: "I did not know the glories of your personality, and therefore I committed an offense at your lotus feet in the open assembly. You are so kind, however, that you did not accept my offense. Instea
d, when I was falling down because of accusing you, you saved me by your merciful glance. You are most great. Kindly excuse me and be satisfied with your own exalted qualities."
\par One should be very humble and meek to offer one's desires and chant prayers composed in glorification of the holy name, such as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ayi mukta-kulair up\'e4sya m\'e4nam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 niv
\'e5tta-tar\'f1air upag\'e9yam\'e4n\'e4d.}{\insrsid30033  One should chant such prayers to become free from offenses at the lotus feet of the holy name.
\par (3) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Smara\'ebam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  After one regularly performs the processes of hearing and chanting and after the core of one's heart is cleansed, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 smara\'ebam,}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  remembering, is recommended. In }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (2.1.11) \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 tells King Par\'e9k\'f1it:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 etan nirvidyam\'e4n\'e4n\'e4m\line icchat\'e4m akuto-bhayam\line yogin\'e4\'e0 n\'e5pa nir
\'eb\'e9ta\'e0\line harer n\'e4m\'e4nuk\'e9rtanam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "O King, for great }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 who have completely renounced all material connections, for those who desire all material enjoyment and for those who are self-satisfied by dint of transcendental knowledge, constant chanting of the holy name of t
he Lord is recommended." According to different relationships with the Supreme Personality of Godhead, there are varieties of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e4m\'e4nuk\'e9rtanam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 chanting of the holy name, and thus according to different relationships and mellows there are five kinds of remembering. These are as follows: (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
) conducting research into the worship of a particular form of the Lord, (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 b}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
) concentrating the mind on one subject and withdrawing the mind's activities of thinking, feeling and willing from all other subjects, (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 c}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) concentra
ting upon a particular form of the Lord (this is called meditation), (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 d}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) concentrating one's mind continuously on the form of the Lord (this is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dhruv\'e4
nusm\'e5ti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or perfect meditation), and (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 e}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) awakening a likening for concentration upon a particular form (this is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sam\'e4dhi,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or trance). Mental concentration upon particular pastimes of the Lord in particular circumstances is also called remembrance. Therefore }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sam\'e4dhi,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 trance, can be possible in five different ways in terms of one's relationship. Specifically, the trance of devotees on the stage of neutrality is called mental concentration.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 (4) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid12320918 P}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4da-sevanam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  According to one's taste and strength, hearing, chanting and remembrance may be followed by }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 One obtains the perfection of remembering when one constantly thinks of the lotus feet of the Lord. Being intensely attached to thinking of the Lord's lotus feet is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 When one is particularly adherent to the process of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  this process gradually includes other proce
sses, such as seeing the form of the Lord, touching the form of the Lord, circumambulating the form or temple of the Lord, visiting such places as Jagann\'e4tha Pur\'e9, Dv\'e4rak\'e4 and Mathur\'e4
 to see the Lord's form, and bathing in the Ganges or Yamun\'e4. Bathing in the Ganges and serving a pure Vai\'f1\'ebava are also known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tad\'e9ya-up\'e4sanam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  This is also }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tad\'e9ya}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means "in relationship with the Lord." Service to the Vai\'f1\'ebava, Tulas\'e9
, Ganges and Yamun\'e4 are included in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  All these processes of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam}{\insrsid30033  help one advance in spiritual life very quickly.

\par (5) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Arcanam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  After }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4da-sevanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  comes the process of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 arcanam,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 worship of the Deity. If one is interested in the process of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 arcanam,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  one must positively take shelter of a bona fide spiritual master and learn the process from him. There are many books for }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 arcana,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  especially }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 N\'e4rada }{\cs1998\i\insrsid6447243 p}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a\'efcar\'e4tra.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  In this age, the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid6447243 P}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a\'efcar\'e4tra}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  system is particularly recommended for }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 arcana,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Deity worship. There are two systems of }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 arcana}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 \emdash the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bh\'e4gavata}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  system and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4\'efcar\'e4trik\'e9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  system. In the }
{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  there is no recommendation of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4\'efcar\'e4trik\'e9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 worship because in this Kali-yuga, even without Deity worship, everything can be perfectly performed simply through hearing, chanting, remembering and worship of the lotus feet of the Lord. R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 states:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7r\'e9-vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9 \'e7rava\'ebe par\'e9k\'f1id abhavad vaiy\'e4saki\'f9 k\'e9rtane
\line prahl\'e4da\'f9 smara\'ebe tad-a\'ecghri-bhajane lak\'f1m\'e9\'f9 p\'e5thu\'f9 p\'fcjane\line akr\'fcras tv abhivandane kapi-patir d\'e4sye 'tha sakhye 'rjuna\'f9\line sarvasv\'e4tma-nivedane balir abh\'fct k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4ptir e\'f1\'e4\'e0 param

\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja attained salvation simply by hearing, and \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m
\'e9 attained salvation simply by chanting. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja attained salvation by remembering the Lord. The goddess of fortune, Lak\'f1m\'e9dev\'e9, attained perfection by worshiping the Lord's lotus feet. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja attained salvation by worshiping the Deity of the Lord. Akr\'fcra attained salvation by offering prayers, Hanum\'e4n by rendering service, Arjuna by establishing friendship with the Lord, and Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja by offering ever
ything to the service of the Lord." All these great devotees served the Lord according to a particular process, but every one of them attained salvation and became eligible to return home, back to Godhead. This is explained in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 It is ther
efore recommended that initiated devotees follow the principles of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid6447243 N\'e4rada-p}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 a\'efcar\'e4tra}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 by worshiping the Deity in the temple. Especially for householder devotees who are opulent in material possessions, the path of Deity worship is strongly recommended. An o
pulent householder devotee who does not engage his hard-earned money in the service of the Lord is called a miser. One should not engage paid }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 to worship the Deity. If one does not personally worship the Deity but engages paid servants instead, he
 is considered lazy, and his worship of the Deity is called artificial. An opulent householder can collect luxurious paraphernalia for Deity worship, and consequently for householder devotees the worship of the Deity is compulsory. In our K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement there are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahmac\'e4r\'e9s, g\'e5hasthas, v\'e4naprasthas}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4s\'e9s,}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  but the Deity worship in the temple should be performed especially by the householders. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahmac\'e4r\'e9s}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 can go with the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4s\'e9s}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  to preach, and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 v\'e4naprasthas}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  should prepare thems
elves for the next status of renounced life, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 G\'e5hastha}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 devotees, however, are generally engaged in material activities, and therefore if they do not take to Deity worship, their falling down is positively assured. Deity worship means following the
 rules and regulations precisely. That will keep one steady in devotional service. Generally householders have children, and then the wives of the householders should be engaged in caring for the children, just as women acting as teachers care for the chi
ldren in a nursery school.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 G\'e5hastha}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 devotees must adopt the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 arcana-vidhi,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 or Deity worship according to the suitable arrangements and directions given by the spiritual master. Regarding those unable to take to the Deity worship in the temple, there is the following statement in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Agni Pur\'e4\'eba.}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 Any householder devotee circumstantially unable to worship the Deity must at least see the Deity worship, and in this way he may achieve success also. The special purpose of Deity worship is to keep oneself always pure and clean. }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 G\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  devotees should be actual examples of cleanliness.
\par Deity worship should be continued along with hearing and chanting. Therefore every }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 mantra}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is preceded by the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 nama\'f9.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  In all the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 mantras}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  there are specific potencies, of which the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  devotees must take advantage. There are many }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 mantras}
{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  preceded by the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 nama\'f9,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  but if one chants the holy name of the Lord, he receives the result of chanting }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 nama\'f9}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  many times. By chanting the holy name of the Lord, one can reach the platform of
 love of Godhead. One might ask, then what is the necessity of being initiated? The answer is that even though the chanting of the holy name is sufficient to enable one to progress in spiritual life to the standard of love of Godhead, one is nonetheless s
usceptible to contamination because of possessing a material body. Consequently, special stress is given to the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 arcana-vidhi.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  One should therefore regularly take advantage of both the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bh\'e4gavata}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  process and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p\'e4\'efcar\'e4trik\'e9}{\insrsid30033  process.
\par Deity worship has two divisions, namely pure and mixed with fruitive activities. For one who is steady, Deity worship is compulsory. Observing the various types of festivals, such as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9 Janm\'e4\'f1\'f6am\'e9, R\'e4ma-navam
\'e9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 N\'e5si\'e0ha-caturda\'e7\'e9,}{\insrsid30033  is also included in the process of Deity worship. In other words, it is compulsory for householder devotees to observe these festivals.

\par Now let us discuss the offenses in Deity worship. The following are offenses: (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to enter the temple with shoes or being carried on a palanquin, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 b}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) not to observe the prescribed festivals, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 c}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to avoid offering obeisances in front of the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 d}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to offer prayers in an unclean state, not having washed one's hands after eating, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 e}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to offer obeisances with one hand, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 f}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to circumambulate directly in front of the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to spread one's legs before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 h}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to sit before the Deity while holding one's ankles with one's hands, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 i}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to lie down before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 j}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to eat before the Deity, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to speak lies before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 l}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to address someone loudly before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 m}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to talk nonsense before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 n}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to cry before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 o}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to argue before the Deity, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to chastise someone before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 q}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to show someone favor before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 r}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to use harsh words before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 s}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to wear a woolen blanket before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 t}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to blaspheme someone before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 u}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to worship someone else before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 v}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to use vulgar language before the Deity, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 w}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to pass air before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 x}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to avoid very opulent worship of the Deity, even though one is able to perform it, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 y}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to eat something not offered to the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 z}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to avoid offering fresh fruits to the Deity according to the season, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 aa}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to offer food to the Deity which has already been used or from which has first been given to others (in other
 words, food should not be distributed to anyone else until it has been offered to the Deity), (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bb}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to sit with one's back toward the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 cc}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to offer obeisances to someone else in front of the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 dd}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) not to chant proper prayers when offering obeisances to the spiritual master, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ee}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to praise oneself before the Deity, and (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ff}{\insrsid30033 ) to blaspheme the demigods. In the worship of the Deity, these thirty-two offenses should be avoided.
\par In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Var\'e4ha Pur\'e4\'eba}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  the following offenses are mentioned: (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to eat in the house of a rich man, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 b}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to enter the Deity's room in the dark, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 c}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to worship the Deity without following the regulative principles, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 d}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to enter the temple without vibrating any sound, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 e}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to collect food that has been seen by a dog, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 f}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to break silence while offering worship to the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to go to the toilet during the time of worshiping the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 h}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to offer incense without offering flowers, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 i}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to worship the Deity with forbidden flowers, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 j}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to begin worship without having washed one's teeth, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to begin worship after sex, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 l}{\insrsid30033 
) to touch a lamp, dead body or a woman during her menstrual period, or to put on red or bluish clothing, unwashed clothing, the clothing of others or soiled clothing. Other offenses are to worship the Deity after seein
g a dead body, to pass air before the Deity, to show anger before the Deity, and to worship the Deity just after returning from a crematorium. After eating, one should not worship the Deity until one has digested his food, nor should one touch the Deity o
r engage in any Deity worship after eating safflower oil or hing. These are also offenses.
\par In other places, the following offenses are listed: (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to be against the scriptural injunctions of the Vedic literature or to disrespect within one's heart the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9ma
d-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  while externally falsely accepting its principles, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 b}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to introduce differing }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stras,}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 c}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to chew pan and betel before the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 d}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to keep flowers for worship on the leaf of a castor oil plant, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 e}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to worship the Deity in the afternoon, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 f}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to sit on the altar or to sit on the floor to worship the Deity (without a seat), (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to touch the Deity with the left hand while bathing the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 h}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to worship the Deity with a stale or used flower, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 i}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to spit while worshiping the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 j}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to adve
rtise one's glory while worshiping the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to apply }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tilaka}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  to one's forehead in a curved way, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 l}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to enter the temple without having washed one's feet, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 m}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to offer the Deity food cooked by an uninitiated person, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 n}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to worship the Deity and offer }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhoga}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  to the Deity within the vision of an uninitiated person or non-Vai\'f1\'ebava, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 o}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to offer worship to the Deity without worshiping Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha deities like Ga\'ebe\'e7a, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 p}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to worship the Deity while perspiring, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 q}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to refuse flowers offered to the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 r}{\insrsid30033 ) to take a vow or oath in the holy name of the Lord.
\par If one commits any of the above offenses, one must read at least one chapter of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  This is confirmed in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Skanda-Pur\'e4\'eba, Avant\'e9-kha\'eb\'f2a.}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Similarly, there is another injunction, stating that one who reads the thousand names of Vi\'f1\'ebu can be released from all offenses. In the same }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Skanda-Pur\'e4\'eba, Rev\'e4-kha\'eb\'f2a,}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  it is said that one who recites prayers to }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tulas\'e9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or sows a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tulas\'e9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 seed is also freed from all offenses. Similarly, one who worships the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4lagr\'e4ma-\'e7il\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  can also be relieved of offenses. In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Brahma\'eb\'f2a Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  it is said that one who worships Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, whose four hands bear a conchshell, disc, lotus flower and club, can be relieved from the above offenses. In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c4di-var\'e4ha Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\insrsid30033  it is said that a worshiper who has committed offenses may fast for one day at the holy place known as \'c7aukarava and then bathe in the Ganges.
\par In the process of worshiping the Deity it is sometimes enjoined that one worship the Deity within the mind. In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba, Uttara-kha\'eb\'f2a,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 it is said, "All persons can generally worship within the mind." The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Gautam\'e9ya Tantra}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  states, "For a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 who has no home, worship of the Deity within the mind is recommended." In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 N\'e4rada }{\cs1998\i\insrsid15860748 p}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a\'efcar\'e4tra}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  it is stated by Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a that worship of the Deity within the mind is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 m\'e4nasa-p\'fcj\'e4,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 One can become free from the four miseries by this method. Sometimes worship from the mind can be independently executed. According to the instruction of Avirhotra Muni, one of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 nava-yogendras,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 as mentioned in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  one may worship the Deity by chanting all the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 mantras.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 Eight kinds of Deities are mentioned in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and the mental Deity is one of them. In this regard, the following description is given in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Brahma-vaivarta
 Pur\'e4\'eba.
\par }{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 In the city of Prati\'f1\'f6h\'e4na-pura, long ago, there resided a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 who was poverty-stricken but innocent and not dissatisfied. One day he heard a discourse in an assembly of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  concerning how to worship the Deity in the temple. In that mee
ting, he also heard that the Deity may be worshiped within the mind. After this incident, the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  having bathed in the God\'e4var\'e9
 River, began mentally worshiping the Deity. He would wash the temple within his mind, and then in his imagination he would
 bring water from all the sacred rivers in golden and silver waterpots. He collected all kinds of valuable paraphernalia for worship, and he worshiped the Deity very gorgeously, beginning from bathing the Deity and ending with offering }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4rati.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Thus he felt 
great happiness. After many years had passed in this way, one day within his mind he cooked nice sweet rice with ghee to worship the Deity. He placed the sweet rice on a golden dish and offered it to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, but he felt that the sweet rice was very hot, and therefore he touched it with his finger. He immediately felt that his finger had been burned by the hot sweet rice, and thus he began to lament. While the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  was in pain, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu in Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha began smiling, and the goddess of fortune inquired from the Lord why He was smiling. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu then ordered His associates to bring the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  to Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha. Thus the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  attained the liberation of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 s\'e4m\'e9pya,}{
\insrsid30033  the facility of living near the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par (6) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Vandanam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Although pray
ers are a part of Deity worship, they may be considered separately like the other items, such as hearing and chanting, and therefore separate statements are given herewith. The Lord has unlimited transcendental qualities and opulences, and one who feels i
nfluenced by the Lord's qualities in various activities offers prayers to the Lord. In this way he becomes successful. In this connection, the following are some of the offenses to be avoided: (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) to offer obeisances on one hand, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 b}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to offer obeisances with one's body covered, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 c}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to show one's back to the Deity, (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 d}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) to offer obeisances on the left side of the Deity, (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 e}{\insrsid30033 ) to offer obeisances very near the Deity.
\par (7) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 D\'e4syam.}{\insrsid30033  There is the following statement in regard to assisting the Lord as a servant. After many, many thousands of births, when one comes to understand that he is an eternal servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, one can deliver others from this universe. If one simply continues to think that he is an eternal servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, even without performing any other proce
ss of devotional service, he can attain full success, for simply by this feeling one can perform all nine processes of devotional service.
\par (8) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Sakhyam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  In regard to worshiping the Lord as a friend, the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Agastya-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  states that a devotee engaged in perfo
rming devotional service by }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7rava\'ebam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'e9rtanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 sometimes wants to see the Lord personally, and for this purpose he resides in the temple. Elsewhere there is this statement: "O my Lord, Supreme Personality and eternal friend, although You are full of bli
ss and knowledge, You have become the friend of the residents of V\'e5nd\'e4
vana. How fortunate are these devotees!" In this statement the word "friend" is specifically used to indicate intense love. Friendship, therefore, is better than servitude. In the stage above }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 d\'e4sya-rasa,}{\insrsid30033 
 the devotee accepts the Supreme Personality of Godhead as a friend. This is not at all astonishing, for when a devotee is pure in heart the opulence of his worship of the Deity diminishes as spontaneous love for the Personality of Godhead
 is manifested. In this regard, \'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9 mentions \'c7r\'e9d\'e4ma Vipra, who expressed to himself his feelings of obligation, thinking, "Life after life, may I be connected with K\'e5\'f1\'eba in this friendly attitude."
\par (9) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c4tma-nivedanam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c4tma-nivedanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  re
fers to the stage at which one who has no motive other than to serve the Lord surrenders everything to the Lord and performs his activities only to please the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Such a devotee is like a cow that is cared for by its master. Wh
e
n cared for by its master, a cow is not in anxiety over its maintenance. Such a cow is always devoted to its master, and it never acts independently, but only for the master's benefit. Some devotees, therefore, consider dedication of the body to the Lord 
to be }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4tma-nivedanam,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and as stated in the book known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhakti-viveka,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  sometimes dedication of the soul to the Lord is called }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4tma-nivedanam.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The best examples of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4tma-nivedanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  are found in Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and Ambar\'e9\'f1a Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c4tma-nivedanam}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is also sometimes found in the behavior of Rukmi\'eb\'e9dev\'e9 at Dv\'e4rak\'e4.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033\charrsid16000366 SB 7.5.25
