ANDaa YaQaaNDaE\'e5PaNaqYaMaaNaa\'82\line  STae_PaqXaTaN\}YaaMau\'e5daiMan b\'d6a" )) 31 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 na te vidu\'f9 sv\'e4rtha-gati\'e0 hi vi\'f1\'ebu\'e0
\par dur\'e4\'e7ay\'e4 ye bahir-artha-m\'e4nina\'f9
\par andh\'e4 yath\'e4ndhair upan\'e9yam\'e4n\'e4s
\par te 'p\'e9\'e7a-tantry\'e4m uru-d\'e4mni baddh\'e4\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash not; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash they; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vidu\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash know; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sva-artha-gatim}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the ultimate goal of life, or their own real interest; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hi}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vi\'f1\'ebum}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and His abode; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dur\'e4\'e7ay\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash being ambitious to enjoy this material world; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ye}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash who; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bahi\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash external sense objects; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 artha-m\'e4nina\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash considering as valuable; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 andh\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash persons who are blind; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yath\'e4}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash just as; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 andhai\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by other blind men; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 upan\'e9yam\'e4n\'e4\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash being led; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash they; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 api}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash although; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7a-tantry\'e4m}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash to the ropes (laws) of material nature; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 uru}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash having very strong; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 d\'e4mni}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash cords; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 baddh\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash bound.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 Persons who are strongly entrapped by the consciousness o
f enjoying material life, and who have therefore accepted as their leader or guru a similar blind man attached to external sense objects, cannot understand that the goal of life is to return home, back to Godhead, and engage in the service of Lord Vi\'f1
\'ebu. A
s blind men guided by another blind man miss the right path and fall into a ditch, materially attached men led by another materially attached man are bound by the ropes of fruitive labor, which are made of very strong cords, and they continue again and ag
ain in materialistic life, suffering the threefold miseries.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
Since there must always be a difference of opinion between demons and devotees, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, when criticized by his son Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, should not have been surprised that Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja differed from his way of life. Nonetheless, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was extremely angry and wanted to rebuke his son for deriding his teacher or spiritual master, who had been born in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  family of the great }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4c\'e4rya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7ukra}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means "semen," and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4c\'e4rya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  refers to a teacher or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  Hereditary }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 gurus,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  or spiritual masters, have been accepted everywhere since time immemorial, but Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja declined to accept such a seminal }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  or take instruction from him. An actual }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7rotriya,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  one who has heard or received perfect knowledge through }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 parampar\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 the disciplic succession. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja did not recognize a seminal spiritual master. Such spiritual masters are not at all interested in Vi\'f1\'ebu. Indeed, they are hopeful of material success (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
bahir-artha-m\'e4nina\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bahi\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means "external," }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 artha}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means "interest," and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4nina}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 means "taking very seriously." Generally speaking, practically everyone is unaware of the spiritual world. The knowledge of the materialists is res
tricted within the four-billion-mile limit of this material world, which is in the dark portion of the creation; they do not know that beyond the material world is the spiritual world. Unless one is a devotee of the Lord, one cannot understand the existen
ce of the spiritual world. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Gurus,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  teachers, who are simply interested in this material world are described in this verse as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 andha,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  blind. Such blind men may lead many other blind followers without true knowledge of material conditions, but they are not accepted by devotees like Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja. Such blind teachers, being interested in the external, material world, are always bound by the strong ropes of material nature.
