and fully engaged in thought of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 govinda-parirambhita\'f9.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja engaged himself always in meditation, and thus he was protected by Govinda. Just as a small child on the lap of his father or mother is fully protected, a devotee, in all conditions, is protected by the Supreme Lord. Does this mean that when Prahl\'e4
da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was attacked by the demons, the R\'e4k\'f1asas, Govinda was also attacked by the demons? This is not possible. There have been many at
tempts by the demons to hurt or kill the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but He cannot be injured by any material means because He is always in transcendence. Therefore the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pare brahma\'ebi}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  are used here. The demons, the R\'e4k\'f1asas, can neither see nor to
uch the Supreme Lord, although they may superficially think that they are striking the Lord's transcendental body with their material weapons. The Supreme Personality of Godhead is described in this verse as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 anirde\'e7ye.
}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  We cannot understand Him to be in a particular place, for He is all-pervasive. Moreover, He is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 akhil\'e4tm\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 the active principle of everything, even material weapons. Those who cannot understand the position of the Lord are unfortunate. They may think that they can kill the Supreme Personality 
of Godhead and His devotee, but all their attempts will be futile. The Lord knows how to deal with them.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.5.42
