\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu wanted Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja to be trained as a diplomatic king in ruling the kingdom, the country or the world, but not to be advised about renunciation or the renounced order of life. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  here does not refer to some religious faith. As clearly stated, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharmo hy asyopade\'f1\'f6avyo r\'e4j\'ef\'e4\'e0 yo g\'e5ha-medhin\'e4m.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  There are two kinds of royal families\emdash one whose members are simply attached to household life and the other consisting of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 r\'e4jar\'f1is,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  kings who govern with ruling power but are as good as great saints. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja wanted to become a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 r\'e4jar\'f1i,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  whereas Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu wanted him to become a king attached to sense enjoyment (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 g\'e5ha-medhin\'e4m}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). Therefore in the 
\'c4ryan system there is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  by which everyone should be educated according to his position in society's division of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 var\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7
\'fcdra}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ) and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4\'e7rama}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahmacarya, g\'e5hastha, v\'e4naprastha}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 A devotee purified by devotional service is always in the transcen
dental position above the mundane qualities. Thus the difference between Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was that Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu wanted to keep Prahl\'e4da in mundane attachment whereas Prahl\'e4
da was above the modes of material nature. As long as one is under the control of material nature, his occupational duty is different from that of a person not under such control. One's real }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma,}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or occupational duty, is described in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma\'e0 tu s\'e4k\'f1
\'e4d bhagavat-pra\'eb\'e9tam}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). As described to his order carriers by Dharmar\'e4ja, or Yamar\'e4ja, a living being is a spiritual identity, and therefore his occupational duty is also spiritual. The real }
{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  is that which is advised in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  One must give up
 one's material occupational duties, just as one must give up his material body. Whatever one's occupational duty, even according to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 system, one must give it up and engage in one's spiritual function. One's real }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or occupational duty, is explained by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 J\'e9vera 'svar\'fcpa' haya-k\'e5\'f1\'ebera 'nitya-d\'e4sa': }{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 every living being is an eternal servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. That is one's real occupational duty.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.5.52
