One whose mind and senses are uncontrolled becomes increasingly attached to family life because of insatiable lusty desires and very strong illusi
on. In such a madman's life, the remaining years are also wasted because even during those years he cannot engage himself in devotional service.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
This is the account of one hundred years of life. Although in this age a lifetime of one hundred years 
is generally not possible, even if one has one hundred years, the calculation is that fifty years are wasted in sleeping, twenty years in childhood and boyhood, and twenty years in invalidity (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 jar\'e4-vy\'e4dhi}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). This leaves only a few more years, but because of
 too much attachment to household life, those years are also spent with no purpose, without God consciousness. Therefore, one should be trained to be a perfect }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  in the beginning of life and then to be perfect in sense control, following the regulative principles, if one becomes a householder. From household life one is ordered to accept }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 v\'e4naprastha}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  life and go to the forest and then accept }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 That is the perfection of life. From the very beginning of life, those who are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ajitendriya,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  who can
not control their senses, are educated only for sense gratification, as we have seen in the Western countries. Thus the entire duration of a life of even one hundred years is wasted and misused, and at the time of death one transmigrates to another body, 
which may not be human. At the end of one hundred years, one who has not acted as a human being in a life of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tapasya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 (austerity and penance) must certainly be embodied again in a body like those of cats, dogs and hogs. Therefore this life of lusty desires and sense gratification is extremely risky.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.6.9
