\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
What person too attached to household life due to being unable to control his senses can liberate himself? An attached householder is bound very strongly by ropes of affection for his family [wife, children and other relatives].
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's first proposal was }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kaum\'e4ra \'e4caret pr\'e4j\'efo dharm\'e4n bh\'e4gavat\'e4n iha: }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 "One who is sufficiently intelligent should use the human form of body from the very beginning of life
\emdash in other words, from the tender age of childhood\emdash to practice the activities of devotional service, giving up all other engagements." }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Dharm\'e4n bh\'e4gavat\'e4n}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  means the religious principle of reviving our relationship with the Supreme Personality of Godhead. For this purpose K\'e5\'f1\'eba personally advises, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-dharm\'e4
n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 "Give up all other duties and surrender unto Me." While in the material world we manufacture so many duties in the name of so many isms, but our actual duty is to free ourselves fr
om the cycle of birth, death, old age and disease. For this purpose, one must first be liberated from material bondage, and especially from household life. Household life is actually a kind of license for a materially attached person by which to enjoy sen
se gratification under regulative principles. Otherwise there is no need of entering household life.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
Before entering household life, one should be trained as a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 brahmac\'e4r\'e9,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  living under the care of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 guru,}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 whose place is known as the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 guru-kula.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Brahmac\'e4r\'e9 guru-kule vasan d\'e4nto guror hitam}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{
\cs3007\i\insrsid5139582\charrsid5139582 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  7.12.1). From the very beginning, a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 is trained to sacrifice everything for the benefit of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 guru.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  A }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 is advised to go begging alms door to door, addressing all women as mother, and whatever he collects goes to the benefit of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 guru.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 In this way he learns how to control his senses and sacrifice everything for the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 guru.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  When he is fully trained, if he likes he is allowed to marry. Thus he is not an ordinary }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  who has learned only how to satisfy his senses. A trained }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 can gradually give up household life and go to the forest to become increasingly enlightened in spiritual life and at last take }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja explained to his father that to be freed from all material anxieties one should go to the forest. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Hitv\'e4tma-p\'e4ta\'e0 g\'e5ham andha-k\'fcpam.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 One should give up his household, which is a place for going further and further down into the darkest regions of material existence. The first advice, therefore, is that one must give up household life (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5ham andha-k\'fcpam}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
). However, if one prefers to remain in the dark well of household life because of uncontrolled senses, he becomes increasingly entangled by ropes of affection for his wife, children, servants, house, money and so on. Su
ch a person cannot attain liberation from material bondage. Therefore children should be taught from the very beginning of life to be first-class }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 brahmac\'e4r\'e9s.}{\insrsid30033 
 Then it will be possible for them to give up household life in the future.
\par To return home, back to Godhead, one must be completely free from material attachment. Therefore, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  means }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 vair\'e4gya-vidy\'e4,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 the art that can help one develop a distaste for material enjoyment.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 v\'e4sudeve bhagavati\line bhakti-yoga\'f9 prayojita\'f9\line janayaty \'e4\'e7u vair\'e4
gya\'e0\line j\'ef\'e4na\'e0 ca yad ahaitukam
