Svalpam apy asya dharmasya tr\'e4yate mahato bhay\'e4t:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  if one performs even very slight devotional service, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba is always ready to save one from the greatest danger. The definite example is Aj\'e4mila. Aj\'e4
mila separated himself from the Supreme Personality of Godhead by performing many sinful activities and was condemned by Yamar\'e4ja to be very severely punished, but because at the time of death he chanted the name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, although he was calling not for the Supreme Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba but for his son named N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, he was saved from the hands of Yamar\'e4ja. Therefore, pleasing N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a does not require as much endeavor as pleasing one's family, community and nation. We have seen important political leaders killed for a slight discrepancy in their behavior. Therefore pleasing one's society, family, community and nation is extremely
 difficult. Pleasing N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, however, is not at all difficult; it is very easy.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 One's duty is to revive one's relationship with N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
