\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead, the supreme controller, who is infallible and indefatigable, is present in different forms of life, from the inert living beings [sth\'e4vara], such as the plants, to Brahm\'e4, the foremost created
 living being. He is also present in the varieties of material creations and in the material elements, the total material energy and the modes of material nature [sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba and tamo-gu\'eb
a], as well as the unmanifested material nature and the fa
lse ego. Although He is one, He is present everywhere, and He is also the transcendental Supersoul, the cause of all causes, who is present as the observer in the cores of the hearts of all living entities. He is indicated as that which is pervaded and as
 the all-pervading Supersoul, but actually He cannot be indicated. He is changeless and undivided. He is simply perceived as the supreme sac-cid-\'e4
nanda [eternity, knowledge and bliss]. Being covered by the curtain of the external energy, to the atheist He appears nonexistent.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s3008\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14425756 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
Not only is the Supreme Personality of Godhead present as the Supersoul of all living entities; at the same time, He pervades everything in the entire creation. He exists in all circumstances and at all times. He exists in the heart of Lord Brahm\'e4
 and also in the cores of the hearts of the hogs, dogs, trees, plants and so on. He is present everywhere. He is present not only in the heart of the living entity, but also in material things, even in the atoms, protons and electrons be
ing explored by material scientists.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 The Lord is present in three features\emdash 
as Brahman, Param\'e4tm\'e4 and Bhagav\'e4n. Because He is present everywhere, He is described as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sarva\'e0 khalv ida\'e0 brahma.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Vi\'f1\'ebu exists beyond Brahman. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  confirms that K\'e5\'f1\'eba, by His Brahman feature, is all-pervading (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarvam}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ), but Brahman depends upon K
\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 brahma\'ebo hi prati\'f1\'f6h\'e4ham}{\insrsid30033 ). Without K\'e5\'f1\'eba, there could be no existence of Brahman or Param\'e4tm\'e4. Therefore, Bhagav\'e4n, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is the 
ultimate realization of the Absolute Truth. Although He is present as the Param\'e4tm\'e4 in the core of everyone's heart, He is nonetheless one, either as an individual or as the all-pervading Brahman.
\par The supreme cause is K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and devotees who have surrendered to the Supreme Personality of Godhead can realize Him and His presence within the universe and within the atom (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a\'eb\'f2\'e4ntara-stha-param\'e4\'ebu-cay\'e4
ntara-stham}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). This realization is possible only for devotees who have fully surrendered unto the lotus feet of the Lord; for others it is not possible. This is confirmed by the Lord Himself in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (7.14):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1\'e4 gu\'eba-may\'e9\line mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4\line m\'e4
m eva ye prapadyante\line m\'e4y\'e4m et\'e4\'e0 taranti te
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The process of surrender in a devotional attitude is accepted by a
 fortunate living being. After wandering through many varieties of life on many planetary systems, when one comes to the real understanding of the Absolute Truth by the grace of a devotee, one surrenders to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as confirmed
 in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 janman\'e4m ante j\'ef\'e4nav\'e4n m\'e4\'e0 prapadyate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's class friends, who were born of Daitya families, thought that realizing the Absolute was extremely difficult. Indeed, we have experience that many, many people say this v
ery thing. Actually, however, this is not so. The Absolute, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is most intimately related to all living entities. Therefore if one understands the Vai\'f1\'eb
ava philosophy, which explains how He is present everywhere and how He acts everywhere, to worship the Supreme Lord or to realize Him is not at all difficult. Realization of the Lord, however, is possible only in the association of devotees. Therefore 
\'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, in His teachings to R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said (Cc. }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Madhya}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  19.151):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahm\'e4\'eb\'f2a bhramite kona bh\'e4gyav\'e4n j\'e9va\line guru-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pras\'e4
de p\'e4ya bhakti-lat\'e4-b\'e9ja
