\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 The Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4
}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (18.55), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti y\'e4v\'e4n ya\'e7 c\'e4smi tattvata\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 "One can understand the Supreme Personality as He is only by devotional service." Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja ultimately instructed his class friends, the sons of the demons, to accept the process of devotional service by preaching the science of K\'e5
\'f1\'eba consciousness to everyone. Preaching is the best service to the Lord. The Lord will immediately be extremely satisfied with one who engages in this service of preaching K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. This is confirmed by the Lord Himself in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (18.69). }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Na ca tasm\'e4n manu\'f1ye\'f1u ka\'e7cin me priya-k\'e5ttama\'f9:}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  "There is no servant in this world more dear to Me than he, nor will there ever be one more dear." If one sincerely tries his best to spread K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness by preaching the glories of the Lord and His supremacy, even if he is imperfectly educated, he becomes the dearmost servant of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  As one performs this service for humanity, without discrimination between friends and enemies, the Lord becomes satisfied, and the mission of one's life is fulfilled. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu therefore advised everyone to become a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 devotee and preach K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 y\'e4re dekha, t\'e4re kaha 'k\'e5\'f1
\'eba'-upade\'e7a}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
). That is the easiest way to realize the Supreme Personality of Godhead. By such preaching, the preacher becomes satisfied, and those to whom he preaches are also satisfied. This is the process of bringing peace and tranquillity to the entire world.

\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4\'e0\line sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam\line suh\'e5da\'e0
 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line j\'ef\'e4tv\'e4 m\'e4\'e0 \'e7\'e4ntim \'e5cchati}{\cs1998\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 One is expected to understand these three formulas of knowledge concerning the Supreme Lord
\emdash that He is the supreme enjoyer, that He is th
e proprietor of everything, and that He is the best well-wisher and friend of everyone. A preacher should personally understand these truths and preach them to everyone. Then there will be peace and tranquillity all over the world.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sauh\'e5dam}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  ("friendliness") is very significant in this verse. People are generally ignorant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, and therefore to become their best well-wisher one should teach them about K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness without discrimination. Since the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'ebu, is situated in the core of everyone's heart, every body is a temple of Vi\'f1\'ebu. One should not misuse this understanding as an excuse for such words as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  If N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba lives in the house of a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daridra,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 a poor man, this does not mean that N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba becomes poor. He lives everywhere\emdash in the houses of the poor and those of the rich\emdash but in all circumstances He remains N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a; to think that He becomes either poor or rich is a material calculation. He is always }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'f1a\'f2-ai\'e7varya-p\'fcr\'eba,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  full in six opulences, in all circumstances.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.6.25
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 25
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid30033 \b\v\f75\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 Tau\'ede c Ta\}a ik-Mal/>YaMaNaNTa Aa}{\f0\insrsid30033 \'db}{\f35\insrsid30033 e
\line  ik&- TaEGauR<aVYaiTak-raidh Yae SviSa\'d6a" }{\insrsid30033 )\line DaMaaRdYa" ik-MaGau<aeNa c k-ai\'bfTaeNa\line  Saar&Jauza& cr<aYaae\'e5PaGaaYaTaa& Na" )) 25 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 tu\'f1\'f6e ca tatra kim alabhyam ananta \'e4dye
\par ki\'e0 tair gu\'eba-vyatikar\'e4d iha ye sva-siddh\'e4\'f9
\par dharm\'e4daya\'f9 kim agu\'ebena ca k\'e4\'eck\'f1itena
\par s\'e4ra\'e0 ju\'f1\'e4\'e0 cara\'ebayor upag\'e4yat\'e4\'e0 na\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tu\'f1\'f6e}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
when satisfied; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ca}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash also; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tatra}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash that; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kim}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash what; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 alabhyam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash unobtainable; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 anante}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4dye}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the original source of everything, the cause of all causes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kim}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash what need; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tai\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash with them; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gu\'eba-vyatikar\'e4t}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash due to the actions of the modes of material nature; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iha}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash in this world; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ye}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash which; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sva-siddh\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash automatically achieved; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dharma-\'e4daya\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the three principles of material advancement, namely religion, economic development and sense gratification; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kim}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
what need; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 agu\'ebena}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash with liberation into the Supreme; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ca}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash and; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e4\'eck\'f1itena}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash desired; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 s\'e4ram}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash essence; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ju\'f1\'e4m}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash relishing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 cara\'ebayo\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the two lotus feet of the Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 upag\'e4yat\'e4m}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash who glorify the qualities of the Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of us.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
Nothing is unobtainable for devotees who have satisfied the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the cause of all causes, the original source of everything. The Lord is the reservoir of unlimited sp
iritual qualities. For devotees, therefore, who are transcendental to the modes of material nature, what is the use of following the principles of religion, economic development, sense gratification and liberation, which are all automatically obtainable u
nder the influence of the modes of nature? We devotees always glorify the lotus feet of the Lord, and therefore we need not ask for anything in terms of dharma, k\'e4ma, artha and mok\'f1a.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 In an advanced civilization, people are eager to be religious, to
 be economically well situated, to satisfy their senses to the fullest extent, and at last to attain liberation. However, these are not to be magnified as desirable. Indeed, for a devotee these are all very easily available. Bilvama\'ecgala \'d6h\'e4
kura said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mukti\'f9 svaya\'e0 mukulit\'e4\'efjali sevate 'sm\'e4n dharm\'e4rtha-k\'e4ma-gataya\'f9 samaya-prat\'e9k\'f1\'e4\'f9.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 Liberation always stands at the door of a devotee, ready to carry out his orders. Material advancement in religion, economic development, sense gratification and liberation simp
ly wait to serve a devotee at the first opportunity. A devotee is already in a transcendental position; he does not need further qualifications to be liberated. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (14.26), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa gu\'eb\'e4n samat\'e9tyait\'e4n brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  a devotee
 is transcendental to the actions and reactions of the three modes of material nature because he is situated on the Brahman platform.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 agu
\'ebena ca k\'e4\'eck\'f1itena:}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  if one is engaged in the transcendental loving service of the lotus feet of the Lord, he does not need anything in terms of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma, artha, k
\'e4ma}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mok\'f1a.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  therefore, in the beginning of the transcendental literature, it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma\'f9 projjhita-kaitavo 'tra.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Dharma, artha, k\'e4ma}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mok\'f1a}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kaitava}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 \emdash false and unnecessary. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Nirmatsar\'e4\'eb\'e4m,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 persons who are completely transcendental to the material activities of separateness, who make no distinction between "mine" and "yours," but who simply engage in the devotional service of the Lord, are actually fit to accept }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharm\'e4n bhagavat\'e4n iha}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). Because they are }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nirmatsara,}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  not jealous of anyone, they want to make others devotees, even their enemies. In this regard, \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya remarks, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e4\'eck\'f1ate mok\'f1a-gam api sukha\'e0 n\'e4k\'e4\'eck\'f1ato yath\'e4.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Devotees are n
ot desirous of any material happiness, including the happiness derived from liberation. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnya\'e0 j\'ef\'e4na-karm\'e4dy-an\'e4v\'e5tam.}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Karm\'e9s}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  desire material happiness, and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  desire liberation, but a devotee does not desire anything; he i
s simply satisfied by rendering transcendental loving service at the lotus feet of the Lord and glorifying Him everywhere by preaching, which is his life and soul.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.6.26
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 26
