occupational duties, or one's livelihood; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 manye}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash I consider; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tat}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash them; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 etat}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash these; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 akhilam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash all; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 nigamasya}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 Vedas;}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 satyam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash truth; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sva-\'e4tma-arpa\'ebam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the full surrendering of one's self; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sva-suh\'e5da\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
unto the supreme friend; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 paramasya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the ultimate; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pu\'e0sa\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash personality.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 Religion, economic development and sense gratification\emdash 
these are described in the Vedas as tri-varga, or three ways to salvation. Within these three categories are
 education and self-realization; ritualistic ceremonies performed according to Vedic injunction; logic; the science of law and order; and the various means of earning one's livelihood. These are the external subject matters of study in the Vedas, and ther
efore I consider them material. However, I consider surrender to the lotus feet of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu to be transcendental.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 These instructions of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja stress the transcendental position of devotional service. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (14.26):
