\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash like; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 v\'e5k\'f1asya}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash of a tree; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e4lena}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 
\emdash in due course of time; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7vara-m\'fcrtin\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash whose form is the ability to transform or control the bodily activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 Just as the fruits and flowers of a tree in due course of 
time undergo six changes\emdash birth, existence, growth, transformation, dwindling and then death\emdash 
the material body, which is obtained by the spirit soul under different circumstances, undergoes similar changes. However, there are no such changes for the spirit soul.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
This is a very important verse in understanding the difference between the spiritual soul and the material body. The soul is eternal, as stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 (2.20):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 na j\'e4yate mriyate v\'e4 kad\'e4cin\line n\'e4ya\'e0 bh\'fctv\'e4 bhavit\'e4 v\'e4 na bh
\'fcya\'f9\line ajo nitya\'f9 \'e7\'e4\'e7vato 'ya\'e0 pur\'e4\'ebo\line na hanyate hanyam\'e4ne \'e7ar\'e9re
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"For the soul there is never birth nor death. Nor, having once been, does he ever cease to be. He is unborn, eternal, ever-existing, undying and primeval. He is not slain when the body is slain." The spirit 
soul is eternal, being freed from waste and change, which take place because of the material body. The example of a tree and its fruits and flowers is very simple and clear. A tree stands for many, many years, but with the seasonal changes its fruits and 
f
lowers undergo six transformations. The foolish theory of modern chemists that life can be produced by chemical interactions cannot be accepted as truth. The birth of a human being's material body takes place due to a mixture of the ovum and semen, but th
e
 history of birth is that although the ovum and semen mix together after sex, there is not always pregnancy. Unless the soul enters the mixture, there is no possibility of pregnancy, but when the soul takes shelter of the mixture the body takes birth, exi
s
ts, grows, transforms and dwindles, and ultimately it is vanquished. The fruits and flowers of a tree seasonally come and go, but the tree continues to stand. Similarly, the transmigrating soul accepts various bodies, which undergo six transformations, bu
t the soul remains permanently the same (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ajo nitya\'f9 \'e7\'e4\'e7vato 'ya\'e0 pur\'e4\'ebo na hanyate hanyam\'e4ne \'e7ar\'e9re}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
). The soul is eternal and ever existing, but the bodies accepted by the soul are changing.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 There are two kinds of soul\emdash the Supreme Soul (the Personality of G
odhead) and the individual soul (the living entity). As various bodily changes take place in the individual soul, different millenniums of creation take place in the Supreme Soul. In this regard, Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'f1a\'f2 vik\'e4r\'e4\'f9 \'e7ar\'e9rasya\line na vi\'f1\'ebos tad-gatasya\line ca tad-adh
\'e9na\'e0 \'e7ar\'e9ra\'e0 ca\line j\'ef\'e4tv\'e4 tan mamat\'e4\'e0 tyajet
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
Since the body is the external feature of the soul, the soul is not dependent on the body; rather, the body is dependent on the soul. One who understands this truth should not be very much anxious about
 the maintenance of his body. There is no possibility of maintaining the body permanently or eternally. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Antavanta ime deh\'e4 nityasyokt\'e4\'f9 \'e7ar\'e9ri\'eba\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  This is the statement of }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (2.18). The material body is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 antavat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (perishable), but the soul within the body is eternal (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nityasyokt\'e4\'f9 \'e7ar\'e9ri\'eba\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and the individual souls, who are part and parcel of Him, are both eternal. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Nityo nity\'e4n\'e4\'e0
 cetana\'e7 cetan\'e4n\'e4m.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is the chief living being, whereas the individual living entities are parts of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. All the various grades of bodies\emdash 
from the gigantic universal body to the small body of an ant\emdash are perishable, but the Supersoul and the soul, being equal in quality, both exist eternally. This is further explained in the next verses.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.19, SB 7.7.20, SB 7.7.19-20
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXTS 19-20
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
