-Ya" Svd*Ga( heTauVYaaRPak-ae_Sa&GYaNaav*Ta" )) 19 ))\line WTaE\'dcaRdXai>aivR\'dcaNaaTMaNaae l/+a<aE" ParE" )\line Ah& MaMaeTYaSa\'d9av& dehadaE MaaehJa& TYaJaeTa( )) 20 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4 nityo 'vyaya\'f9 \'e7uddha
\par eka\'f9 k\'f1etra-j\'efa \'e4\'e7raya\'f9
\par avikriya\'f9 sva-d\'e5g hetur
\par vy\'e4pako 'sa\'ecgy an\'e4v\'e5ta\'f9
\par }\pard \s23\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid30033 etair dv\'e4da\'e7abhir vidv\'e4n
\par }\pard \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid30033 \'e4tmano lak\'f1a\'ebai\'f9 parai\'f9
\par aha\'e0 mamety asad-bh\'e4va\'e0
\par deh\'e4dau mohaja\'e0 tyajet
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
the spirit soul, the part of the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 nitya\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash without birth or death; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 avyaya\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash with no possibility of dwindling; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7uddha\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash without the material contamination of attachment and detachment; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 eka\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash individual; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'f1etra-j\'efa\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
who knows and is therefore different from the material body; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \'e4\'e7raya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid15361046\charrsid15361046 \emdash }{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 the original foundation;}{
\cs1867\fs16\cf27\up12\insrsid12398837\charrsid12398837 1}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046   }{\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 avikriya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid15361046\charrsid15361046 \emdash }{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 
not undergoing changes like the body;}{\cs1867\fs14\cf27\up12\insrsid12398837\charrsid12398837 2}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046  }{\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 sva-d\'e5k}{\fs28\insrsid15361046\charrsid15361046 \emdash }{
\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 self-illuminated;}{\cs1867\fs14\cf27\up12\insrsid12398837\charrsid12398837 3}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 hetu\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash 
the cause of all causes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 vy\'e4paka\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash spreading throughout the body in the form of consciousness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 asa\'ecg\'e9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash not depending on the body (free to transmigrate from one body to another); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 an\'e4v\'e5ta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash 
not covered by material contamination; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 etai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash by all these; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 dv\'e4da\'e7abhi\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash twelve; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 vidv\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash a person who is not foolish but fully aware of things as they are; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \'e4tmana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash of the spirit soul; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 lak\'f1a\'ebai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash symptoms; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 parai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash transcendental; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 aham}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash I ("I am this body"); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 mama}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash mine ("everything in relationship with this body is mine"); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 iti}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash 
thus; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 asat-bh\'e4vam}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash a false conception of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 deha-\'e4dau}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash 
identifying oneself with the material body and then with one's wife, children, family, community, nation and so on; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 moha-jam}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash produced from illusory knowledge; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 tyajet}{\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid15361046 \emdash must give up.
\par }\pard\plain \s858\ql \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\tx360\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4544364 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs16\cf27\up12\insrsid4544364\charrsid12398837 \chftn }{
\cs1998\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid15361046 Without the shelter of the spirit soul, the material body cannot exist.}{\i\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid15361046 
\par }{\cs1867\fs16\cf27\up12\insrsid15361046\charrsid12398837 2}{\cs1998\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid15361046 As already explained, the fruits and flowers of a tree take birth, exist, grow, transform, dwindle
 and die according to seasonal changes, but the tree, through all of these changes remains the same. Similarly, the }{\cs1998\i\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid12398837 \'e4tm\'e4}{\i\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid15361046  }{
\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid15361046 is free from all changes}{\i\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid15361046 .
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15361046 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs16\cf27\up12\insrsid15361046\charrsid12398837 3}{
\fs22\cf27\insrsid4544364\charrsid15361046 One does not need to make the soul prominent; it is automatically prominent. One can very easily understand that in the living body there is a spiritual soul.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 "\'c4tm\'e4
" refers to the Supreme Lord or the living entities. Both of them are spiritual, free from birth and death, free from deterioration and free from material contamination. They are individua
l, they are the knowers of the external body, and they are the foundation or shelter of everything. They are free from material change, they are self-illuminated, they are the cause of all causes, and they are all-pervading. They have nothing to do with t
h
e material body, and therefore they are always uncovered. With these transcendental qualities, one who is actually learned must give up the illusory conception of life, in which one thinks, "I am this material body, and everything in relationship with thi
s body is mine."
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (15.7) Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba clearly says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mamaiv\'e4\'e0\'e7o j\'e9va-loke j\'e9va-bh\'fcta\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 "All the living entities are part of Me." Therefore the living entities are qualitatively the same as the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the leader, the Supreme among all the living entities. In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vedas}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nityo nity\'e4n\'e4\'e0 cetana\'e7 cetan\'e4n\'e4m:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 the Lord is the chief individual living entity, the leader of the subordinate living entities. Because the living entities are parts or samples of
 God, their qualities are not different from those of the Supreme Lord. The living entities have the same qualities as the Lord, just as a drop of sea water is composed of the same chemicals as the great sea itself. Thus there is oneness in quality but a 
d
ifference in quantity. One can understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead by understanding the sample, the living entity, because all the qualities of God exist in a minute quantity in the living entities. There is oneness, but God is great whereas the
 living entities are extremely small. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 A\'ebor a\'eb\'e9y\'e4n mahato mah\'e9y\'e4n}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Ka\'f6ha Upani\'f1ad}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  1.2.20). The living entities are smaller than the atom, but God is greater than the greatest. Our conception of greatness may be represented by the sky because we think of the 
sky as being unlimitedly big, but God is bigger than the sky. Similarly, we have knowledge that the living entities are smaller than atoms, being one ten-thousandth the size of the tip of a hair, yet the quality of being the supreme cause of all causes ex
i
sts in the living entity as well as in the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Indeed, it is due to the presence of the living entity that the body exists and bodily changes take place. Similarly, it is because the Supreme Lord is within this universe that th
e changes dictated by the material laws occur.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 eka\'f9,}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  meaning "individual," is significant. As explained in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (9.4), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 mat-sth\'e4ni sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni na c\'e4ha
\'e0 te\'f1v avasthita\'f9.}{\insrsid30033  Everything, material and spiritual, including earth, water, air, fire
, sky and the living entities, exists on the platform of spirit soul. Although everything is an emanation from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one should not think that the Supreme Lord is dependent upon anything else.
\par Both God and the living entity are fully conscious. As living entities, we are conscious of our bodily existence. Similarly, the Lord is conscious of the gigantic cosmic manifestation. This is confirmed in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Vedas.}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Yasmin dyau\'f9 p\'e5thiv\'e9 c\'e4ntar\'e9k\'f1am. Vij\'ef\'e4t\'e4ram adhikena vij\'e4n\'e9y\'e4t. Ekam ev\'e4dvit\'e9yam. \'c4tma-jyoti\'f9 samr\'e4\'f2 ihov\'e4ca. Sa im\'e4n lok\'e4n as\'e5
jata. Satya\'e0 j\'ef\'e4nam anantam. Asa\'ecgo hy aya\'e0 puru\'f1a\'f9. P\'fcr\'ebasya p\'fcr\'ebam \'e4d\'e4ya p\'fcr\'ebam ev\'e4}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4148974 va\'e7i\'f1yate}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 .}{\insrsid30033 
 All these Vedic injunctions prove that both the Supreme Personality of Godhead and the minute soul are individual. One is great, and the other is small, but both of them are the cause of all causes\emdash 
the corporally limited and the universally unlimited.
\par We should always remember that although we are equal to the Supreme Personality of Godhead in quality, we ar
e never equal to Him in quantity. Persons with a small fund of intelligence, finding themselves equal in quality with God, foolishly think that they are equal in quantity also. Their intelligence is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 avi\'e7uddha-buddhaya
\'f9}{\insrsid4148974 \emdash }{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 unpolished or contaminated intelligence. When such persons, after endeavoring hard for many, many lives to understand the supreme cause, are finally in actual knowledge of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, V
\'e4sudeva, they surrender unto Him (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 v\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). Thus they become great }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 mah\'e4tm\'e4s,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 perfect souls. If one is fortunate enough to understand his relationship with God, knowing that God is great (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 vibhu}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ) whereas the living entity is small (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 a\'ebu}{
\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ), he is perfect in knowledge. The individual exists in darkness when he thinks that he is the material body and that everything in relationship with the material body belongs to him. This is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 
aha\'e0 mama}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 janasya moho 'yam aha\'e0 mameti}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 ). This is illusion. One must give up his illusory conception and thus become fully aware of everything.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.21
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 21
