\par k\'f1etre\'f1u dehe\'f1u tath\'e4tma-yogair
\par adhy\'e4tma-vid brahma-gati\'e0 labheta
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 svar\'ebam}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash gold; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yath\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash just as; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gr\'e4vasu}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash in the stones of gold ore; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hema-k
\'e4ra\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the expert who knows about gold; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'f1etre\'f1u}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash in the gold mines; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yogai\'f9}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by various processes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tat-abhij\'efa\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash an expert who can understand where gold is; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4
pnuy\'e4t}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash very easily obtains; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'f1etre\'f1u}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash within the material fields; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dehe\'f1u}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the human bodies and all the rest of the 8,400,000 different bodily forms; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tath\'e4}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash similarly; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4tma-yogai\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by spiritual processes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 adhy\'e4tma-vit}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash one who is expert in und
erstanding the distinction between spirit and matter; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 brahma-gatim}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash perfection in spiritual life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 labheta}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash may obtain.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
An expert geologist can understand where there is gold and by various processes can extract it from the gold ore. Similarly, a 
spiritually advanced person can understand how the spiritual particle exists within the body, and thus by cultivating spiritual knowledge he can attain perfection in spiritual life. However, as one who is not expert cannot understand where there is gold, 
a foolish person who has not cultivated spiritual knowledge cannot understand how the spirit exists within the body.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
Here is a very good example concerning spiritual understanding. Foolish rascals, including so-called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  philosophers and scient
ists, cannot understand the existence of the soul within the body because they are lacking in spiritual knowledge. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vedas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  enjoin, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
tad-vij\'ef\'e4n\'e4rtha\'e0 sa gurum ev\'e4bhigacchet: }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 to understand spiritual knowledge, one must approach a bona fide spiritual master.
 Unless one has been trained in geology, one cannot detect gold in stone. Similarly, unless one has been trained by a spiritual master, he cannot understand what is spirit and what is matter. Here it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
yogais tad-abhij\'efa\'f9.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  This indicates that one wh
o has connected himself with spiritual knowledge can understand that there is a spiritual soul within the body. However, one who is in an animalistic conception of life and has no spiritual culture cannot understand. As an expert mineralogist or geologist
 
can understand where there is gold and can then invest his money to dig there and chemically separate the gold from the ore, an expert spiritualist can understand where the soul is within matter. One who has not been trained cannot distinguish between gol
d and stone. Similarly, fools and rascals who have not learned from an expert spiritual master what is soul and what is matter cannot understand the existence of the soul within the body. To understand such knowledge, one must be trained in the mystic }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  system, or, finally, in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  system. As stated in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (18.55), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 Unless one takes shelter of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  process, one cannot understand the existence of the soul within the body. Therefore }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  begins by teaching:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dehino 'smin yath\'e4 dehe\line kaum\'e4ra\'e0 yauvana\'e0 jar\'e4\line tath\'e4 deh\'e4
ntara-pr\'e4ptir\line dh\'e9ras tatra na muhyati
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"As the embodied soul continually passes, in this body, from boyhood to youth to old age, the soul similarly passes into another body at death. The
 self-realized soul is not bewildered by such a change." (Bg. 2.13) Thus the first instruction is that one should understand that the soul is within the body and is transmigrating from one body to another. This is the beginning of spiritual knowledge. Any
 person who is not expert in understanding this science or is unwilling to understand it remains in the bodily conception of life, or the animalistic conception of life, as confirmed in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yasy\'e4tma-buddhi\'f9 ku\'ebape tri-dh\'e4tuke.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 .. sa eva go-khara\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
). Every member of human society should clearly understand the instructions of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 for only in this way can one be spiritually elevated and automatically give up the false, illusory knowledge by which one thinks, "I am this body, and everything belonging to this body is mine [}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 aha\'e0 mameti}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ]." This doggish conception should be rejected immediately. One should be prepared to understand the spirit soul and the supreme spirit, God, who are eternally related. Thus one may return home, back to Godhea
d, having solved all the problems of life.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.22
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11368625 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT 22
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s3004\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid8789409 \b\v\f75\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 A\'edaE Pa[k*-TaYa" Pa[ae}{\cs3017\insrsid30033\charrsid5006070 \'a2}{
\cs3015\insrsid30033\charrsid5006070 -a\'f1Ya Wv ih Tad(Gau<aa" )\line ivk-ara" zae@XaacaYa\'8c" PauMaaNaek-" SaMaNvYaaTa( )) 22 ))}{\insrsid30033 
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 a\'f1\'f6au prak\'e5taya\'f9 prokt\'e4s
\par traya eva hi tad-gu\'eb\'e4\'f9
\par vik\'e4r\'e4\'f9 \'f1o\'f2a\'e7\'e4c\'e4ryai\'f9
\par pum\'e4n eka\'f9 samanvay\'e4t
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 a\'f1\'f6au}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash eight; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 prak\'e5taya\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash material energies; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 prokt\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash it is said; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
traya\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash three; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 eva}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash certainly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hi}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash 
indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tat-gu\'eb\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the modes of material energy; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vik\'e4r\'e4\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash transformations; 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'f1o\'f2a\'e7a}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash sixteen; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4c\'e4ryai\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash by the authorities; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pum\'e4n}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash the living entity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 eka\'f9}{\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash one; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 samanvay\'e4t}{
\cs2996\fs28\insrsid30033\charrsid11368625 \emdash from conjunction.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
The Lord's eight separated material energies, the three modes of material nature and the sixteen transformations [the eleven senses and the five gross material elements like earth and water]\emdash within all the
se, the one spiritual soul exists as the observer. Therefore all the great \'e4c\'e4ryas have concluded that the individual soul is conditioned by these material elements.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 As explained in the previous verse, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
k\'f1etre\'f1u dehe\'f1u tath\'e4tma-yogair adhy\'e4tma-vid brahma-gati\'e0 labheta:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 "A spiritually advanced person can understand how the spiritual particle exists within the body, and thus by cultivating spiritual knowledge he can attain perfection in spiritual life." The intelligent person who is expert in finding t
he self within the body must understand the eight external energies, which are listed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (7.4):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bh\'fcmir \'e4po 'nalo v\'e4yu\'f9\line kha\'e0 mano buddhir eva ca\line aha\'eck\'e4ra it
\'e9ya\'e0 me\line bhinn\'e4 prak\'e5tir a\'f1\'f6adh\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intelligence and false ego\emdash 
all together these eight comprise My separated material energies." }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bh\'fcmi,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  earth, includes all the objects of sense perception\emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 r\'fcpa}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (form), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 rasa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (taste), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 gandha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (smell), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7abda}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (sound) and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 spar\'e7a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (touch). Within the earth are the fragrance of roses, the taste of sweet fruit, and whatever else we want. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4
gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (1.10.4), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-k\'e4ma-dugh\'e4 mah\'e9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the earth (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mah\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
) contains all our requirements. Thus the objects of sense perception are all present in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bh\'fcmi,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or the earth. The gross material elements and subtle material elements (mind, intelligence and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 aha\'eck\'e4ra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  false ego) constitute the total material energy.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
Within the total material energy are the three material modes or qualities. These qualities\emdash }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba}{
\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 \emdash 
belong not to the soul but to the material energy. It is because of the interaction of these three material modes of nature that the five knowledge-gathering senses, the five working senses and their controller, the mind, are manifested. Then, according 
to these modes, the living entity gets the opportunity to perform different types of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 karma}{\insrsid30033  with different types of knowledge, thinking, feeling and willing. Thus the bodily machine begins to work.
\par This has all been properly analyzed in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 s\'e4\'eckhya-yoga}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  by the great }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4c\'e4ryas,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  especially by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, in His incarnation as Devah\'fcti-putra Kapila. This is indicated here by the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4c\'e4ryai\'f9.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  We need not follow anyone who is not an authorized }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4
c\'e4rya.}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c4c\'e4ryav\'e4n puru\'f1o veda:}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  one can understand the truth fully when he has taken shelter of an expert }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e4c\'e4rya.
\par }{\insrsid30033 The living entity is individual, but the body is a composition of many material elements. This is proved by the fact that as soon as the living entity quits this combination of material 
elements, it becomes a mere conglomeration of matter. The matter is qualitatively one, and the spiritual soul is qualitatively one with the Supreme. The Supreme is one, and the individual soul is one, but the individual soul is understood to be the master
 
of the individual combination of material energy, whereas the Supreme Lord is the controller of the total material energy. The living entity is the master of his particular body, and according to his activities he is subjected to different types of pains 
and pleasures. However, although the Supreme Person, the Param\'e4tm\'e4, is also one, He is present as an individual in all the different bodies.
\par The material energy is in fact divided into twenty-four elements. The individual soul, the owner of the individual body, is a twenty-fifth subject, and above everything is Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu as Param\'e4tm\'e4
, the supreme controller, who is the twenty-sixth subject. When one understands all of these twenty-six subjects, he becomes }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 adhy\'e4tma-vit,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  an expert in understanding the distinc
tion between matter and spirit. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (13.3), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1etra-k\'f1etraj\'efayor j\'ef\'e4nam:}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  understanding of the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1etra}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (the constitution of the body) and of the individual soul and the Supersoul constitutes real }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na,}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 or knowledge. Unless one ultimately understands that the Supreme Lord is eternally related with the individual soul, one's knowledge is imperfect. This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (7.19):

\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 janman\'e4m ante\line j\'ef\'e4nav\'e4n m\'e4\'e0 prapadyate\line v\'e4
sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti\line sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9
