of the living entity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 svapna\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash a dream; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash like; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 arpyate}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash is placed.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
Through polluted intelligence one is subjected to the modes of nature, and thus one is conditioned by material existence. Like a dreami
ng state in which one falsely suffers, material existence, which is due to ignorance, must be considered unwanted and temporary.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
The unwanted condition of temporary life is called ignorance. One can very easily understand that the material body is 
temporary, for it is generated at a certain date and ends at a certain date, after undergoing the six kinds of change, namely birth, death, growth, maintenance, transformation and dwindling. This condition of the eternal soul is due to his ignorance, and 
although it is temporary, it is unwanted. Because of ignorance one is put into temporary bodies one after another. The spirit soul, however, does not need to enter such temporary bodies. He does so only due to his ignorance or his forgetfulness of K\'e5
\'f1\'eba. Therefore in the human form of life, when one's intelligence is developed, one should change his consciousness by trying to understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Then one can be liberated. This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (4.9), where the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
 punar janma\line naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"One who knows the transcendental nature of My appearance and activities does not, upon leaving the body, take his birth again in this material world, but attains My eternal abode, O Arjuna." Unless one understands K\'e5\'f1\'eba and comes to K\'e5\'f1
\'eba consciousness, one must continue in material bondage. To end this conditional life, one must surrender to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Indeed, that is demanded by the Supreme Lord. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Sarva-dharm\'e4
n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11471083 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 As advised by Mah\'e4r\'e4ja \'c5\'f1abhadeva, }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 na s\'e4dhu manye yata \'e4tmano 'yam asann api kle\'e7ada \'e4sa deha\'f9.}{\cs3007\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 One must be intelligent enough to understand that although one's body is temporary and will not endure for long, as long a
s one has a body he must undergo the pangs of material existence. Therefore, if by good association, by the instructions of a bona fide spiritual master, one takes to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, his conditional life of material existence is vanquished, and his original consciousness, known as K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, is revived. When one is K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious, he can realize that material existence, whether one is awake or dreaming, is nothing but a dream and has no factual value. This realization is possible by the grac
e of the Supreme Lord. This grace is also present in the form of the instructions of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\insrsid30033  Therefore \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu's mission is for everyone to engage in welfare activities to awaken the foolish living entity, especially in human society, so that he may come to the platform of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness and benefit by liberation from conditional life.
\par In this connection, \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya cites the following verses:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 du\'f9kha-r\'fcpo 'pi sa\'e0s\'e4ro\line buddhi-p\'fcrvam av\'e4pyate\line yath\'e4 svapne 
\'e7ira\'e7 cheda\'e0\line svaya\'e0 k\'e5tv\'e4tmano va\'e7a\'f9
\par tato du\'f9kham av\'e4pyeta\line tath\'e4 j\'e4garito 'pi tu\line j\'e4nann apy \'e4tmano du\'f9kham\line ava\'e7as tu pravartate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
One must realize that the material condition of life is full of distresses. One can realize this with purified intelligence. When one's intelligence
 is purified, he can understand that unwanted, temporary, material life is just like a dream. Just as one suffers pain when his head is cut off in a dream, in ignorance one suffers not only while dreaming but also while awake. Without the mercy of the Sup
reme Personality of Godhead, one continues in ignorance and is thus subjected to material distresses in various ways.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.28
