burning of the seed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yoga\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the process by which one can be linked with the Supreme; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 prav\'e4ha}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
of the continuous current in the form of wakefulness, dreaming and deep sleep; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 uparama\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the cessation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dhiya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of the intelligence.

\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
Therefore, my dear friends, O sons of the demons, your duty is to take to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, which can burn the seed of fruitive activities artificially created by the modes of material nature and stop the flow of the intelligence in wakefulne
ss, dreaming and deep sleep. In other words, when one takes to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, his ignorance is immediately dissipated.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (14.26):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4\'e0 ca yo 'vyabhic\'e4re\'eba\line bhakti-yogena sevate\line sa gu\'eb\'e4n samat\'e9
tyait\'e4n\line brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"One who engages in full devotional service, who does not fall down in any circumstance, at once transcends the modes of material nature and thus comes to the level of Brahman." By the practice of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  one immediately comes to the spiri
tual platform, transcendental to the actions and reactions of the three modes of material nature. The root of ignorance is material consciousness, which must be killed by spiritual consciousness, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. The word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 b\'e9ja-nirhara\'ebam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to burning the root cause of material life to ashes. In the Medin\'e9 dictionary, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 is explained by its result: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoge 'p\'fcrv\'e4rtha-sampr\'e4ptau sa\'ecgati-dhy\'e4na-yukti\'f1u.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  When one is put into an awkward position because of ignorance, the process by which one can be fr
eed from this entanglement is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  This is also called liberation. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Muktir hitv\'e4nyath\'e4-r\'fcpa\'e0 svar\'fcpe\'eba vyavasthiti\'f9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means giving up one's position in ignorance or illusion, by which one thinks in a way contrary to his constitutional position.
 Returning to one's constitutional position is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mukti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and the process by which one does this is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Thus }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is above }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma, j\'ef\'e4na}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4\'eckhya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Indeed, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is the ultimate goal of life. K\'e5\'f1\'eba therefore advised Arjuna to become a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tasm\'e4
d yog\'e9 bhav\'e4rjuna}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba further advised in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  that the first-class }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is he who has come to the platform of devotional service.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yogin\'e4m api sarve\'f1\'e4\'e0\line mad-gaten\'e4ntar\'e4tman\'e4\line \'e7raddh\'e4v\'e4
n bhajate yo m\'e4\'e0\line sa me yuktatamo mata\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Of all }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  h
e who always abides in Me with great faith, worshiping Me in transcendental loving service, is most intimately united with Me in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 and is the highest of all." (Bg. 6.47) Thus one who always thinks of K\'e5\'f1\'eba within the core of his heart is the best }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  By practicing this best of all }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  systems, one is liberated from the material condition.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.29
