In the previous verse it has been said that the process which immediately increases
 one's love and affection for the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the best of the many thousands of ways to become free from the entanglement of material existence. It is also said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharmasya tattva\'e0 nihita\'e0 guh
\'e4y\'e4m:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  actually the truth of religious principles is extremely confidential. Nonetheless, it can be understood very easily if one actually adopts the principles of religion. As it is said, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dharma\'e0 tu s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d bhagavat-pra\'eb\'e9tam:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 the process of religion is enunciated by the Supreme Lord because He is th
e supreme authority. This is also indicated in the previous verse by the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhagavatodita\'f9.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 The injunctions or directions of the Lord are infallible, and their benefits are fully assured. According to His directions, which are explained in this verse, the perfect form of religion is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 To practice }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga,}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  one must first accept a bona fide spiritual master. \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9, in his }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5ta-sindhu}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 (1.2.74-75), advises:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-p\'e4d\'e4\'e7rayas tasm\'e4t\line k\'e5\'f1\'eba-d\'e9k\'f1\'e4di-\'e7ik\'f1a\'ebam
\line vi\'e7rambhe\'eba guro\'f9 sev\'e4\line s\'e4dhu-vartm\'e4nuvartanam
\par sad-dharma-p\'e5cch\'e4 bhog\'e4di-\line ty\'e4ga\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'ebasya hetave
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
One's first duty is to accept a bona fide spiritual master. The student or disciple should be very inquisitive; he should be eager to know the complete truth about eternal religion (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 san\'e4tana-dharma}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). The words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-\'e7u\'e7r\'fc\'f1ay\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 mean that one should personally serve the spiritual master by giving him bodily comforts, helping him in bathing, dressing, sleeping, eating and so on. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-\'e7u\'e7r\'fc\'f1a\'ebam.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  A disciple should serve the spiritual master as a menial servant, and whatever he has in his possession should be dedicated to the spiritual master. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Pr\'e4\'ebair arthair dhiy\'e4 v\'e4c\'e4.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Everyone has his life, his wealth, his intelligence and his words, and all of them should be offered to 
the Supreme Personality of Godhead through the via medium of the spiritual master. Everything should be offered to the spiritual master as a matter of duty, but the offering should be made to the spiritual master with heart and soul, not artificially to g
ain material prestige. This offering is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 arpa\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Moreover, one should live among devotees, saintly persons, to learn the etiquette and proper behavior of devotional service. \'c7r\'e9
la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura remarks in this connection that whatever 
is offered to the spiritual master should be offered with love and affection, not for material adoration. Similarly, it is recommended that one associate with devotees, but there must be some discrimination. Actually, a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s
\'e4dhu,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  a saintly person, must be saintly in his behavior (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4dhava\'f9 sad-\'e4c\'e4r\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Unless one adheres to the standard behavior, one's position as a }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4dhu,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  a saintly person, is not complete. Therefore a Vai\'f1\'ebava, a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4dhu,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  must completely adhere to the standard of behavior. 
\'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura says that a Vai\'f1\'ebava, a person initiated into the Vai\'f1\'ebava cult, should be offered the respect befitting a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava, which means that he should be offered service and prayers. However, one should not associate with him if he is not a fit person with whom to associate.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.32
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 32
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid8789409 \b\v\f75\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 hir" SaveRzu >aUTaezu >aGavaNaaSTa wR\'ecr" )\line 
wiTa >aUTaaiNa MaNaSaa k-aMaESTaE" SaaDau MaaNaYaeTa( )) 32 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 hari\'f9 sarve\'f1u bh\'fcte\'f1u
\par bhagav\'e4n \'e4sta \'e9\'e7vara\'f9
\par iti bh\'fct\'e4ni manas\'e4
\par k\'e4mais tai\'f9 s\'e4dhu m\'e4nayet
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hari\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sarve\'f1u}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in all; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bh\'fcte\'f1u}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash living entities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhagav\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
the supreme personality; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4ste}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash is situated; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the supreme controller; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iti}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash thus; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bh\'fct\'e4ni}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash all living entities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 manas\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by such understanding; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e4mai
\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by desires; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash those; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 s\'e4dhu m\'e4nayet}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash one should highly esteem.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
One should always remember the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His localized representation as the Param\'e4tm\'e4, who is situated in the core of every living entity's heart. Thus one should offer r
espect to every living entity according to that living entity's position or manifestation.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Hari\'f9 sarve\'f1u bh\'fcte\'f1u.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 This statement is sometimes misunderstood by unscrupulous persons who wrongly conclude that because Hari, the Supreme Personality of G
odhead, is situated in every living entity, every living entity is therefore Hari. Such foolish persons do not distinguish between the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and the Param\'e4tm\'e4
, who are situated in every body. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  is the living entity, and the Param\'e4tm\'e4 is the Supreme P
ersonality of Godhead. The individual living entity, however, is different from the Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supreme Lord. Therefore }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 hari\'f9 sarve\'f1u bh\'fcte\'f1u}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 means that Hari is situated as Param\'e4tm\'e4, not as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  although }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 is a part of Param\'e4tm\'e4. Offering respect to every living entity means offering respect to the Param\'e4tm\'e4 situated in every living entity. One should not misunderstand every living entity to be the Param\'e4tm\'e4
. Sometimes unscrupulous persons designate a living entity as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, sv\'e4m\'e9-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  this N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba or that N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a. One should clearly understand that although N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba is situated in the core of the heart of every living entity, the living entity never becomes N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.33
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 33
