By these activities [as mentioned above] one is able to cut down the influence of the enemies, namely lust, anger, greed, illusion, madness and jealousy, and when thus situated, one can render service to the Lord. In this way one surely attains the pla
tform of loving service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
As mentioned in verses thirty and thirty-one, one's first duty is to approach the spiritual master, the representative of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, to begin rendering service to him. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja proposed that from the very beginning of life (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kaum\'e4ra \'e4caret pr\'e4j\'efa\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ) a small child should be trained to serve the spiritual master while living at the }
{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-kula.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Brahmac\'e4r\'e9 guru-kule vasan d\'e4nto guror hitam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  }{
\cs3010\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5139582\charrsid5139582 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  7.12.1). This is the beginning of spiritual life. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Guru-p\'e4d\'e4\'e7raya\'f9, s\'e4dhu-vartm\'e4
nuvartanam, sad-dharma-p\'e5cch\'e4.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  By following the instructions of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
\'e7\'e4stras,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  the disciple attains the stage of devotional service and becomes unattached to possessions. Whatever he possesses he offers to the spiritual master, the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
guru,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  who engages him in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid8330074 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 .}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 The disciple follows strictly and in this way learns how to control his senses. Then, by using his pure intelligence, he gradually becomes a lover of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as confirmed by \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4dau \'e7raddh\'e4 tata\'f9 s\'e4dhu-sa\'ecga\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ). In this way one's life becomes perfect, and his attachment for K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a becomes positively manifested. In that stage, he is situated in ecstasy, experiencing }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bh\'e4va}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 anubh\'e4va,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  as explained in the following verse.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.34
