\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
  When the mind is in touch with the impersonal Brahman one becomes satisfied, but one must advance further to render service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, for one's remaining merged in the Brahman effulgence is not always as
sured.  As it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4ruhya k\'e5cchre\'eba para\'e0 pada\'e0 tata\'f9 patanty adho 'n\'e4d\'e5ta-yu\'f1mad-a\'ecghraya\'f9:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
one may merge in the Brahman feature of the Absolute Truth, but there is a chance that one may fall because of not being acquainted with Adhok\'f1aja, or V\'e4sudeva.  Of course, such }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahma-sukha}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  undoubtedly eliminates material happiness, but when one advances through impersonal Brahman and localized Param\'e4tm\'e4
 to approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead in relationship with Him as a servant, friend, parent or conj
ugal lover, one's happiness becomes all-pervading.  Then one automatically feels transcendental bliss, just as one becomes happy seeing the shining of the moon.  One acquires natural happiness upon seeing the moon, but when one can see the Supreme Persona
lity of Godhead, one's transcendental happiness increases hundreds and thousands of times.  As soon as one is very intimately connected with the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one surely becomes free from all material contamination.  }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Y\'e4 nirv\'e5tis tanu-bh\'e5t\'e4m.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756   This cessation of all material happiness is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nirv\'e5ti}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nirv\'e4\'eba.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756   \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5ta-sindhu}
{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (1.1.38):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahm\'e4nan}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid16269355 do bhaved e\'f1a\line cet par\'e4rdha-gu\'eb\'e9}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e5ta\'f9\line naiti bhakti-sukh\'e4mbhodhe\'f9\line param\'e4\'ebu-tul\'e4m api
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "If }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahm\'e4nanda,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the bliss o
f merging in the Brahman effulgence, were multiplied one hundred trillion times, it would still not equal even an atomic fragment of the ocean of transcendental bliss felt in devotional service."
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4\line na \'e7ocati na k\'e4\'eck\'f1ati\line sama\'f9
 sarve\'f1u bh\'fcte\'f1u\line mad-bhakti\'e0 labhate par\'e4m
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"One who is transcendentally situated at once realizes the Supreme Brahman and becomes fully joyful. He never laments nor desires to have anything; he is equally disposed toward all living entities. In that state he atta
ins pure devotional service unto the Lord." (Bg. 18.54) If one advances further from the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahma-nirv\'e4\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  platform, one enters the stage of devotional service (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mad-bhakti\'e0 labhate par\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 adhok\'f1aj\'e4lambham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to keeping the mind always engaged in
 the Absolute Truth, who is beyond the mind and material speculation. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Sa vai mana\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pad\'e4ravindayo\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 This is the result of Deity worship. By constantly engaging in the service of the Lord and thinking of His lotus feet, one is automatically freed from all material contamination. Thus the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahma-nirv\'e4\'eba-sukham
}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  indicates that when one is in touch with the Absolute Truth, material sense gratification is completely nullified.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.38
