\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 r\'e4ya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash wealth; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kalatram}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash one's wife and feminine friends; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pa\'e7ava\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash domestic animals like cows, horses, asses, cats and dogs; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 suta-\'e4daya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash children and so on; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 g\'e5h\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash big buildings and residences; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mah\'e9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash land; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ku\'efjara}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash elephants; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ko\'e7a}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash treasury house; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bh\'fctaya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
and other luxuries for sense gratification and material enjoyment; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sarve}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash all; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 artha}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash economic development; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k
\'e4m\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash and sense gratification; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'f1a\'eba-bha\'ecgura}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash perishable in a moment; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4yu\'f1a\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
of one whose duration of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kurvanti}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash effect or bring; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 martyasya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of one who is destined to die; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kiyat}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash how much; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 priyam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash pleasure; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 cal\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash flickering and temporary.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s2998\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16347101 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
One's riches, beautiful wife and female friends, one's sons and daughters, one's residence, one's domestic animals like cows, elephants and horses, one's treasury, economic development and sense gratification\emdash inde
ed, even the lifetime in which one can enjoy all these material opulences\emdash 
are certainly temporary and flickering. Since the opportunity of human life is temporary, what benefit can these material opulences give to a sensible man who has understood himself to be eternal?
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
This verse describes how the advocates of economic development are frustrated by the laws of nature. As the previous verse asks, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ki\'e0 vi\'f1ayopap\'e4danai\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 what is the actual benefit of so-called economic development? The history of the w
orld has factually proved that attempts to increase economic development for bodily comfort through the advancement of material civilization have done nothing to remedy the inevitability of birth, death, old age and disease. Everyone has knowledge of huge
 empires throughout the history of the world\emdash the Roman Empire, the Moghul Empire, the British Empire and so on\emdash but all the societies engaged in such economic development (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarve 'rtha-k\'e4m\'e4\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 ) have been frustrated by the laws of nature through periodic wars, pestilence, famine and so on. Thus all their attempts have been flickering and temporary. In this verse, therefore, it is said, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kurvanti martyasya kiyat priya\'e0 cal\'e4\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  one may be very proud of possessing a vast empire, but such empires are impermanent; after
 one hundred or two hundred years, everything is finished. All such positions of economic development, although created with great endeavor and hardship, are vanquished very soon. Therefore they have been described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 cal
\'e4\'f9.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  An intelligent man should conclude that material economic development is not at all pleasing. The entire world is described in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 du\'f9kh\'e4layam a\'e7\'e4\'e7vatam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 \emdash 
miserable and temporary. Economic development may be pleasing for some time, but it cannot endure. Thus many big business
men are now very morose because they are being harassed by various plundering governments. In conclusion, why should one waste his time for so-called economic development, which is neither permanent nor pleasing to the soul?
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 On the other hand, our relationship with K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is eternal. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Nitya-siddha k\'e5\'f1\'eba-prema.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  The pure souls are eternally in love with K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, and this permanent love, either as a servant, a friend, a parent or a conjugal lover, is not at all difficult to revive. Especially in this age, the concession is that simply by chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mantra}
{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 harer n\'e4ma harer n\'e4ma harer n\'e4maiva kevalam}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
) one revives his original relationship with God and thus becomes so happy that he does not want anything material. As enunciated by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 na dhana\'e0 na jana\'e0 na sundar\'e9\'e0 kavit\'e4
\'e0 v\'e4 jagad-\'e9\'e7a k\'e4maye.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  A very advanced devotee in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness does not want riches, followers or possessions. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 R\'e4ya\'f9 kalatra\'e0 pa\'e7
ava\'f9 sut\'e4dayo g\'e5h\'e4 mah\'e9 ku\'efjara-ko\'e7a-bh\'fctaya\'f9.}{\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083 
 The satisfaction of possessing material opulences, although perhaps of a different standard, is available even in the lives of dogs and hogs, who cannot revive their eternal relationship with K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. In human life, however, our eternal, dormant relationship with K\'e5\'f1\'eba is possible to revive. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja has described this life as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 arthadam.}{
\cs3007\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid11471083  Consequently, instead of wasting our time for economic development, which cannot give us any happiness, if we simply try to revive our eternal relationship with K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, we will properly utilize our lives.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.40
