\'e7\'fcdr\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the laborer class; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vraja-okasa\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash village cowherd men; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 khag\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash birds; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e5g\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash animals; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 p\'e4pa-j\'e9v\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash sinful living entities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 santi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
can become; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash certainly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 acyutat\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the qualities of Acyuta, the Supreme Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gat\'e4\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash obtained.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 O my friends, O sons of demons, everyone, including you (the Yak\'f1as and R\'e4k\'f1
asas), the unintelligent women, \'e7\'fcdras and cowherd men, the birds, the lower animals and the sinful living entities, can revive his original, eternal spiritual life and exist forever simply by accepting the principles of bhakti-yoga.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 The devotees are referred to as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
acyuta-gotra,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  or the dynasty of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The Lord is called Acyuta, as indicated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 senayor ubhayor m}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10971549 adhye ratha\'e0 sth\'e4paya me 'cyuta}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
). The Lord is infallible in the material world because He is the supreme spiritual person. Similarly, the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'e9vas,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 who are part and parcel of the Lord, can also become infallible. Although Prahl\'e4da's mother was in the conditional state and was the wife of a demon, even Yak\'f1as, R\'e4k\'f1asas, women, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdras}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  and even birds and other lower living entities can be elevated to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acyuta-gotra,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 
 the family of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. That is the highest perfection. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba never falls, when we revive our spiritual consciousness, K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, we never fall again to material existen
ce. One should understand the position of the supreme Acyuta, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756  (4.9):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
 punar janma\line naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "One who knows the transcendental nature of My appearan
ce and activities does not, upon leaving the body, take his birth again in this material world, but attains My eternal abode, O Arjuna." One should understand Acyuta, the supreme infallible, and how we are related with Him, and one should take to the serv
ice of the Lord. This is the perfection of life. \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acyutat\'e4\'e0 cyuti-varjanam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acyutat\'e4m}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to one who never falls to this material world but always remains in the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha world, fully engaged in the service of the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.7.55
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 55
