mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (1.1.10), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mand\'e4\'f9 sumanda-matayo manda-bh\'e4gy\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja is the guide of all the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mandas,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or bad living entities who are under the influence of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  He is the benefactor even of the slow and bad living entities in this material world. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Kula-bheda-kar\'e4dhama:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  by his actions, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja made great personalities who established big, big families seem insignificant. Everyone is interested in his own family and in making his dynasty famous, but Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was so liberal that he made no d
istinction between one living entity and another. Therefore he was greater than the great }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 praj\'e4patis}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  who established their dynasties. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 stabdham}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means obstinate. A devotee does not care for the instructions of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asuras.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  When they give instructions, he remains silent. A devotee cares about the instructions of K\'e5
\'f1\'eba, not those of demons or nondevotees. He does not give any respect to a demon, even though the demon be his father. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Mac-ch\'e4sanodv\'e5ttam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was disobedient to the orders of his demoniac father. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yama-k\'f1ayam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  every conditioned soul is under the control of Yamar\'e4ja, but Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu said that he considered Prahl\'e4da Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja his deliverer, for Prahl\'e4da would stop Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu's repetition of birth and death. Because Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, being a great devotee, was better than any }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was to be brought among the society of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yog\'e9s.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Thus \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kura has explained these words in a very interesting way as they can be interpreted from the side of Sarasvat\'e9, the mother of learning.
