\'e4\'e0 prakop\'e4ya na \'e7\'e4ntaye.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  If good instructions are given to a foolish person, he does not take advantage of them, but becomes more and more angry. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's authorized instructions to his father were not accepted by Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu as truth; instead Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu became increasingly angry at his great son, who was a pure devotee. This kind of difficulty always exists when a devotee preaches K
\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness to persons like Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, who are interested in money and women. (The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 hira\'ebya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means "gold," and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ka\'e7ipu}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to cushions or good bedding.) Moreover, a father does not like to be instructed by his son, especially if the father is a demon. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's Vai\'f1\'eb
ava preaching to his demoniac father was indirectly effective, for because of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu's excessive jealousy of K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His devotee, he was inviting }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 to kill him very quickly. Thus he was expediting his being killed by the Lord Himself. Although Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was a demon, he is described here by the added word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7r\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Why? The answer is that fortunately he had such a great devotee son as Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. Thus although he was a demon, he would attain salvation and return home, back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033\charrsid11610905 SB 7.8.12
