f God because they cannot see Him. But what the demon does not know is stated by the Lord Himself in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (7.25): }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e4ha\'e0 prak\'e4\'e7a\'f9
 sarvasya yogam\'e4y\'e4-sam\'e4v\'e5ta\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  "I am never manifest to the foolish and unintelligent. For them I am covered by }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yogam\'e4y\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
" The Lord is open to being seen by devotees, but nondevotees cannot see Him. The qualification for seeing God is stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (5.38): }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prem\'e4
\'efjana-cchurita-bhakti-vilocanena santa\'f9 sadaiva h\'e5daye\'f1u vilokayanti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  A devotee who has developed a genuine love for K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a can always see Him everywhere, whereas a demon, not having a clear understanding of the Supreme Lord, cannot see Him. When Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was threatening to kill Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Prahl\'e4
da certainly saw the column standing before him and his father, and he saw that the Lord was present in the pillar to encourage him not to fear his demoniac father's words. The Lord was present to protect him. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu marked Prahl\'e4
da's observation and asked him, "Where is your God?" Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja replied, "He is everywhere." Then Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu asked, "Why is He not in this pillar before me?" Thus in all circumstances the devotee can always see the Supreme Lord, whereas the nondevotee cannot.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja has here been addressed by his father 
as "the most unfortunate." Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu thought himself extremely fortunate because he possessed the property of the universe. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, his legitimate son, was to have inherited this vast property, but because of his impudence, he was going to die at his father's hands. Therefore the demoniac father considered Prahl\'e4da the most unfortunate because Prahl\'e4
da would not be able to inherit his property. Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu did not know that Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was the most fortunate person within the three worlds because Prahl\'e4
da was protected by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Such are the misunderstandings of demons. They do not know that a devotee is protected by the Lord in all circumstances (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kaunteya pratij\'e4n\'e9hi na me bhakta\'f9
 pra\'eba\'e7yati}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.8.13
