 The end of the millennium is the time for Your anger. Now that this insignificant demon Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu has been killed, O my Lord, who are naturally affectionate to Your devotee, kindly protect his son Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who is 
standing nearby as Your fully surrendered devotee.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the creator of the material world. There are three processes in creation-namely creation, maintenance and finally annihilation. During the period of annihilati
on, at the end of each millennium, the Lord becomes angry, and the part of anger is played by Lord \'c7iva, who is therefore called Rudra. When the Lord appeared in great anger to kill Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu, everyone was extremely afraid of the Lord's attitude, but Lord \'c7iva, knowing very well that the Lord's anger is also His }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 l\'e9l\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  was not afraid. Lord \'c7
iva knew that he would have to play the part of anger for the Lord. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 K\'e4la}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means Lord \'c7iva (Bhairava), and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kopa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 refers to the Lord's anger. These words, combined together as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kopa-k\'e4la,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 refer to the end of each millennium. Actually the Lord is always affectionate toward His devotees, even though He may appear very angry. Because He is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 avyay\'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid8541047 \emdash }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 because He never falls down\emdash even when angry the Lord is affectionate toward His devotees. Therefore Lord \'c7iva reminded the Lord to act like an affectionate father toward Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, who was standing by the Lord's side as an exalted, fully surrendered devotee.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.8.42
