for those who are always engaged in the service; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mukti\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash liberation from material bondage; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te
\'f1\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of them (the pure devotees); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bahumat\'e4}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash thought very important; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 n\'e4ra-si\'e0ha}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O Lord }{\fs28\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 , half lion and half human being; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 aparai\'f9 kim}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash then what is the use of other possessions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid30033 King Indra said:}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
 O Supreme Lord, You are our deliverer and protector. Our shares of sacrifices, which are actually Yours, have been recovered from the demon by You. Because the demoniac king Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu was most fearsome, our hearts, which are Your permanent abode, were all overtaken by him. Now, by Your presence, the gloom and darkness in our h
earts have been dissipated. O Lord, for those who always engage in Your service, which is more exalted than liberation, all material opulence is insignificant. They do not even care for liberation, not to speak of the benefits of k\'e4
ma, artha and dharma.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 In this material world there are two kinds of people\emdash the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 devat\'e4s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (demigods) and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asuras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (demons). Although the demigods are attached to material enjoyment, they are devotees of the Lord who act according to the rules and regulations of the Vedic injunctions. During the reign of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu, everyone was disturbed in the routine duties of Vedic civilization. When Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was killed, all the demigods, who had always been disturbed by Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, felt relief in their general way of life.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Be
cause the government in Kali-yuga is full of demons, the living conditions of devotees are always disturbed. Devotees cannot perform }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 and thus they cannot partake of the remnants of food offered in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  for the worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. The hearts of t
he demigods are always filled with fear of the demons, and therefore they cannot think of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The engagement of the demigods is to think of the Lord always within the cores of their hearts. The Lord says in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (6.47):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yogin\'e4m api sarve\'f1\'e4\'e0\line mad gaten\'e4ntar\'e4tman\'e4\line \'e7raddh\'e4v\'e4
n bhajate yo m\'e4\'e0\line sa me yuktatamo mata\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "And of all }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 he who always abides in Me with great faith, worshiping Me in transcendental loving service, is most intimately united with Me in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and is 
the highest of all." The demigods fully absorb themselves in meditation upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead to become perfect }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 but because of the presence of demons, their hearts are filled with the activities of the demons. Thus their hearts, which are meant to be the abode of the Supreme Lord, are practically occupied by the demons. All the demigods felt relieved when Hira\'eb
yaka\'e7ipu was dead, for they could easily think of the Lord. They could then receive the results of sacrifices and become happy even though in the material world.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.8.43
