ipu's coming to this earth and acting as the Lord's enemy was prearranged. Jaya and Vijaya were cursed by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Sanaka, Sanat-kum\'e4ra, Sanandana and San\'e4
tana because Jaya and Vijaya checked these four Kum\'e4ras. The Lord accepted this cursing of His servants and agreed that they would have to go to the material world and would then return to Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha after serving the term of the curse. Jaya and Vijaya were
 very much perturbed, but the Lord advised them to act as enemies, for then they would return after three births; otherwise, ordinarily, they would have to take seven births. With this authority, Jaya and Vijaya acted as the Lord's enemies, and now that t
hese two were dead, all the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas understood that the Lord's killing of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was special mercy bestowed upon them.
\par }\pard\plain \s1178\ql \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Seventh Canto, Eighth Chapter, of the }{
\cs2344\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  entitled "Lord }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Slays the King of the Demons."
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf18\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9: Prahl\'e4da Pacifies Lord }{\insrsid3609589 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033  with Prayers
\par }\pard\plain \s330\qc \li0\ri0\sb540\sa540\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat10 \b\f35\fs36\cf8\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\insrsid8789409 CHAPTER NINE\line }{\insrsid30033 Prahl\'e4da Pacifies Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033  with Prayers
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12083645 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 As related in this chapter, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, following the order of Lord Brahm\'e4
, pacified the Lord when the Lord was extremely angry after having killed Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu.
\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid30033 After Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was killed, the Lord continued to be very angry, and the demigods, headed by Lord Brahm\'e4, could not pacify Him. Even mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the goddess of fortune, the constant companion of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, could not dare come before Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033 . Then Lord Brahm\'e4 asked Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja to go forward and pacify the Lord's anger. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, being confident of the affection of his master, Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033 , was not af
raid at all. He very gravely appeared before the Lord's lotus feet and offered Him respectful obeisances. Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033 , being very much affectionate toward Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, put His hand on Prahl\'e4
da's head, and because of being personally touched by the Lord, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja immediately achieved }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 brahma-j\'ef\'e4na,}{\insrsid30033 
 spiritual knowledge. Thus he offered his prayers to the Lord in full spiritual knowledge and full devotional ecstasy. The instructions given by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja in the form of his prayers are as follows.
\par Prahl\'e4da said, "I am not proud of being able to offer prayers to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. I simply take shelter of the mercy of the Lord, for without d}{\insrsid5920619 evotion one cannot appease Him.}{\insrsid30033 
 One cannot please the Supreme Personality of Godhea
d simply by dint of high parentage or great opulence, learning, austerity, penance or mystic power. Indeed, these are never pleasing to the Supreme Lord, for nothing can please Him but pure devotional service. Even if a nondevotee is a }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid30033  qualified w
ith the twelve brahminical symptoms, he cannot be very dear to the Lord, whereas if a person born in a family of dog-eaters is a devotee, the Lord can accept his prayers. The Lord does not need anyone's prayers, but if a devotee offers his prayers to the 
L
ord, the devotee benefits greatly. Ignorant persons born in low families, therefore, can sincerely offer heartfelt prayers to the Lord, and the Lord will accept them. As soon as one offers his prayers to the Lord, he is immediately situated on the Brahman
 platform.
\par Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033  appeared for the benefit of all human society, not only for Prahl\'e4da's personal benefit. The fierce form of Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033 
 may appear most awful to a nondevotee, but to the devotee the Lord is always affectionate as He is in ot
her forms. Conditioned life in the material world is actually extremely fearful; indeed, a devotee is not afraid of anything else. Fear of material existence is due to false ego. Therefore the ultimate goal of life for every living entity is to attain the
 position of being ser}{\insrsid5920619 vant of the servant of the Lord}{\insrsid30033 
. The miserable condition of the living entities in the material world can be remedied only by the mercy of the Lord. Although there are so-called material protectors like Lord Brahm\'e4 and the other demigo
ds, or even one's own father, they are unable to do anything if one is neglected by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. However, one who has fully taken shelter of the Lord's lotus feet can be saved from the onslaught of material nature. Therefore every l
i
ving entity should be unattracted by material so-called happiness and should take shelter of the Lord by all means. That is the mission of human life. To be attracted by sense gratification is simply foolish. Whether one is a devotee of the Lord or is a n
ondevotee does not depend upon one's birth in a high or low family. Even Lord Brahm\'e4
 and the goddess of fortune cannot achieve the full favor of the Lord, whereas a devotee can very easily attain such devotional service. The Lord's mercy is bestowed equally upon everyone, regardless of whether one is high or low. Because Prahl\'e4da Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja was blessed by N\'e4rada Muni, Prahl\'e4da became a great devotee. The Lord always saves the devotee from impersonalists and voidists. The Lord is present in everyone's heart as 
the Supersoul to give the living being protection and all benefits. Thus the Lord acts sometimes as the killer and sometimes as the protector. One should not accuse the Lord for any discrepancies. It is His plan that we see varieties of life within this m
aterial world. All of them are ultimately His mercy.
\par Although the entire cosmic manifestation is nondifferent, the material world is nonetheless different from the spiritual world. Only by the mercy of the Supreme Lord can one understand how the wonderful m
aterial nature acts. For example, although Lord Brahm\'e4 appeared from the lotus seat that had grown from the abdomen of Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'eb
u, he could not understand what to do after his appearance. He was attacked by two demons, Madhu and Kai\'f6abha, who took away Vedic knowledge, but the Lord killed them and entrusted to Lord Brahm\'e4
 the Vedic knowledge. Thus the Lord appears in every millennium in the societies of demigods, human beings, animals, saints and aquatics. All such incarnations are meant to protec
t the devotees and kill the demons, but this killing and protecting does not reflect any sense of partiality on the part of the Supreme Lord. The conditioned soul is always attracted by the external energy. Therefore he is subjected to lust and greed, and
 
he suffers under the conditions of material nature. The Lord's causeless mercy toward His devotee is the only means by which to get out of material existence. Anyone engaged in glorifying the Lord's activities is always unafraid of this material world, wh
ereas one who cannot glorify the Lord in that way is subjected to all lamentation.
\par Those interested in silently worshiping the Lord in solitary places may be eligible for liberation themselves, but a pure devotee is always aggrieved to see others suffering.
 Therefore, not caring for his own liberation, he always engages in preaching by glorifying the Lord. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, therefore, had tried to deliver his class friends by preaching and had never remained silent. Although being silent, observing austerit
ies and penances, learning the Vedic literature, undergoing ritualistic ceremonies, living in a solitary place and performing }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 japa}{\insrsid30033 
 and transcendental meditation are approved means of liberation, they are meant for nondevotees or for cheaters who want to li
ve at the expense of others. A pure devotee, however, being freed from all such deceptive activities, is able to see the Lord face to face.
\par The atomic theory of the composition of the cosmic manifestation is not factual. The Lord is the cause of everything
, and therefore He is the cause of this creation. One should therefore always engage in devotional service by offering respectful obeisances to the Lord, offering prayers, working for the Lord, worshiping the Lord in the temple, always remembering the Lor
d and always hearing about His transcendental activities. Without these six kinds of activity, one cannot attain to devotional service.
\par Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja thus offered his prayers to the Supreme Lord, begging His mercy at every step. Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033  was pacified by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's prayers and wanted to give him benedictions by which Prahl\'e4da could procure all kinds of material facilities. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, however, was not misled by material facilities. Rather, he wanted to remain always a ser}{\insrsid5920619 
vant of the servant of the Lord}{\insrsid30033 .
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.1
