\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 The Supreme Lord, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, i
s always fully satisfied in Himself. Therefore when something is offered to Him, the offering, by the Lord's mercy, is for the benefit of the devotee, for the Lord does not need service from anyone. To give an example, if one's face is decorated, the refl
ection of one's face in a mirror is also seen to be decorated.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 it is recommended that a devotee follow nine principles; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9 smara\'eba\'e0 p\'e4da-sevanam/ arcanam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vandana\'e0 d
\'e4sya\'e0 sakhyam \'e4tma-nivedanam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  This service of g
lorifying the Lord by hearing, chanting and so on is not, of course, meant for the benefit of the Lord; this devotional service is recommended for the benefit of the devotee. The Lord is always glorious, whether the devotee glorifies Him or not, but if th
e devotee engages in glorifying the Lord, the devotee himself automatically becomes glorious. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Ceto-darpa\'eba-m\'e4rjana\'e0 bhava-mah\'e4-d\'e4v\'e4gni-nirv\'e4pa\'ebam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 By glorifying the Lord constantly, the living entity becomes purified in the core of his heart, and thus he can understand that he does not belong to the material world but is a spirit soul whose actual activity is to advance in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness so that he may become free from the material clutches. Thus the blazing fire of material existence is immediately extinguished (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhava-mah\'e4-d\'e4v\'e4gni-nirv\'e4pa\'ebam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
). A foolish person is amazed that K\'e5\'f1\'eba orders, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "Abandon all varieties of religious activities and just surrender unto Me." Some foolish scholars even say that this i
s too much to demand. But this demand is not for the benefit of the Supreme Personality of Godhead; rather, it is for the benefit of human society. If human beings individually and collectively surrender everything to the Supreme Personality of Godhead in
 full K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, all of human society will benefit. One who does not dedicate everything to the Supreme Lord is described in this verse as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 avidu\'f1a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  a rascal. In }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (7.15), the Lord Himself speaks in the same way:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 na m\'e4\'e0 du\'f1k\'e5tino m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\'f9\line prapadyante nar\'e4dham\'e4\'f9\line m
\'e4yay\'e4pah\'e5ta-j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\line \'e4sura\'e0 bh\'e4vam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid8723402  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4\'e7rit\'e4\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"Those miscreants who are grossly foolish, lowest among mankind, whose knowledge is stolen by illusion, and who partake of the atheistic nature of demons, do not surrender unto Me." Because of ignorance and misfortune, the atheists and the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nar\'e4dhamas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the lowest of men, do not surrender unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore although the Supreme Lord, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is full in Himself, He appears in different }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yugas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  to demand the surrender of the conditioned souls so that they will benefit by becoming free from the material clutches. In conclusion, the more we engage in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness and render service unto the Lord, the more we benefit. K\'e5\'f1\'eba does not need service from any of us.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.12
