\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 My 
dear Lord, now I have complete experience concerning the worldly opulence, mystic power, longevity and other material pleasures enjoyed by all living entities, from Lord Brahm\'e4
 down to the ant. As powerful time, You destroy them all. Therefore, because of my experience, I do not wish to possess them. My dear Lord, I request You to place me in touch with Your pure devotee and let me serve him as a sincere servant.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 By studying }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  every intelligent man can get experience like that of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja through the historical incidents mentioned in this great literature of spiritual knowledge. By following in the footsteps of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, one should gain thorough experience that all material opulence is perishable at every moment. Even this body, for which we try to acquire so many sensual pleasures, may perish at any time. The soul, however, is eternal. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Na hanyate hanyam\'e4ne \'e7ar\'e9re:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the soul is never vanquished, even when the body is destroyed. An intelligent man, therefore, should ca
re for the happiness of the spirit soul, not of the body. Even if one receives a body with a long duration of life, like those of Lord Brahm\'e4
 and the other great demigods, it will also be destroyed, and therefore an intelligent man should be concerned with the imperishable spirit soul.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 To save oneself, one must take shelter of a pure devotee. Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4
kura therefore says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ch\'e4\'f2iy\'e4 vai\'f1\'ebava-sev\'e4 nist\'e4ra p\'e4yeche keb\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  If one wants to save himself from material nature's onslaughts, which arise because 
of the material body, one must become K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious and try to fully understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (4.9), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
janma karma ca me divyam eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  One should understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba in truth, and this one can do only by serving a pure devotee. Thus Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja prays that Lord }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  place him in touch with a pure devotee and servant instead of awarding him material opulence. Every intelligent man within this material world must follow Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Mah\'e4jano yena gata\'f9 sa panth\'e4\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja did not want to enjoy the estate left by his father; rather, he wanted to become a ser}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid14908864 
vant of the servant of the Lord}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 . The illusory human civilization that perpetually endeavors for happiness through material advancement is rejected by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and those who strictly follow in his footsteps.

\par There are different types of material opulence, known technically as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhukti, mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 siddhi.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhukti}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to being situated in a very good position, like a position with the demigods in the higher planetary systems, where one can enjoy material sense gratification to the greatest extent. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Mukti}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to being disgusted with material advancement and thus desiring to become one with the Supreme. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Siddhi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to executing a severe type
 of meditation, like that of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  to attain eight kinds of perfection (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 a\'ebim\'e4, laghim\'e4, mahim\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 etc.). All who desire some material advancement through }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhukti, mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 siddhi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 are punishable in due course of time, and they return to material activities. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja rejected them all; he simply wanted to engage as an apprentice under the guidance of a pure devotee.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.25
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 25
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
