the place for generating; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 nirvidyate}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash become satiated; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tu}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash but; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 jana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash people in general; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yat api}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash although; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iti}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash thus; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vidv\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash so-called learned philosophers, scientists and politicians; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e4ma-analam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the blazing fire of lusty desires; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 madhu-lavai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash with drops of honey (happiness); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7amayan}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash controlling; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dur\'e4pai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash very difficult to obtain.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
In this material world, every living entity desires some future happiness, which is exactly like a mirage in the desert. Where is water in the desert, or, in other words, where is happiness in this material world? As for this body, what is 
its value? It is merely a source of various diseases. The so-called philosophers, scientists and politicians know this very well, but nonetheless they aspire for temporary happiness. Happiness is very difficult to obtain, but because they are unable to co
ntrol their senses, they run after the so-called happiness of the material world and never come to the right conclusion.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
There is a song in the Bengali language which states, "I constructed this home for happiness, but unfortunately there was a fire
, and everything has now been burnt to ashes." This illustrates the nature of material happiness. Everyone knows it, but nonetheless one plans to hear or think something very pleasing. Unfortunately, all of one's plans are annihilated in due course of tim
e. There were many politicians who planned empires, supremacy and control of the world, but in due time all their plans and empires\emdash and even the politicians themselves\emdash were vanquished. Everyone should take lessons from Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja about how we are engaged in so-called temporary happiness through bodily exercises for sense enjoyment. All of us repeatedly make plans, which are all repeatedly frustrated. Therefore one should stop such planmaking.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 As one cannot stop a blazing fire by constantly pouring ghe
e upon it, one cannot satisfy oneself by increasing plans for sense enjoyment. The blazing fire is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhava-mah\'e4-d\'e4v\'e4gni,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the forest fire of material existence. This forest fire occurs automatically, without endeavor. We want to be happy in the material world
, but this will never be possible; we shall simply increase the blazing fire of desires. Our desires cannot be satisfied by illusory thoughts and plans; rather, we have to follow the instructions of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Then we shall be happy. Otherwise, in the name of happiness, we shall continue to suffer miserable conditions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.26
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 26
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
