\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash where; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 aham}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash I (am); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 raja\'f9-prabhava\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash being born in a body full of passion; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7a}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O my Lord; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tama\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the mode of ignorance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 adhike}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash surpassing in; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 asmin}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in this; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 j\'e4ta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash born; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sura-itara-kule}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in a family of atheists or demons (who are subordinate to the devotees); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kva}
{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash where; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tava}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash Your; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 anukamp\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash causeless mercy; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 brahma\'eba\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of Lord Brahm\'e4; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tu}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash but; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhavasya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of Lord \'c7iva; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash nor; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vai}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash even; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ram\'e4y
\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of the goddess of fortune; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yat}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash which; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 me}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of me; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 arpita\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash offered; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7irasi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash on the head; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 padma-kara\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash lotus hand; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pras\'e4da\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the symbol of mercy.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
O my Lord, O Supreme, because I was born in a family full of the hellish material qualities of passion and ignorance, what is my position? And what is to be said of Your causeless mercy, which was never offered even to Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7
iva or the goddess of fortune, Lak\'f1m\'e9? You never put Your lotus hand upon their heads, but You have put it upon mine.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was surprised at the causeless mercy of the Supreme Lord, the Personality of Godhead, for although Prahl\'e4da was born in a demoniac family and although the Lord had never before placed His lotus hand on the head of Brahm\'e4, \'c7
iva or the goddess of fortune, His constant companion, Lord }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  kindly placed His hand on the head of Prahl\'e4da. This is the meaning of 
causeless mercy. The causeless mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead may be bestowed upon anyone, regardless of his position in this material world. Everyone is eligible to worship the Supreme Lord, irrespective of his material position. This is con
firmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (14.26):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4\'e0 ca yo 'vyabhic\'e4re\'eba\line bhakti yogena sevate\line sa gu\'eb\'e4n samat\'e9
tyait\'e4n\line brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"One who engages in full devotional service, who does not fall down in any circumstance, at once transcends the modes of material nat
ure and thus comes to the level of Brahman." Anyone who engages in continuous devotional service to the Lord is situated in the spiritual world and has nothing to do with the material qualities (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu
\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tamo-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Because Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was situated on the spiritual platform, he had nothing to do with his body, which had been born of the modes of passion and ignorance. The symptoms of passion and ignorance are described in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (1.2.19) as lust and hankering (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tad\'e4 rajas tamo-bh\'e4v\'e4\'f9 k\'e4ma-lobh\'e4daya\'e7 ca ye}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, being a great devotee, thought the body born of his father to be born of passion and ignorance, but because Prahl\'e4da was fully engaged in the service of the Lord, his body did not belong to the material world. The pure Vai\'f1\'eb
ava's body is spiritualized even in this life. For example, when iron is put into a fire it becomes red-hot and is no longer iron but fire. Similarly, the so-called material bodies of devotees who fully engage in the devotional servic
e of the Lord, being constantly in the fire of spiritual life, have nothing to do with matter, but are spiritualized.
\par \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya remarks that the goddess of fortune, the mother of the universe, could not get mercy similar to that which was offered to Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, for although the goddess of fortune is always a constant companion of the Supreme Lord, the Lord is more inclined to His devotees. In other words, devotional service is so great that when it is offered even by those born in low familie
s, the Lord accepts it as being more valuable than the service offered by the goddess of fortune. Lord Brahm\'e4
, King Indra and the other demigods living in the upper planetary systems are situated in a different spirit of consciousness, and therefore they are sometimes troubled by demons, but a devotee, even if situated in the lower planets, enjoys life in K\'e5
\'f1\'eba consciousness under any circumstances. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid14560262 P}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 arata\'f9 svata\'f9 karmata\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 as he acts himself, as he is instructed by others or as he performs his material activities, he enjoys life in every respect. In this regard, Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya quotes the following verses, which are mentioned in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
Brahma-tarka:
