\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
My dear Lord, O Supreme Personality of Godhead, because of my association with material desires, one after another, I was gradually falling into a blind well full of snakes, following the general populace. But Your servant N\'e4rada M
uni kindly accepted me as his disciple and instructed me how to achieve this transcendental position. Therefore, my first duty is to serve him. How could I leave his service?
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 As will be seen in later verses, even though Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was direct
ly offered all the benedictions he might have desired, he refused to accept such offerings from the Supreme Personality of Godhead. On the contrary, he asked the Lord to engage him in the service of His servant N\'e4
rada Muni. This is the symptom of a pure devotee. One should serve the spiritual master first. It is not that one should bypass the spiritual master and desire to serve the Supreme Lord. This is not the principle for a Vai\'f1\'ebava. Narottama d\'e4sa 
\'d6h\'e4kura says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 t\'e4\'ecdera cara\'eba sevi bhakta-sane v\'e4sa\line janame janame haya, ei abhil\'e4\'f1a

\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 One should not be anxious to offer direct service to the Lord. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu advised that one become a servant of the servant of the servant of the Lord (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 gop\'e9-bhartu\'f9 pada-kamalayor d\'e4sa-d\'e4s\'e4nud\'e4sa\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). This is the proce
ss for approaching the Supreme Lord. The first service should be rendered to the spiritual master so that by his mercy one can approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead to render service. While teaching R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9, \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pras\'e4de p\'e4ya bhakti-lat\'e4-b\'e9ja:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 one can achieve the seed of devotional service by the mercy of the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the spiritual master, and then by the mercy of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. This is the secret of success. First one should try to please the spiritual master, and then o
ne should attempt to please the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura also says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ya}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid14384418 sya pras\'e4d\'e4d bhagavat-pras\'e4do}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 .}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  One should not attempt to please the Supreme Personality of Godhead by concoction. One must first be prepared to serve
 the spiritual master, and when one is qualified he is automatically offered the platform of direct service to the Lord. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja proposed that he engage in the service of N\'e4
rada Muni. He never proposed that he engage directly in the service of the Lord. This is the right conclusion. Therefore he said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 so 'ha\'e0 katha\'e0 nu vis\'e5je tava bh\'e5tya-sev\'e4m:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "How can I give up the service of my spiritual master, who has favored me in such a way that I am now able to see You face to face?" Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja prayed to the Lord that he might continue to engage in the service of his spiritual master, N
\'e4rada Muni.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.29
