ye bhajanti tu m\'e4\'e0 bhakty\'e4\line mayi te te\'f1u c\'e4py aham
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead is undoubtedly equal to everyone. He has no friend and no enemy, but as one desires benefits from the Lord, the Lord is very pleased to award them. The lower and highe
r positions of different living entities are due to their desires, for the Lord, being equal to all, fulfills everyone's desires. The killing of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and saving of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja also strictly followed this law of the supreme controller's activities. When Prahl\'e4da's mother, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu's wife, Kay\'e4dhu, was under the protection of N\'e4rada, she prayed for the protection of her son from the enemy, and N\'e4
rada Muni gave assurance that Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja would always be saved from the enemy's hands. Thus when Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was going to kill Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the Lord saved Prahl\'e4da to fulfill His promise in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kaunteya pratij\'e4n\'e9hi na me bhakta\'f9 pra\'eba\'e7yati}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) and to prove true the words of N\'e4
rada. The Lord can fulfill many purposes through one action. Thus the killing of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and the saving of Prahl\'e4
da were enacted simultaneously to prove the truthfulness of the Lord's devotee and the fidelity of the Lord Himself to His own purpose. The Lord acts only to satisfy the desires of His dev
otees; otherwise He has nothing to do. As confirmed in the Vedic language, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 na tasya k\'e4rya\'e0 kara\'eba\'e0 ca vidyate:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the Lord has nothing to do personally, for everything is done through His different potencies (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pa}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid3617703 r\'e4sya \'e7aktir vividhaiva \'e7r\'fcyate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). The Lord has m
ultifarious energies, through which everything is done. Thus when He personally does something, it is only to satisfy His devotee. The Lord is known as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakta-vatsala}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 because He very much favors His devoted servant.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.30
