\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
The entire cosmic manifestation is but an expansion of the Lord's energy; everything rests in Him, yet He exists separately, beyond creation, maintenance and annihilation. The varieties of creation are performed by His externa
l energy. Because the energy and energetic are one, everything is one (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva\'e0 khalv ida\'e0 brahma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Therefore without K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid13517011 Parabrahman}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 , nothing can exist. The difference between the material and spiritual worlds is that His external energy is manifeste
d in the material world, whereas His spiritual energy exists in the spiritual world. Both energies, however, belong to the Supreme Lord, and therefore in a higher sense there is no exhibition of material energy because everything is spiritual energy. The 
energy in which the Lord's all-pervasiveness is not realized is called material. Otherwise, everything is spiritual. Therefore Prahl\'e4da prays, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ekas tvam eva jagad etam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  "You are everything.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.31
