O my Lord, O Supreme Personality of Godhead, after the annihilation the creative energy is kept in You, who appear to sleep with half-closed eyes. Actually, however, You do not sleep like a
n ordinary human being, for You are always in a transcendental stage, beyond the creation of the material world, and You always feel transcendental bliss. As K\'e4ra\'ebodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'eb
u, You thus remain in Your transcendental status, not touching material objects. Although You appear to sleep, this sleeping is distinct from sleeping in ignorance.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 As explained very clearly in the }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (5.47):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ya\'f9 k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4r\'ebava-jale bhajati sma yoga-\line nidr\'e4m ananta-jagad-a\'eb\'f2
a-sa-roma-k\'fcpa\'f9\line \'e4dh\'e4ra-\'e7aktim avalambya par\'e4\'e0 sva-m\'fcrti\'e0\line govindam \'e4di-puru\'f1a\'e0 tam aha\'e0 bhaj\'e4mi
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"I worship the primeval Lord Govinda, who lies down in the Causal Ocean in His plenary portion as Mah\'e4-}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5114529 V}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 i\'f1\'eb
u, with all the universes generating from the pores of hair on His transcendental body, and who accepts the mystic slumber of eternity." The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4di-puru\'f1a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the original Supreme Personality of Godhead\emdash K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Govinda\emdash expands Himself as Mah\'e4-}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12202470 V}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 i\'f1\'eb
u. After the annihilation of this cosmic manifestation, He keeps Himself in transcendental bliss. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga-nidr\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 is used in reference to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. One should understand that this }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nidr\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or sleep, is not like our }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nidr\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 in the mode of ignorance. The Lord is always situated in transcendence. He is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sac-cid-\'e4nanda}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash eternally in bliss\emdash and thus
 He is not disturbed by sleep like ordinary human beings. It should be understood that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is in transcendental bliss in all stages. \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya concisely states that the Lord is }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 turya-sthita\'f9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  always situated in transcendence. In transcendence there is no such thing as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'e4gara\'eba-nidr\'e4-}{\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 su\'f1upti}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash wakefulness, sleep and deep sleep.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The practice of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 is similar to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga-nidr\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  of Mah\'e4-}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5114529 V}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 i\'f1\'ebu. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 are advised to keep their eyes half closed, but this state is not at all one of sleep, although imitation }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  especially in the modern age, manifest their so-called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  by sleeping. In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stra, yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dhy\'e4n\'e4vasthita,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  a state of full meditation, but this is meditation upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Dhy\'e4n\'e4vasthita-tad-gatena manas\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the mind should always be situated at the lotus feet of the Lord. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 practice does not mean sleeping. The mind should always be actively fixed at the lotus feet of the Lord. Then one's practice of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  will be successful.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.33
