\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
This cosmic manifestation, the material world, is also Your body. This total lump of matter is agitated by Your potent energy known as k\'e4la-\'e7akti, and thus the three modes of material nature are manifested. You awaken from the bed of \'c7e\'f1
a, Ananta, and from Your navel a small transcendental seed is generated. It is from this seed that the lotus flower of the gigantic universe is manifested, exactly as a banyan tree grows from a small seed.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The three different forms of }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12202470 Mah\'e4-Vi\'f1\'ebu}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash namely K\'e4ra\'ebodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu and K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, who are the origin of creation and maintenance\emdash are gradually being described. From }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid12202470 Mah\'e4-Vi\'f1\'ebu}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 , Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu is generated, and from Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu gradually expands. Thus }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid12202470 Mah\'e4-Vi\'f1\'ebu}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is the original cause of Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, and from Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu comes the lotus flower from which Lord Brahm\'e4
 is manifested. Thus the original cause of everything is Vi\'f1\'ebu, and consequently the cosmic manifestation is not different from Vi\'f1\'ebu. This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (10.8), wherein K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhavo matta\'f9 sarva\'e0 pravartate:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  "I am the source of all spiritual and material worlds. Everything emanates from Me." Garbhodaka\'e7
\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu is an expansion of K\'e4ra\'ebodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, who is an expansion of Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba. In this way, K\'e5\'f1\'eba is ultimately the cause of all causes (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-k\'e4ra\'eba-k\'e4ra
\'ebam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). The conclusion is that both the material world and spiritual world are considered to be the body of the Supreme Lord. W
e can understand that the material body is caused by the spiritual body and is therefore an expansion of the spiritual body. Thus when one takes up spiritual activities, one's entire material body is spiritualized. Similarly, in this material world, when 
the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement expands, the entire material world becomes spiritualized. As long as we do not realize this, we live in the material world, but when we are fully K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious we live not in the material world but in the spiritual world.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.34
