sva-karma-patitam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash fallen because of the reactions of one's own material activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhava}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash compared to the world of nescience (birth, death, old age and disease); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vaitara\'eby\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in the river known as Vaitara\'eb\'e9 (which lies in front of the doorway of Yamar\'e4ja, the superintendent of death); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 anya\'f9 anya}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash one after another; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 janma}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash birth; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mara\'eba}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash death; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4\'e7ana}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash different types of eating; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bh\'e9ta-bh\'e9tam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash being exceedingly afraid; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pa\'e7yan}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash seeing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 janam}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the living entity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash one's own; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 para}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of others; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vigraha}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash in the body; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vaira-maitram}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash considering friendship and enmity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hanta}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash alas; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iti}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash in this way; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 p\'e4racara}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O You, who are on the other side of the river of death; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 p\'e9p\'e5hi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
kindly save us all (from this dangerous condition); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'fc\'f2ham}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash we are all foolish, bereft of spiritual knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 adya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
today (because You are personally present here).
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 My dear Lord, You are always transcendentally situated on the o
ther side of the river of death, but because of the reactions of our own activities, we are suffering on this side. Indeed, we have fallen into this river and are repeatedly suffering the pains of birth and death and eating horrible things. Now kindly loo
k upon us\emdash not only upon me but also upon all others who are suffering\emdash and by Your causeless mercy and compassion, deliver us and maintain us.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, a pure Vai\'f1\'eb
ava, prays to the Lord not only for himself but for all other suffering living entities. There are two classes of Vai\'f1\'ebavas\emdash the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhajan\'e4nand\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 go\'f1\'f6hy-\'e4nand\'e9s.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhajan\'e4nand\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  worship the Lord only for their own personal benefit, but the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 go\'f1\'f6hy-\'e4nand\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  try to elevate all others to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness so that they may be saved.
 Fools who cannot perceive repeated birth and death and the other miseries of materialistic life cannot be sure of what will happen to them in their next birth. Indeed, these foolish, materially contaminated rascals have manufactured an irresponsible way 
of life that does not consider the next life. They do not know that according to one's own activities, one receives a body selected from 8,400,000 species. These rascals have been described in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 du\'f1k\'e5tino m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Nondevotees, those who are not K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious, must engage in sinful activities, and therefore they are }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'fc\'f2has}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash fools and rascals. They are such fools that they do not know what will happen to them in their next life. Although they see varieties of living creatures eating abominable things
\emdash pigs eating stool, crocodiles eating all kinds of flesh, and so on\emdash 
they do not realize that they themselves, because of their practice of eating all kinds of nonsense in this life, will be destined to eat the most abominable things in their next life. A Vai\'f1\'eb
ava is always afraid of such an abominable life, and to free himself from such horrible conditions, he engages himself in the devotional service of the Lord. The Lord is compassionate to them, and therefore He appears for their benefit.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yad\'e4 yad\'e4 hi dharmasya\line gl\'e4nir bhavati bh\'e4rata\line abhyutth\'e4
nam adharmasya\line tad\'e4tm\'e4na\'e0 s\'e5j\'e4my aham
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Whenever and wherever there is a decline in religious practice, O descendant of Bh\'e4
rata, and a predominant rise of irreligion\emdash at that time I descend Myself." (Bg. 4.7) The Lord is always ready to help the fallen souls, but because they are fools and rascals, they do not take to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness and abide by the instructions of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore although \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu is personally the Supreme Lord, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, He comes as a devotee to preach the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Y\'e4re dekha, t\'e4re kaha 'k\'e5\'f1\'eba'-upade\'e7a.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  One must therefore become a sincere servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c4m\'e4ra \'e4j\'ef\'e4ya guru ha\'ef\'e4
 t\'e4ra' ei de\'e7a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (Cc. }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Madhya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  7.128). One should become a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and spread K\'e5\'f1\'eba consc
iousness all over the world, simply by preaching the teachings of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.42
