\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 eva}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash certainly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 udvije}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash I am disturbed or afraid; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 para}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O Supreme; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 duratyaya}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash insurmountable or very difficult to cross; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vaitara\'eby\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of the Vaitara\'eb\'e9, the river of the material world; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tvat-v\'e9rya}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of Your Lordship's glories and activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 g\'e4yana}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash from chanting or distributing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mah\'e4-am\'e5ta}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
in the great ocean of nectarean spiritual bliss; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 magna-citta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash whose consciousness is absorbed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7oce}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash I am simply lamenting; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tata\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash from that; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vimukha-cetasa\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the fools and rascals who are bereft of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
indriya-artha}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in sense gratification; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4-sukh\'e4ya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash for temporary, illusory happiness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bharam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
the false burden or responsibility (of maintaining one's family, society and nation and elaborate arrangements for that purpose); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 udvahata\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash who are lifting (by making grand pla
ns for this arrangement); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vim\'fc\'f2h\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash although all of them are nothing but fools and rascals (I am thinking of them also).
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
O best of the great personalities, I am not at all afraid of material existence, for wherever I stay I am fully absorbed in 
thoughts of Your glories and activities. My concern is only for the fools and rascals who are making elaborate plans for material happiness and maintaining their families, societies and countries. I am simply concerned with love for them.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Throughou
t the entire world, everyone is making big, big plans to adjust the miseries of the material world, and this is true at present, in the past and in the future. Nonetheless, although they make elaborate political, social and cultural plans, they have all b
een described herein as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vim\'fc\'f2ha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash fools. The material world has been described in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 du\'f9kh\'e4layam a\'e7\'e4\'e7vatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash temporary and miserable\emdash but these fools are trying to turn the material world into }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sukh\'e4layam,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  a place of happiness, not knowing how everything acts by the arrangement of material nature, which works in her own way.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prak\'e5te\'f9 kriyam\'e4\'eb\'e4ni\line gu\'ebai\'f9 karm\'e4\'ebi sarva\'e7a\'f9\line aha
\'eck\'e4ra-vim\'fc\'f2h\'e4tm\'e4\line kart\'e4ham iti manyate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "The bewildered spirit soul, under the influence of the three modes of material nature, thin
ks himself to be the doer of activities that are in actuality carried out by nature." (Bg. 3.27)
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 There is a plan for material nature, personally known as Durg\'e4
, to punish the demons. Although the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asuras,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the godless demons, struggle for existence, they are directly attacked by the goddess Durg\'e4
, who is well equipped with ten hands with different types of weapons to punish them. She is carried by her lion carrier, or the modes of passion and ignorance. Everyone struggles very hard to fight through the modes 
of passion and ignorance and conquer material nature, but at the end everyone is vanquished by nature's laws.
\par There is a river known as Vaitara\'eb\'e9 between the material and spiritual worlds, and one must cross this river to reach the other side, or the spiritual world. This is an extremely difficult task. As the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (7.14), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1\'e4 gu\'eba-may\'e9 mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "This divine energy of Mine, consisting of the three modes of material nature, is difficult to overcome." The same word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 duratyaya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 meaning "very difficult," is used here. Therefore one cannot surpass the stringent laws of material nature except by the mercy of the Supreme Lord. Nonetheless, although all materialists are baffled in their plans, they try again and again to bec
ome happy in this material world. Therefore they have been described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vim\'fc\'f2ha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash first-class fools. As for Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, he was not at all unhappy, for although he was in the material world, he was full of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. Those who are K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious, trying to serve the Lord, are not unhappy, whereas one who has no assets in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness and is struggling for existence is not only foolish but extremely unhappy also. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was happy and unhappy simultaneously. He felt happiness and transcendental bliss because of his being K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious, yet he felt great unhappiness for the fools and rascals who make elaborate plans to be happy in this material world.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.44
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 44
