\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pr\'e4ye\'eba}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash generally, in almost all cases; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 deva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O my Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 munaya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the great saintly persons; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash personal, own; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vimukti-k\'e4m\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash ambitious for liberation from this material world; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 maunam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash silently; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 caranti}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash they wander (in places like the Himalayan forests, where they have no touch with the activities of the materialists); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vijane}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in solitary places; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 para-artha-ni\'f1\'f6h\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash interested in working for others by giving them the benefit of the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement, by enlightening them with K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 et\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash these; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vih
\'e4ya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash leaving aside; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e5pa\'eb\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash fools and rascals (engaged in materialistic activity who do not know the benefit of the human form of life); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vimumuk\'f1e}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash I desire to be liberated and to return home, back to Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 eka\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash alone; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 anyam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash other; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tvat}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash but for You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 asya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of this; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7ara\'ebam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash shelter; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhramata\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of the living entity rotating and wandering throughout the material universes; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 anupa\'e7ye}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash do I see.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 My dear Lord }{\fs28\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
, I see that ther
e are many saintly persons indeed, but they are interested only in their own deliverance. Not caring for the big cities and towns, they go to the Himalayas or the forest to meditate with vows of silence [mauna-vrata]. They are not interested in delivering
 others. As for me, however, I do not wish to be liberated alone, leaving aside all these poor fools and rascals. I know that without K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, without taking shelter of Your lotus feet, one cannot be happy. Therefore I wish to bring them back to shelter at Your lotus feet.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 This is the decision of the Vai\'f1\'eb
ava, the pure devotee of the Lord. For himself he has no problems, even if he has to stay in this material world, because his only business is to remain in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. The K\'e5\'f1\'eba
 conscious person can go even to hell and still be happy. Therefore Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 naivodvije para duratyaya-vaitara\'eby\'e4\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "O best of the great personalities, I am not at all afraid of material existence." The pure devotee is never unhappy in any condition of life. This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (6.17.28):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-par\'e4\'f9 sarve\line na kuta\'e7cana bibhyati\line svarg\'e4
pavarga-narake\'f1v\line api tuly\'e4rtha-dar\'e7ina\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Devotees solely engaged in the devotional service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4
r\'e4ya\'eba, never fear any condition of life. For them the heavenly planets, liberation and the hellish planets are all the same, for such devotees are interested only in the service of the Lord."
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 For a devotee, being situated in the heavenly planets and being in the
 hellish planets are equal, for a devotee lives neither in heaven nor in hell but with K\'e5\'f1\'eba in the spiritual world. The secret of success for the devotee is not understood by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karm\'e9s}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Karm\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  therefore try to be happy by material adjustment, and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 want to be happy by becoming one with the Supreme. The devotee has no such interest. He is not interested in so-called meditation in the Himalayas or the forest. Rather, his interest is in the busiest part of the world, where he teaches people K\'e5\'f1
\'eba consciousness. The K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement was started for this purpose. We do not teach one to meditate in a secluded place just so that one may show that he has become very much advanced and may be proud of his so-called transcendental meditati
on, although he engages in all sorts of foolish materialistic activity. A Vai\'f1\'ebava like Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja is not interested in such a bluff of spiritual advancement. Rather, he is interested in enlightening people in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness because that is the only way for them to become happy. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja says clearly, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e4nya\'e0 tvad asya \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 bhramato 'nupa\'e7ye:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  "I know that without K
\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, without taking shelter of Your lotus feet, one cannot be happy." One wanders within the universe, life after life, but by the grace of a devotee, a servant of \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, one can get the clue to K\'e5\'f1
\'eba consciousness and then not only become happy in this world but also return home, back to Godhead. That is the real target in life. The members of the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement are not at all interested in so-called meditation in the Himalayas or the forest, where one will only make a show of meditation, nor are they interested in opening many schools for }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and meditation in the cities. Rather, every member of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is interested in going door to door to try to convince people about the teachings of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4 As It Is,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the teachings of Lord Caitanya. That is the purpose of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba movement. The members of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement must be fully convinced that without K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a one cannot be happy. Thus the K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious person avoids all kinds of pseudo spiritualists, transcendentalists, meditators, monists, philosophers and philanthropists.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.45
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 45
