\par t\'e5pyanti neha k\'e5pa\'eb\'e4 bahu-du\'f9kha-bh\'e4ja\'f9
\par ka\'eb\'f2\'fctivan manasija\'e0 vi\'f1aheta dh\'e9ra\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yat}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
that which (is meant for material sense gratification); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 maithuna-\'e4di}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash represented by talking of sex, reading sexual literature or enjoying sex life (at home or outside, as in a club); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 g\'e5hamedhi-sukham}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash all types of material happiness based on attachment to family, society, friendship, etc.; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash indeed; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tuccham}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash insignificant; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ka\'eb\'f2\'fcyanena}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash with the itching; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 karayo\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
of the two hands (to relieve the itching); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash like; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 du\'f9kha-du\'f9kham}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
different types of unhappiness (into which one is put after such itching sense gratification); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 t\'e5pyanti}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash become satisfied; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash never; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 iha}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in material sense gratification; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e5pa\'eb\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the foolish persons; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bahu-du\'f9kha-bh\'e4ja\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash subjected to various types of material unhappiness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ka\'eb\'f2\'fcti-vat}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash if one can learn from such itching; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 manasi-jam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash which is simply a mental concoction (actually there is no happiness); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vi\'f1aheta}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash and tolerates (such itching); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dh\'e9ra\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
(he can become) a most perfect, sober person.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 Sex life is compared to the rubbing of two hands to relieve an itch. G\'e5
hamedhis, so-called g\'e5hasthas who have no spiritual knowledge, think that this itching is the greatest platform of happiness, although actually it is a source of distress. The k\'e5pa\'ebas, the fools who are just the opposite of br\'e4hma\'eb
as, are not satisfied by repeated sensuous enjoyment. Those who are dh\'e9ra, however, who are sober and who tolerate this itching, are not subjected to the sufferings of fools and rascals.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Materialists t
hink that sexual indulgence is the greatest happiness in this material world, and therefore they make elaborate plans to satisfy their senses, especially the genitals. This is generally found everywhere, and specifically found in the Western world, where 
t
here are regular arrangements to satisfy sex life in different ways. Actually, however, this has not made anyone happy. Even the hippies, who have given up all the materialistic comforts of their fathers and grandfathers, cannot give up the sensational ha
ppiness of sex life. Such persons are described here as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e5pa\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 misers. The human form of life is a great asset, for in this life one can fulfill the goal of existence. Unfortunately, however, because of a lack of education and culture, people are victimized by the false happiness of sex life. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja therefore advises one not to be misled by this civilization of sense gratification, and especially not by sex life. Rather, one should be sober, avoid sense gratification and be K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious. The 
lusty person, who is compared to a foolish miser, never gets happiness by sense gratification. The influence of material nature is very difficult to surpass, but as stated by K\'e5\'f1\'eba in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (7.14), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4m eva ye prapadyante, m\'e4y\'e4m et\'e4\'e0 taranti te:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  if one voluntarily submits to the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, he can be saved very easily.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 In reference to the low-grade happiness of sex life, Y\'e4mun\'e4c\'e4
rya says in this connection:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yad-avadhi mama ceta\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-p\'e4d\'e4ravinde\line nava-nava-rasa-dh\'e4
many udyata\'e0 rantum \'e4s\'e9t\line tad-avadhi bata n\'e4r\'e9-sa\'ecgame smaryam\'e4ne\line bhavati mukha-vik\'e4ra\'f9 su\'f1\'f6hu ni\'f1\'f6h\'e9vana\'e0 ca
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Since I have been engaged in the transcendental loving service of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, realizing ever-new pleasure in Him, whenever I think of sex pleasure, I spit at the thought, and my lips curl with distaste." Y\'e4mun\'e4c\'e4
rya had formerly been a great king who enjoyed sexual happiness in various ways, but since he later engaged himself in the service of the Lord, he enjoyed spiritual bliss and hated to think of sex life. If sexual thoughts 
came to him, he would spit with disgust.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.46
