\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash chanting or reciting }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mantras;}{\fs28\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sam\'e4dhaya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash remaining in trance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4pavargy\'e4\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash these are ten types of activities for advancing on the path of liberation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pr\'e4ya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash generally; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 param}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
the only means; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 puru\'f1a}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O my Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash all of them; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tu}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash but; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ajita-indriy\'e4\'eb\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of persons who cannot control the senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 v\'e4rt\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash means of living; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhavanti}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash are; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 uta}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash so it is said; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 v\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash or; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 atra}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in this connection; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tu}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash but; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 d\'e4mbhik\'e4n\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
of persons who are falsely proud.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
O Supreme Personality of Godhead, there are ten prescribed methods on the path to liberation\emdash to remain silent, not to speak to anyone, to observe vows, to amass all kinds of Vedic knowledge, to undergo
 austerities, to study the Vedas and other Vedic literatures, to execute the duties of var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma, to explain the \'e7\'e4
stras, to stay in a solitary place, to chant mantras silently, and to be absorbed in trance. These different methods for liberation a
re generally only a professional practice and means of livelihood for those who have not conquered their senses. Because such persons are falsely proud, these procedures may not be successful.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (6.1.15):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kecit kevalay\'e4 bhakty\'e4\line v\'e4sudeva-par\'e4ya\'eb\'e4\'f9\line agha\'e0
 dhunvanti k\'e4rtsnyena\line n\'e9h\'e4ram iva bh\'e4skara\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Only a rare person who has adopted complete, unalloyed devotional service to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a can uproot the weeds of sinful actions with no possibility that they will revive. He can do thi
s simply by discharging devotional service, just as the sun can immediately dissipate fog by its rays." The real purpose of human life is to attain liberation from material entanglement. Such liberation may be achieved by many methods (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tapas\'e4 brahmacarye\'eba \'e7amena ca damena ca}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ), but all of them more or less depend on }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tapasya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  austerity, which begins with celibacy. 
\'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 says that those who are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 v\'e4sudeva-par\'e4ya\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  who have fully surrendered to the lotus feet of Lord V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, automatically ac
hieve the results of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mauna}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (silence), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vrata}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (vows) and other such methods simply by discharging devotional service. In other words, these methods are not so powerful. If one takes to devotional service, all of them are very easily performed.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Mauna,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  for exa
mple, does not mean that one should just stop speaking. The tongue is meant for speaking, although sometimes, to make a big show, a person remains silent. There are many who observe silence some day in a week. Vai\'f1\'eb
avas, however, do not observe such silence. Silence means not speaking foolishly. Speakers at assemblies, conferences and meetings generally speak foolishly like toads. This is described by \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 v\'e4co vegam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  One who wants to say something can show himself to be a big orator, but r
ather than go on speaking nonsense, better to remain silent. This method of silence, therefore, is recommended for persons very attached to speaking nonsense. One who is not a devotee must speak nonsensically because he does not have the power to speak ab
out the glories of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Thus whatever he says is influenced by the illusory energy and is compared to the croaking of a frog. One who speaks about the glories of the Lord, however, has no need to be silent. Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu recommends, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e9rtan\'e9ya\'f9 sad\'e4 hari\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  one should go on chanting the glories of the Lord twenty-four hours a day. There is no question of becoming }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mauna,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or silent.
\par The ten processes for liberation or improvement on the path of liberation are not meant for the devotees. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Kevalay\'e4 bhakty\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 if one simply engages in devotional service to the Lord, all ten methods of liberation are automatically observed. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's proposal is that such processes may be recommended for the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ajitendriya,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  those who cannot conquer their senses. Devotees, however, have already conquered their senses. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Sarvop\'e4dhi-vinirmukta\'e0 tat-paratvena nirmalam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 a devotee is already freed from material contamination. \'c7r\'e9la Bhaktisiddh\'e4nta Sarasvat\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura therefore said:
\par }\pard\plain \s320\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 du}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid15410175 \'f1\'f6a mana! tumi kisera vai\'f1\'ebava? }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prati\'f1\'f6h\'e4ra t}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid15410175 are, nirjanera ghare,\line tava hari}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e4ma kevala kaitava
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 There are many who like to chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  in a silent, solitary place, but if one is not interested in preaching, talking constantly to the nondevotees, the influence of the modes of nature is ve
ry difficult to surpass. Therefore unless one is extremely advanced in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, one should not imitate Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura, who had no other business than chanting the holy name always, twenty-four hours a day. Prahl\'e4da Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja does not condemn such a process; he accepts it, but without active service to the Lord, simply by such methods one generally cannot attain liberation. One cannot attain liberation simply by false pride.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.9.47
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 47
