\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.10 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 This chapter describes how the Supreme Personality of Godhead }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{
\insrsid30033  disappeared, after pleasing Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. It also describes a benediction given by Lord \'c7iva.
\par Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033  wanted to bestow benedictions upon Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, one after another, but Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, thinking them impediments on the path of spiritual progress, did not accept any of them. Instead, he 
fully surrendered at the Lord's lotus feet. He said: "If anyone engaged in the devotional service of the Lord prays for personal sense gratification, he cannot be called a pure devotee or even a devotee. He may be called only a merchant engaged in the bus
iness of give and take. Similarly, a master who wants to please his servant after taking service from him is also not a real master." Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, therefore, did not ask anything from the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Rather, he said that if the Lor
d wanted to give him a benediction, he wanted the Lord to assure him that he would never be induced to take any benedictions for the sake of material desires. Exchanges of devotional service for lusty desires are always very prominent. As soon as lusty de
s
ires awaken, one's senses, mind, life, soul, religious principles, patience, intelligence, shyness, beauty, strength, memory and truthfulness are all vanquished. One can render unalloyed devotional service only when there are no material desires in one's 
mind.
\par The Supreme Personality of Godhead was greatly pleased with Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja for his unalloyed devotion, yet the Lord provided him one material benediction}{\insrsid10911155 \emdash }{\insrsid30033 
that he would be perfectly happy in this world and live his next life in Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha. The Lord gave him the benediction that he would be the king of this material world until the end of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 manvantara}{\insrsid30033 
 millennium and that although in this material world, he would have the facility to hear the glories of the Lord and depend fully on the Lord, performing service to Him in uncontaminated }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga.}{\insrsid30033 
 The Lord advised Prahl\'e4da to perform sacrifices through }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga,}{\insrsid30033  for this is the duty of a king.
\par Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja accepted whatever the Lord had offered him, and he prayed for the Lord to deliver his fat
her. In response to this prayer, the Lord assured him that in the family of such a pure devotee as he, not only the devotee's father but his forefathers for twenty-one generations are liberated. The Lord also asked Prahl\'e4
da to perform the ritualistic ceremonies appropriate after his father's death.
\par Then Lord Brahm\'e4, who was also present, offered many prayers to the Lord, expressing his obligation to the Lord for having offered benedictions to Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. The Lord advised Lord Brahm\'e4 not to offer benedictions to }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 asuras}{\insrsid30033  as he had to Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, for such benedictions indulge them. Then Lord }{\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid30033  disappeared. On that day, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was installed on the throne of the world by Lord Brahm\'e4 and \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya.
\par Thus N\'e4rada Muni described the character of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja for Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, and he further described the killing of R\'e4va\'eba by Lord R\'e4macandra and the killing of \'c7i\'e7up\'e4la and Dantavakra in Dv\'e4
para-yuga. \'c7i\'e7up\'e4la, of course, had merged into the existence of the Lord and thus achieved }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 s\'e4yujya-mukti.}{\insrsid30033  N\'e4rada Muni praised Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira Mah\'e4r\'e4ja because the Supreme Lord, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, was the greatest well-wisher and friend of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas and almost always stayed in their house. Thus the fortune of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas was greater than that of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\fs24\cf0\insrsid30033 \tab }{\insrsid30033 Later, N\'e4rada Muni described how the demon Maya D\'e4nava constructed Tripura for the demons, who became very powerful and defeated the demigods. Because of this defeat, Lord Rudra, \'c7
iva, dismantled Tripura; thus he became famous as Tripur\'e4ri. For this, Rudra is very much appreciated and worshiped by the demigods. This narration occurs at the end of the chapter.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.10.1
