da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said (to the Supreme Personality of Godhead); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash please do not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash me; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pralobhaya}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash allure; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 utpatty\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash because of my birth (in a demoniac family); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 saktam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash (I am already) attached; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e4me\'f1u}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash to material enjoyment; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by all those; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 varai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
benedictions of material possessions; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tat-sa\'ecga-bh\'e9ta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash being afraid of such material association; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 nirvi\'eb\'eba\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
completely detached from material desires; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mumuk\'f1u\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash desiring to be liberated from material conditions of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tv\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash u
nto Your lotus feet; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 up\'e4\'e7rita\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash I have taken shelter.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid30033 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said:}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
 My dear Lord, O Supreme Personality of Godhead, because I was born in an atheistic family I am naturally attached to material enjoyment. Therefore, kindly do not tempt
 me with these illusions. I am very much afraid of material conditions, and I desire to be liberated from materialistic life. It is for this reason that I have taken shelter of Your lotus feet.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033\charrsid14425756 Materialistic life means attachment to the body and ev
erything in relationship to the body. This attachment is based on lusty desires for sense gratification, specifically sexual enjoyment. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 K\'e4mais tais tair h\'e5ta-j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
when one is too attached to material enjoyment, he is bereft of all knowledge (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 h\'e5ta j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  those who are attached to material enjoyment are mostly inclined to worship the demigods to procure various material opulences. They are especially attached to worship of the goddess Durg\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva because this transcend
ental couple can offer their devotees all material opulence. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, however, was detached from all material enjoyment. He therefore took shelter of the lotus feet of Lord }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 , and not the feet of any demigod. It is to be understood that if one really wants release from this material world, from the threefold miseries and from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 janma-m\'e5tyu jar\'e4-vy\'e4dhi}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (birth, death, old age and disease), one must take shelter of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, for without the Supreme Personality of God
head one cannot get release from materialistic life. Atheistic men are very much attached to material enjoyment. Therefore if they get some opportunity to achieve more and more material enjoyment, they take it. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, however, was very careful in this regard. Although born of a materialistic father, because he was a devotee he had no material desires (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnyam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.10.3
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 3
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
