{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash otherwise; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 akhila-guro}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O supreme instructor of the entire creation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
gha\'f6eta}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash such a thing can happen; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 karu\'eb\'e4-\'e4tmana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the Supreme Person, who is extremely kind to His devotees; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ya\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash any person who; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash from You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4\'e7i\'f1a\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash material benefits; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4\'e7\'e4ste
}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash desires (in exchange for serving You); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 na}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash such a person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bh\'e5tya
\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash a servitor; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash such a person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vai}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 va\'ebik}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash a merchant (who wants to get material profit from his business).
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 Otherwise, O my Lord, O supreme instructor of the entire world, You a
re so kind to Your devotee that You could not induce him to do something unbeneficial for him. On the other hand, one who desires some material benefit in exchange for devotional service cannot be Your pure devotee. Indeed, he is no better than a merchant
 who wants profit in exchange for service.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
It is sometimes found that one comes to a devotee or a temple of the Lord just to get some material benefit. Such a person is described here as a mercantile man. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  speaks of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4rto jij\'ef\'e4sur arth\'e4rth\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4rta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to one who is physically distressed, and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
arth\'e4rth\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to one in need of money. Such persons are forced to approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead for mitigation of their distress or to get some money by the benediction of 
the Lord. They have been described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 suk\'e5t\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 pious, because in their distress or need for money they have approached the Supreme Lord. Unless one is pious, one cannot approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead. However, although a pious man may receive s
ome material benefit, one who is concerned with material benefits cannot be a pure devotee. When a pure devotee receives material opulences, this is not because of his pious activity but for the service of the Lord. When one engages in devotional service,
 one is automatically pious. Therefore, a pure devotee is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid8800353 any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnyam}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 .}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 He has no desire for material profit, nor does the Lord induce him to try to profit materially. When a devotee needs something, the Supreme Personality of Godhead supplies it (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga-k\'f1ema\'e0 vah\'e4my aham}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
Sometimes materialists go to a temple to offer flowers and fruit to the Lord because they have learned from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 that if a devotee offers some flowers and fruits, the Lord accepts them. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (9.26) the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 patra\'e0 pu\'f1pa\'e0 phala\'e0 toya\'e0\line yo me bhakty\'e4 prayacchati\line tad aha
\'e0 bhakty-upah\'e5tam\line a\'e7n\'e4mi prayat\'e4tmana\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"If one offers Me with love and devotion a leaf, a flower, fruit or water, I will accept it." Thus a man with a mercantile mentality thinks that if he can
 get some material benefit, like a large amount of money, simply by offering a little fruit and flower, this is good business. Such persons are not accepted as pure devotees. Because their desires are not purified, they are still mercantile men, even thou
gh they go to temples to make a show of being devotees. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Sarvop\'e4dhi-vinirmukta\'e0 tat-paratvena nirmalam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 only when one is fully freed from material desires can one be purified, and only in that purified state can one serve the Lord. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'eba h\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a-sevana\'e0 bhaktir ucyate.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  This is the pure devotional platform.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.10.5
