pa' haya-k\'e5\'f1\'ebera 'nitya-d\'e4sa': }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 every living being is eternally a servant of the Supreme Lord, K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (5.29), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4\'e0 sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "I am the proprietor of all planets, and I am the supreme enjoyer." This is the natural position of the Lord, and the natural position of the living being is to surrender unto Him (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka
\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). If this relationship
 continues, then real happiness exists eternally between the master and servant. Unfortunately, when this eternal relationship is disturbed, the living entity wants to become separately happy and thinks that the master is his order supplier. In this way t
h
ere cannot be happiness. Nor should the master cater to the desires of the servant. If he does, he is not the real master. The real master commands, "You must do this," and the real servant immediately obeys the order. Unless this relationship between the
 Supreme Lord and the subordinate living entity is established, there can be no real happiness. The living entity is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4\'e7raya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  always subordinate, and the Supreme Personality of Godhead is }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vi\'f1aya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the supreme objective, the goal of life. Unfortunate persons trapped in this material world do not know this. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Na te vidu\'f9 sv\'e4rtha-gati\'e0 hi vi
\'f1\'ebum:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 illusioned by the material energy, everyone in this material world is unaware that the only aim of life is to approach Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4r\'e4dhan\'e4n\'e4\'e0 sarve\'f1\'e4\'e0\line vi\'f1\'ebor \'e4r\'e4dhana\'e0 param
\line tasm\'e4t paratara\'e0 devi\line tad\'e9y\'e4n\'e4\'e0 samarcanam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Lord \'c7
iva explains to his wife, Parvat\'e9, the goddess Durg\'e4, that the highest goal of life is to satisfy Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who can be satisfied only when His servant is satisfied. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu therefore teaches, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 gop\'e9-bhartu\'f9 pada-kamalayor d\'e4sa-d\'e4s\'e4nud\'e4sa\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  One must become a servant of the servant. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja also prayed to Lord }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10038355 N\'e5si\'e0
hadeva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  that he might be engaged as the servant of the Lord's servant. This is the prescribed metho
d of devotional service. As soon as a devotee wants the Supreme Personality of Godhead to be his order supplier, the Lord immediately refuses to become the master of such a motivated devotee. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (4.11) the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ye yath\'e4 m\'e4\'e0 prapadyante t\'e4\'e0s tathaiva bhaj\'e4my aham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "As one surrenders unto Me, I reward him accordingly." Materialistic persons are generally inclined to material profits. As long as one continues in such an adulterated position, he does not receive the benefit of returning home, back to Godhead.
