prabhu taught us how to pray for benedictions from the Lord. He said:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 na dhana\'e0 na jana\'e0 na sundar\'e9\'e0\line kavit\'e4\'e0 v\'e4 jagad-\'e9\'e7a k\'e4
maye\line mama janmani janman\'e9\'e7vare\line bhavat\'e4d bhaktir ahaituk\'e9 tvayi}{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"O my Lord, I do not want from You any amount of wealth, nor many followers, nor a beautiful wife, for these are all materialistic desires. But if I have to ask You for any benediction, I pray that in whatever forms of life I may take my birth, under an
y circumstances, I will not be bereft of Your transcendental devotional service." Devotees are always on the positive platform, in contrast to the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s, who want to make everything impersonal or void. One cannot remain void (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcnyav\'e4d\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ); rather, one must possess something. Therefore, the devotee, on the positive side, wants to possess something, and this possession is very nicely described by Prahl\'e4da Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja, who says, "If I must take some benediction from You, I pray that within the core of my heart there may be no material desires." The desire to serve the Supreme Personality of Godhead is not at all material.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.10.8
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 8
