\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 manasi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash within the mind; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sthit\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash situated; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tarhi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash at that time only; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 eva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pu\'eb\'f2ar\'e9ka-ak\'f1a}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O lotus-eyed Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhagavattv\'e4ya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
to be equally as opulent as the Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kalpate}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash becomes eligible.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 O my Lord,
 when a human being is able to give up all the material desires in his mind, he becomes eligible to possess wealth and opulence like Yours.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
Atheistic men sometimes criticize a devotee by saying, "If you do not want to take any benediction from the Lord and if the servant of the Lord is as opulent as the Lord Himself, why do you ask for the benediction of being engaged as the Lord's servant?" 
\'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9 comments, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhagavattv\'e4ya bhagavat-sam\'e4n ai\'e7vary\'e4ya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavattva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  becoming as good as the Suprem
e Personality of Godhead, does not mean becoming one with Him or equal to Him, although in the spiritual world the servant is equally as opulent as the master. The servant of the Lord is engaged in the service of the Lord as a servant, friend, father, mot
her or conjugal lover, all of whom are equally as opulent as the Lord. This is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acintya-bhed\'e4bheda-tattva.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 The master and servant are different yet equal in opulence. This is the meaning of simultaneous difference from the Supreme Lord and oneness with Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.10.10
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 10
