avas there had been many, many devotees, such as the descendants of the Yadu dynasty and Vasi\'f1\'f6ha, Mar\'e9ci, Ka\'e7yapa, Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva, who were all extremely fortunate. The P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, however, were bette
r than all of them because K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself lived with them constantly. N\'e4rada Muni therefore specifically mentioned that within this material world (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e5-loke}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) the P\'e4\'eb\'f2
