avas to Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra and Duryodhana. Because K\'e5\'f1\'eba was the well-wisher of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, He also acted as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 by becoming the spiritual master of Arjuna. Arjuna accepted K\'e5\'f1\'eba as his spiritual master (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7i\'f1yas t}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid3108755 e 'ha\'e0 \'e7\'e4dhi m\'e4\'e0 tv\'e4\'e0 prapannam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ), and K\'e5\'f1\'eba sometimes chastised him. For example, the Lord said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 a\'e7ocy\'e4n anva\'e7ocas tva\'e0 praj\'ef\'e4-v\'e4d\'e4\'e0\'e7 ca bh\'e4\'f1ase: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"while speaking learned words, you are mourning for what is not worthy of grief." The Lord also said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kutas tv\'e4 ka\'e7malam ida\'e0 vi\'f1ame samupasthitam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "My dear Arjuna, how have these impurities come upon you?" Such was the intimate relationship between the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas and K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In the same way, a pure devotee of the Lord is always with K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a through thick and thin; his way of life is K\'e5\'f1\'eba. This is the statement of the authority \'c7r\'e9 N\'e4rada Muni.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.10.50
