f the entire world. One should not be influenced by the illusory energy and think Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba to be an ordinary human being. Those who really seek the Absolute Truth come to the understanding that K\'e5\'f1\'eba is everything (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 v\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Such great souls are very rare. Nonetheless, if one studies the entire }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  as it is, K\'e5\'f1
\'eba is very easy to understand. The K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is just trying to make K\'e5\'f1\'eba known all over the world as the Supreme Personality of Godhead (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e5\'f1\'ebas tu bhagav\'e4n svayam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). If people take this movement seriously, their lives as human beings will be successful.
\par }\pard\plain \s1178\ql \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Seventh Canto, Tenth Chapter, of the }{
\cs2344\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  entitled "Prahl\'e4da, the Best Among Exalted Devotees."
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf18\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.11: The Perfect Society: Four Social Classes
\par }\pard\plain \s330\qc \li0\ri0\sb540\sa540\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat10 \b\f35\fs36\cf8\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\insrsid8789409 CHAPTER ELEVEN\line }{\insrsid30033 The Perfect Society: Four Social Classes
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.11 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
This chapter describes the general principles by following which a human being, and specifically one who is interested in advancing in spiritual life, can become perfect.
\par By hearing about the characteristics of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira became extremely pleased. Now he inquired from N\'e4rada Muni about the actual religion of a human being and about special characteristics of }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{\insrsid30033  which marks the highest status of human civilization. When Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira asked N\'e4rada Muni about these matters, N\'e4
rada Muni stopped giving his own statements and quoted statements by Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, for He is the supreme authority for giving religious codes (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 dharma\'e0 tu s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d bhagavat-pra\'eb\'e9tam}{\insrsid30033 
). Every human being is expected to acquire thirty qualities, such as truthfulness, mercy and austerity. The process of following the priniples of religion is known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 san\'e4tana-dharma,}{\insrsid30033  the eternal 
religious system.
\par The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama}{\insrsid30033  system delineates the divisions of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdra.}{\insrsid30033 
 It also sets forth the system of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 sa\'e0sk\'e4ras.}{\insrsid30033  The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na sa\'e0sk\'e4ra,}{\insrsid30033  the ceremony for begetting a child, must be observed by the higher section of pe
ople, namely the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 dvijas.}{\insrsid30033  One who follows the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na sa\'e0sk\'e4ra}{\insrsid30033  system is actually twice-born, but those who do not, who deviate from the principles of }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{\insrsid30033  are called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 dvija-bandhus.}{\insrsid30033  The principal occupations for a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid30033  are worshiping t
he Deity, teaching others how to worship the Deity, studying the Vedic literatures, teaching the Vedic literatures, accepting charity from others and again giving charity to others. A }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid30033 
 should make his livelihood from these six occupational duties. The duty of a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriya}{\insrsid30033  is to give protection to the citizens and levy taxes upon them, but he is forbidden to tax the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br
\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\insrsid30033  The members of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement should therefore be exempt from government taxation. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 K\'f1atriyas}{\insrsid30033  may tax everyone but the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma
\'ebas.}{\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 Vai\'e7yas}{\insrsid30033  should cultivate the land, produce food grains and protect the cows, whereas the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdras,}{\insrsid30033  who by quality never become }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas}{\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 vai\'e7yas,}{\insrsid30033  should serve the three higher classes and be satisfied. Other means of livelihood are also prescribed for the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\insrsid30033  and these are four}{\insrsid10778242 \emdash }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4l\'e9na, y\'e4y\'e4vara, \'e7ila,}{\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 u\'efchana.}{\insrsid30033 
 Each of these occupational duties is successively better.
\par One who is in a lower grade of social life cannot accept the profession of a higher class unless necessary. In times of emergency, all the classes but the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas}{\insrsid30033 
 may accept professional duties of others. The means of livelihood known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e5ta}{\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7ilo\'efchana}{\insrsid30033 ), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 am\'e5ta}{\insrsid30033  (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ay\'e4cita}{\insrsid30033 ), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 m\'e5ta}{\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 y\'e4c\'ef\'e4}{\insrsid30033 ), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 pram\'e5ta}{\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 kar\'f1a\'eba}{
\insrsid30033 ), and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 saty\'e4n\'e5ta}{\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 v\'e4\'ebijya}{\insrsid30033 ) may be accepted by everyone but the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas.}{\insrsid30033  For a }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid30033  or a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriya,}{\insrsid30033  engaging in the service of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 vai\'e7yas}{\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdras}{\insrsid30033 
 is considered the profession of dogs.
\par N\'e4rada Muni also described that the symptom of a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid30033  is controlled senses, the symptoms of a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriya}{\insrsid30033  are power and fame, the symptom of a }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 vai\'e7ya}{\insrsid30033  is service to the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas,}{\insrsid30033  and the symptom of a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdra}{
\insrsid30033  is service to the three higher classes. The qualification for a woman is to be a very faithful and chaste wife. In this way, N\'e4rada Muni described the
 characteristics of higher and lower grades of people and recommended that one follow the principles of his caste or his hereditary occupation. One cannot suddenly give up a profession to which he is accustomed, and therefore it is recommended that one gr
adually be awakened. The symptoms of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas,}{\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdras}{\insrsid30033 
 are very important, and therefore one should be designated only by these symptoms, and not by birth. Designation by birth is strictly forbidden by N\'e4rada Muni and all great personalities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.11.1
