My dear lord, I wish to hear from you about the principles of religion by which one can attain the ultimate goal of life\emdash devotional service. I wish to hear about the general occupational duties of human so
ciety and the system of social and spiritual advancement known as var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 San\'e4tana-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means devotional service. The word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 san\'e4tana}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to that which is eternal, which does not change but continues in all circumstances. We have seve
ral times explained what the eternal occupational duty of the living being is. Indeed, it has been explained by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 J\'e9vera 'svar\'fcpa' haya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid14440980 \emdash }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e5\'f1\'ebera 'nitya-d\'e4sa': }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 the real occupational duty of the living entity is to serve the Supreme Per
sonality of Godhead. Even if one prefers to deviate from this principle he remains a servant because that is his eternal position; but one serves }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the illusory, material energy. The K
\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement, therefore, is an attempt to guide human society to serving the Personality of Godhead instead of serving the material world with no real profit. Our actual experience is that every man, animal, bird and beast\emdash 
indeed, every living entity\emdash is engaged in rendering service. Even though one's body or
 one's superficial religion may change, every living entity is always engaged in the service of someone. Therefore, the mentality of service is called the eternal occupational duty. This eternal occupational duty can be organized through the institution o
f }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  in which there are four }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 var\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) and four }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4\'e7ramas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahmacarya, g\'e5hastha, v\'e4
naprastha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Thus, Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira Mah\'e4r\'e4ja inquired from N\'e4rada Muni about the principles of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 san\'e4
tana-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  for the benefit of human society.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.11.3
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 3
