d bhagavat-pra\'eb\'e9tam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Yamar\'e4ja, the representative of the Lord who takes care of the living beings after their death, gives his verdict as to how and when the living being will change his body. He is the 
authority, and he says that the religious principles consist of the codes and laws given by God. No one can manufacture religion, and therefore manufactured religious systems are rejected by the followers of the Vedic principles. In }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (15.15) it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Vedic knowledge means to understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore, whether one speaks of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vedas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 scriptures, religion or the principles of everyone's occupational duty, all of them must aim at understanding K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (1.2.6) therefore concludes:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa vai pu\'e0s\'e4\'e0 paro dharmo\line yato bhaktir adhok\'f1aje\line ahaituky apratihat
\'e4\line yay\'e4tm\'e4 supras\'e9dati
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 In other words, religious principles aim at learning h
