e questions are bona fide the answers are bona fide. No one should attempt to create or manufacture answers. One must refer to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 and give answers according to Vedic understanding. The words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yath\'e4-\'e7rutam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refer to Vedic knowledge. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  are known as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7ruti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  because this knowledge is received from authorities. The statements of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  are known as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
\'e7ruti-pram\'e4\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  One should quote evidence from the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7ruti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or Vedic literature\emdash 
and then one's statements will be correct. Otherwise one's words will proceed from mental concoction.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.13.24
