es due to undesirable material sense gratification, I have received this human form of life, which can lead to the heavenly planets, to liberation, to the lower species, or to rebirth among human beings.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 All living entities within this material wor
ld are undergoing the cycle of birth and death according to the laws of nature. This struggle of birth and death in different species may be called the evolutionary process, but in the Western world it has been wrongly explained. Darwin's theory of evolut
i
on from animal to man is incomplete because the theory does not present the reverse condition, namely evolution from man to animal. In this verse, however, evolution has been very well explained on the strength of Vedic authority. Human life, which is obt
ained in the course of the evolutionary process, is a chance for elevation (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 svarg\'e4pavarga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) or for degradation (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tira\'e7c\'e4m punar asya ca}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). If one uses this human form of life properly, he can elevate himself to the higher planetary systems, where material happ
iness is many thousands of times better than on this planet, or one may cultivate knowledge by which to become free from the evolutionary process and be reinstated in one's original spiritual life. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
apavarga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or liberation.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Material life is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pavarga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 because here we are subject to five different states of suffering, represented by the letters }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pa, pha, ba, bha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Pa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pari\'e7rama,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  very hard labor. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Pha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 phena,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or foam from the mouth. For example, sometimes we see a horse foaming at the mouth with heavy labor. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Ba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 byarthat\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  disappointment. In spite of so much hard labor, at the end we find disappointment. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhaya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or fear. In material life, one is always in the blazing fire of fear, since no one knows what will happen next. Finally, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e5tyu,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or death. When one attempts to nullify these five different statuses of life\emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pa, pha, ba, bha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash one achieves }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 apavarga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or liberation from the punishment of material existence.
\par The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tira\'e7c\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refers to degraded life.
 Human life, of course, provides an opportunity for the best living conditions. As Western people think, from the monkeys come the human beings, who are more comfortably situated. However, if one does not utilize his human life for }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 svarga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 apavarga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  he f
alls again to the degraded life of animals like dogs and hogs. Therefore a sane human being must consider whether he will elevate himself to the higher planets, prepare to free himself from the evolutionary process, or travel again through the evolutionar
y
 process in higher and lower grades of life. If one works piously one may be elevated to the higher planetary systems or achieve liberation and return home, back to Godhead, but otherwise one may be degraded to a life as a dog, a hog and so on. As explain
ed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (9.25), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 y\'e4nti deva-vrat\'e4 dev\'e4n.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Those interested in being elevated to the higher planetary systems (Devaloka or Svargaloka) must prepare to do so. Similarly, if one wants liberation and wants to return home, back to Godhead, he should prepare himself for that purpose.
\par Our K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is therefore the highest movement for the benediction of human society because this movement is teaching people how to go back home, back to Godhead. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (13.22) it is clearly stated that different forms of life are obtained by association with the three modes of material nature (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e4ra\'eba\'e0 gu\'eba-sa\'ecgo 'sya sad-asad-yoni janmasu}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). According to one's association with the material qualities of goodness, passion and ignorance in this lif
e, in one's next life one receives an appropriate body. Modern civilization does not know that because of varied association in material nature, the living entity, although eternal, is placed in different diseased conditions known as the many species of l
ife. Modern civilization is unaware of the laws of nature.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prak\'e5te\'f9 kriyam\'e4\'eb\'e4ni\line gu\'ebai\'f9 karm\'e4\'ebi sarva\'e7a\'f9\line aha
\'eck\'e4ra-vim\'fc\'f2h\'e4tm\'e4\line kart\'e4ham iti manyate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"The bewildered spirit soul, under the influence of the three modes of material nature, thinks himself the perfo
rmer of activities that are in actuality carried out by nature." (Bg. 3.27) Every living entity is under the full control of the stringent laws of material nature, but rascals think themselves independent. Actually, however, they cannot be independent. Th
is is foolishness. A foolish civilization is extremely risky, and therefore the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement is trying to make people aware of their fully dependent condition under the stringent laws of nature and is trying to save them from being victimized by strong }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 which is K\'e5\'f1\'eba's external energy. Behind the material laws is the supreme controller, K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 may\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9 s\'fcyate sacar\'e4caram}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
). Therefore if one surrenders unto K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4m eva ye prapadyante m\'e4y\'e4m et\'e4\'e0 taranti te}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ), one may immediately be freed from the control of external nature (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa gu\'eb\'e4n samat\'e9tyait\'e4n brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). This should be the aim of life.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.13.26
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 26
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s489\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f75\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 Ta\}aaiPa dMPaTaqNaa& c Sau%aYaaNYaaPaNautaYae )\line k-MaaRi<a ku-vRTaa& d*\'ee
a iNav*taae_iSMa ivPaYaRYaMa( )) 26 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 tatr\'e4pi dam-pat\'e9n\'e4\'e0 ca
\par sukh\'e4y\'e4ny\'e4panuttaye
\par karm\'e4\'ebi kurvat\'e4\'e0 d\'e5\'f1\'f6v\'e4
\par niv\'e5tto 'smi viparyayam
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tatra}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash there; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 api}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash also; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dam-pat\'e9n\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of men and women united by marriage; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ca}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash and; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sukh\'e4ya}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash for the sake of pleasure, specifically the pleasure of sex life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 anya-apanuttaye}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash for avoiding misery; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 karm\'e4\'ebi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash fruitive activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kurvat\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash always engaged in; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 d\'e5\'f1\'f6v\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by observing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 niv\'e5tta\'f9
 asmi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash I have now ceased (from such activities); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 viparyayam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the opposite.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 In this human form of life, men and women
 unite for the sensual pleasure of sex, but by actual experience we have observed that none of them are happy. Therefore, seeing the contrary results, I have stopped taking part in materialistic activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 As stated by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yan maithun\'e4di-g
\'e5hamedhi-sukha\'e0 hi tuccham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Man and woman both seek sexual enjoyment, and when they are united by the ritualistic ceremony of marriage, they are happy for some time, but finally there is dissension, and thus there are so many cases of separation and
 divorce. Although every man and woman is actually eager to enjoy life through sexual unity, the result is disunity and distress. Marriage is recommended to give men and women a concession for restricted sex life, which is also recommended in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Dharm\'e4viruddho bh\'fcte\'f1u k\'e4mo 'smi:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 sex life not against the principles of religion is K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Every living entity is always eager to enjoy sex life because materialistic life consists of eating, sleeping, sex and fear.
 In animal life, eating, sleeping, sexual enjoyment and fear cannot be regulated, but for human society the plan is that although men, like animals, must be allowed to eat, sleep, enjoy sex and take protection from fear, they must be regulated. The Vedic 
plan for eating recommends that one take }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa-\'e7i\'f1\'f6a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pras\'e4da,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  food offered to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yaj\'efa-\'e7i\'f1\'f6\'e4\'e7ina\'f9 santo mucyante }{\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-kilbi\'f1ai\'f9}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 :}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 "The devotees of the Lord are released from all kinds of sins because they eat food that is offered first for sacrifice
." (Bg. 3.13) In material life, one commits sinful activities, especially in eating, and because of sinful activities one is condemned by nature's laws to accept another body, which is imposed as punishment. Sex and eating are essential, and therefore the
y
 are offered to human society under Vedic restrictions so that according to the Vedic injunctions people may eat, sleep, enjoy sex, be protected from fearful life and gradually be elevated and liberated from the punishment of material existence. Thus the 
V
edic injunctions for marriage offer a concession to human society, the idea being that a man and woman united in a ritualistic marriage ceremony should help one another advance in spiritual life. Unfortunately, especially in this age, men and women unite 
for unrestricted sexual enjoyment. Thus they are victimized, being obliged to take rebirth in the forms of animals to fulfill their animalistic propensities. The Vedic injunctions therefore warn, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e4ya\'e0 deho deha-bh
\'e4j\'e4\'e0 n\'e5loke ka\'f1\'f6\'e4n k\'e4m\'e4n arhate vid-bhuj\'e4\'e0 ye.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  One should not enjoy sex life like hogs, and eat everything, even to the limit of stool. A human being should eat }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
pras\'e4da}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  offered to the Deity and should enjoy sex life according to the Vedic injunctions. He should engage himself in the business of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, he should save himself from the fearful condition of material existence, and he should sleep only to recover from fatigue due to working hard.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The learned }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 said that since everything is misused by fruitive workers, he had retired from all fruitive activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.13.27
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 27
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
