a >aaeGaaNSvPSYaaiMa Sa&ivXaNa( )) 27 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 sukham asy\'e4tmano r\'fcpa\'e0
\par sarvehoparatis tanu\'f9
\par mana\'f9-sa\'e0spar\'e7aj\'e4n d\'e5\'f1\'f6v\'e4
\par bhog\'e4n svapsy\'e4mi sa\'e0vi\'e7an
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sukham}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash happiness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
asya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of him; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4tmana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of the living entity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 r\'fcpam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the natural position; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
sarva}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash all; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9ha}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash material activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 uparati\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash completely stopping; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tanu\'f9}
{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the medium of its manifestation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mana\'f9-sa\'e0spar\'e7a-j\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash produced from demands for sense gratification; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 d\'e5\'f1\'f6v\'e4}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash after seeing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhog\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash sense enjoyment; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 svapsy\'e4mi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
I am sitting silently, thinking deeply about these material activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa\'e0vi\'e7an}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash entering into such activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 The actual form of life for the living entities is one of
 spiritual happiness, which is real happiness. This happiness can be achieved only when one stops all materialistic activities. Material sense enjoyment is simply imagination. Therefore, considering this subject matter, I have ceased from all material act
ivities and am lying down here.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The difference between the philosophy of the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s and that of the Vai\'f1\'eb
avas is explained herein. Both the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s and Vai\'f1\'ebavas know that in materialistic activities there is no happiness. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers, therefore, adhering to the slogan }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
brahma satya\'e0 jagan mithy\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  want to refrain from false, materialistic activities. They want to stop all activities and merge in the Supreme Brahman. According to the Vai\'f1\'ebava philosophy, however, if one simply ceases
 from materialistic activity one cannot remain inactive for very long, and therefore everyone should engage himself in spiritual activities, which will solve the problem of suffering in this material world. It is said, therefore, that although the M\'e4y
\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers strive to refrain from materialistic activities and merge in Brahman, and although they may actually merge in the Brahman existence, for want of activity they fall down again into materialistic activity (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4ruhya k\'e5cchre\'eba para\'e0 pada\'e0 tata\'f9 patanty adha\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
). Thus the so-called renouncer, unable to remain in meditation upon Brahman, returns to materialistic activities by opening hospitals and schools and so on. Therefore, simply cultivating knowledge that materialistic activities cannot give one ha
ppiness, and that one should consequently cease from such activities, is insufficient. One should cease from materialistic activities and take up spiritual activities. Then the solution to the problem will be achieved. Spiritual activities are activities 
performed according to the order of K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4nuk\'fclyena k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4nu\'e7\'e9lanam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). If one does whatever K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a says, his activities are not material. For example, when Arjuna fought in response to the order of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, his activities were not material. Fighting for sense gratification is a materialistic activity, but fighting by the order of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is spiritual. By spiritual activities one becomes eligible to go back home, back to Godhead, and then enjoy blissful life eternally. Here, in the material world, everything is bu
t a mental concoction that will never give us real happiness. The practical solution, therefore, is to cease from materialistic activities and engage in spiritual activities. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'eb
o 'nyatra loko 'ya\'e0 karma-bandhana\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 )}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 .}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  If one works for the sake of pleasing the Supreme Lord\emdash Yaj\'efa, or Vi\'f1\'ebu\emdash 
one is in liberated life. If one fails to do so, however, he remains in a life of bondage.
