s distinctly stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  because one has not surrendered to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he must work under the control of material nature and its stringent laws (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid9118762 \'e4 gu\'eba-may\'e9 mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). The only means of becoming fr
ee from this entanglement is to surrender to the Supreme Lord. In the human form of life, the living entity must accept this instruction from the Supreme Person, K\'e5\'f1\'eba: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 
\'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  "Do not plan to achieve happiness and 
drive away distress. You will never be successful. Simply surrender unto Me." Unfortunately, however, the living entity does not accept the Supreme Lord's clearly stated instructions from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and thus he becomes a perpetual captive of the laws of material nature.
\par }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'ebo 'nyatra loko 'ya\'e0 karma-bandhana\'f9:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 if one does not act for the satisfaction of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who is known as Vi\'f1\'eb
u or Yaj\'efa, he must be entangled in the reactions of fruitive activities. These reactions are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 p\'e4pa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pu\'ebya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash 
sinful and pious. By pious activities one is elevated to the higher planetary systems, and by impious activities one is degraded to lower species of life, in which he is punished by the laws of nature. In the lower species of life there is an evolution
ary process, and when the term of the living entity's imprisonment or punishment in the lower species is finished, he is again offered a human form and given a chance to decide for himself which way he should plan. If he again misses the opportunity, he i
s again put into the cycle of birth and death, going sometimes higher and sometimes lower, turning on the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa\'e0s\'e4ra-cakra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the wheel of material existence. As a wheel sometimes goes up and sometimes comes down, the stringent laws of material nature make the l
iving entity in material existence sometimes happy and sometimes distressed. How he suffers in the cycle of happiness and distress is described in the next verse.
