\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 adhy\'e4tmika, adhidaivika}{\fs28\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 adhibhautika;}{\fs28\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 du\'f9khai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by the threefold miseries of mate
rial life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 avimuktasya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of one who is not freed from such miserable conditions (or one who is subjected to birth, death, old age and disease); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 karhicit}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash sometimes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 martyasya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of the living entity subjected to death; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e5cchra-upanatai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash things obtained because o
f severe miseries; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 arthai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash even if some benefit is derived; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'e4mai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash which can fulfill one's material desires; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kriyeta}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash what do they do; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kim}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash and what is the value of such happiness.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
