\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "When one is not attached to anything, but at the same time accepts everything in relation to K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, one is rightly situated above possessiveness." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5ta-sindhu}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 1.2.255) Money is undoubtedly coming in great quantities, but we should not be attached to this money for sense gratification; every cent should be spent for spreading the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness mov
ement, not for sense gratification. There is danger for a preacher when he receives great quantities of money, for as soon as he spends even a single cent of the collection for his personal sense gratification, he becomes a fallen victim. The preachers of
 the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement should be extremely careful not to misuse the immense quantities of money needed to spread this movement. Let us not make this money the cause of our distress; it should be used for K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, and that will cause our eternal happiness. Money is Lak\'f1m\'e9, or the goddess of fortune, the companion of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9 must always remain with N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and then there need be no fear of degradation.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.13.33
