 were also happy, for they would get food and shelter from the three higher classes. In the demoniac civilization of the present day, however, there is no question of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1atriyas;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  there are only so-called workers and a flourishing mercantile class who have no goal in life.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 According to Vedic civilization, the ultimate perfection of life is to take }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  but at the present moment people do not know why }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 is accepted. Because of misunderstanding, they think that one accepts }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  to escape social responsibilities. But one does not accept }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  to escape from responsibility to society. Generally one accepts }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  at the fourth stage of spiritual life. One begins as a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahmac
\'e4r\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  then becomes a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 v\'e4naprastha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and finally a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4
