f it should be invested in printing books, and fifty per cent for expenditures, especially in establishing centers all over the world. The managers of the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement should be extremely cautious in regard to this point. Otherwise money will be the cause of lamentation, illusion, fear, anger, material attachment, material poverty, and unnecessary hard work. When I was alone in V\'e5nd\'e4
