tire constitution of the body, one can surely come to the conclusion that the soul is different from all the body's material constituents, such as earth, water, fire and air. Thus the difference between the body and soul can be realized by a person who is
 thoughtful (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 man\'e9\'f1\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 muni}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
), and after this realization of the individual spirit soul one can very easily understand the supreme spirit soul. If one thus realizes that the individual soul is subordinate to the supreme spirit soul, he achieves self-realizat
ion. As explained in the Thirteenth Chapter of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  there are two souls within the body. The body is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1etra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 and there are two }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'f1etra j\'efas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or occupants of the body, namely the Supersoul (Param\'e4tm\'e4) and the individual soul. The Supersoul a
nd the individual soul are like two birds sitting on the same tree (the material body). One bird, the individual, forgetful bird, is eating the fruit of the tree, not caring for the instructions of the other bird, which is only a witness to the activities
 of the first bird, who is his friend. When the forgetful bird comes to understand the supreme friend who is always with him and trying to give him guidance in different bodies, he takes shelter at the lotus feet of that supreme bird. As explained in the 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  process, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dhy\'e4n\'e4vasthita-tad-gatena manas\'e4 pa\'e7yanti ya\'e0 yogina\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  When one actually becomes a perfect }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yog\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  by meditation he can see the supreme friend and surrender unto Him. This is the beginning of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or actual life in K\'e5
\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.13.45
