\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 
This chapter describes the occupational duties of the householder according to the time, the country and the performer. When Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira Mah\'e4r\'e4ja became very much inquisitive about the occupational duties for the householder, N\'e4
rada Muni advised him that a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha's}{\insrsid30033  first duty is to be fully dependent on V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and to try to satisfy Him in all respects by executing one's 
prescribed devotional service. This devotional service will depend on the instructions of authorities and the association of devotees who are actually engaged in devotional service. The beginning of devotional service is }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7rava
\'ebam,}{\insrsid30033  or hearing. One must hear from the mouths of realized souls. In this way the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha's}{\insrsid30033  attraction to his wife and children will gradually be reduced.
\par As for the maintenance of his family, a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha,}{\insrsid30033  while earning what he requires for his living, must be very conscientious and mu
st not undergo extraordinary endeavor simply to accumulate money and unnecessarily increase in material comforts. Although a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033 
 should externally be very active in earning his livelihood, he should internally be situated as a fully self-realized pers
on, without attachment for material gains. His dealings with family members or friends should be performed simply to fulfill their purpose; one should not be extravagantly engaged in this way. Instructions from family members and society should be accepte
d superficially, but in essence the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  should be engaged in occupational duties advised by the spiritual master and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stra.}{\insrsid30033  Specifically a }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  should engage in agricultural activities to earn money. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 }{\insrsid30033 (18.44), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 k\'e5\'f1i-go-rak\'f1ya-v\'e4\'ebijyam}{
\insrsid2782620 \emdash }{\insrsid30033 agriculture, cow protection and trade}{\insrsid2782620 \emdash }{\insrsid30033 are special duties of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hasthas.}{\insrsid30033 
 If by chance or by the grace of the Lord more money comes, it should be properly engaged for the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement. One should not be eager to earn more money simply for sensual pleasure. A }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{
\insrsid30033  should always remember that one who is endeavoring to accumulate more money than necessary is to be considered a thief and is punishable by the laws of nature.
\par A }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  should be very much affectionate toward lower animals, birds and bees, treating them exactly like his own children. A }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033 
 should not indulge in killing animals or birds for sense gratification. He should provide the necessities of life even to the dogs and the lowest creatures and should not explo
it others for sense gratification. Factually, according to the instructions of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\insrsid30033  every }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033 
 is a great communist who provides the means of living for everyone. Whatever a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  may possess he should equally distribute to all living 
entities, without discrimination. The best process is to distribute }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 pras\'e4da.
\par }{\insrsid30033 A }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  should not be very much attached to his wife; he should engage even his own wife in serving a guest with all attention. Whatever money a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{
\insrsid30033  accumulates by the grace of God he should spend in five activities, namely worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, receiving Vai\'f1\'ebavas and saintly persons, distributing }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 pras\'e4da}{\insrsid30033 
 to the general public and to all living entities, offering }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 pras\'e4da}{\insrsid30033  to his forefathers, and also offering }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 pras\'e4da}{\insrsid30033  to his own self. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 G\'e5
hasthas}{\insrsid30033  should always be ready to worship everyone as mentioned above. The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  should not eat anything not offered to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As it is said in the }{
\cs2542\i\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid30033  (3.13), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa-\'e7i\'f1\'f6\'e4\'e7ina\'f9 santo mucyante sarva-kilbi\'f1ai\'f9:}{\insrsid30033 
 "The devotees of the Lord are released from all kinds of sins because they eat food that is offered first for sacrifice." The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{\insrsid30033  should also visit the holy places of pilgrimage mentioned in the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid2782620 P}{\cs1998\i\insrsid30033 ur\'e4\'ebas.}{\insrsid30033  In this way he should fully engage in worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead for the benefit of his family, his society, his country, and humanity at large.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.14.1
