van bhagavato 'bh\'e9k\'f1\'ebam avat\'e4ra-kath\'e4m\'e5tam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  It is not that because one has once finished }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  he should not hear it again. The word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 abh\'e9k\'f1\'ebam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is very important. We should hear again and again. There is no question of stopping: even if one has read these topics many times, he should go on reading again and again because 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhagavat-kath\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the words spoken by K\'e5\'f1\'eba and spoken by K\'e5\'f1\'eba's devotees about K\'e5\'f1\'eba, are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 am\'e5tam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 nectar. The more one drinks this }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 am\'e5tam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the more he advances in his eternal life.
\par The human form of life is meant for liberation, but unfortunately, due to the influence of Kali-yuga, every day the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 g\'e5hasthas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 are working hard like asses. Early in the morning they rise and travel even a hundred miles away to earn bread. Especially in the Western countries, I have seen that people awaken at five o'clock to go to o
ffices and factories to earn their livelihood. People in Calcutta and Bombay also do this every day. They work very hard in the office or factory, and again they spend three or four hours in transportation returning home. Then they retire at ten o'clock a
nd again rise early in the morning to go to their offices and factories. This kind of hard labor is described in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  as the life of pigs and stool-eaters. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 N\'e4ya\'e0 deho deha-bh\'e4j\'e4\'e0 n\'e5loke ka\'f1\'f6\'e4n k\'e4m\'e4n arhate vid-bhuj\'e4\'e0 ye:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Of all living entities who h
ave accepted material bodies in this world, one who has been awarded this human form should not work hard day and night simply for sense gratification, which is available even for dogs and hogs that eat stool." }{
\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5139582\charrsid5139582 (Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  5.5.1) One must find some time for hearing }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  This is Vedic culture. One should work eight hours at the most to earn his livelihood, and either in the afternoon or in the evening a householder should associate with devotees to hear about the incarnations of K\'e5
\'f1\'eba and His activities and thus be gradually liberated from the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  However, instead of finding time to hear about K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the householders, after working hard in offices and factories, find time to go to a restaurant or a club where instead of hearing about K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and His activities they are very much pleased to hear about the political activities of demons and nondevotees and to enjoy sex, wine, women and meat and in this way waste their time. This is not }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 g\'e5hastha}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  life, but demoniac life. The K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement, however, with its centers all over the world, gives such fallen and condemned persons an opportunity to hear about K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par In a dream we form a society of friendship and love, and when we awaken we see that it has ceased to exi
st. Similarly, one's gross society, family and love are also a dream, and this dream will be over as soon as one dies. Therefore, whether one is dreaming in a subtle way or a gross way, these dreams are all false and temporary. One's real business is to u
nderstand that one is soul (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 aha\'e0 brahm\'e4smi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ) and that his activities should therefore be different. Then one can be happy.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4\line na \'e7ocati na k\'e4\'eck\'f1ati\line sama\'f9
