a is incomplete in his renunciation." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5ta-sindhu}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  1.2.256) Although M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9
 philosophers say that the material creation is false, actually it is not false; it is factual, but the idea that everything belongs to hum
an society is false. Everything belongs to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, for everything is created by Him. All living entities, being the Lord's sons, His eternal parts and parcels, have the right to use their father's property by nature's arrangeme
nt. As stated in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Upani\'f1ads, tena tyaktena bhu\'efj\'e9th\'e4 m\'e4 g\'e5dha\'f9 kasya svid dhanam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Everyone should be satisfied with the things allotted him by the Supreme Personality of Godhead; no one should encroach upon another's rights or property.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  it is said:

