d bhavati parjanyo\line yaj\'efa\'f9 karma-samudbhava\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"All living bodies subsist on food grains, which are produced from rains. Rains are produced by performance of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  [sacrifice], and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is born of prescribed duties." (Bg. 3.14) When food grains are sufficiently produced, both animals and human beings can be nourished without difficulty for their maintenance. This is nature's arrangement. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10832162 P}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 rak\'e5te\'f9 kriyam\'e4\'eba-ni gu\'ebai\'f9 karm\'e4\'ebi sarva\'e7a\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Everyone is
 acting under the influence of material nature, and only fools think they can improve upon what God has created. The householders are specifically responsible for seeing that the laws of the Supreme Personality of Godhead are maintained, without fighting 
between men, communities, societies or nations. Human society should properly utilize the gifts of God, especially the food grains that grow because of rain falling from the sky. As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'ef\'e4d bhavati parjanya\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  So that rainfall will be regulated, humanity should perform }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 sacrifices. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Yaj\'efas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 were previously performed with offerings of oblations of ghee and food grains, but in this age, of course, this is no longer possible, for the production of ghee and food grains has diminished 
because of the sinful life of human society. However, people should take to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness and chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mantra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  as recommended in the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efai\'f9 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-pr\'e4yair yajanti hi sumedhasa\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). If people throughout the world take to the K\'e5\'f1
\'eb
a consciousness movement and chant the easy sound vibration of the transcendental name and fame of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, there will be no scarcity of rainfall; consequently food grains, fruits and flowers will be properly produced, and all 
the necessities of life will be easily obtained. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 G\'e5hasthas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or householders, should take the responsibility for organizing such natural production. It is therefore said, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tasyaiva heto\'f9 prayateta kovida\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  An intelligent person should try to spread K\'e5\'f1\'eba con
sciousness through the chanting of the holy name of the Lord, and all the necessities of life will automatically follow.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.14.8
