By God's favor we sometimes get large quantities of food grains or suddenly receive some contribution or unexpected profit in business. In this
 way we may get more money than needed. So, how should that be spent? There is no need to accumulate money in the bank merely to increase one's bank balance. Such a mentality is described in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (16.13) as asuric, demoniac.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 idam adya may\'e4 labdham\line ima\'e0 pr\'e4psye manoratham\line idam ast\'e9dam api me
\line bhavi\'f1yati punar dhanam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"The demoniac person thinks, 'So much wealth do I have today, and I will gain more according to my schemes. So much is mine now, and it will increase in the future, more and more.' " The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asura}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 is concerned with how much wealth he has in the bank today and how it will increase tomorrow, but unrestricted accumulation of wealth is not permitted either by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 or, in the modern age, by the government. Actually, if one has more than one requires for his necessities, the extra money should be spent for K\'e5\'f1\'eba. According to the Vedic civilization, it should all be given to the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement, as ordered by the Lord Himself in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (9.27):
