 means "path" or "going." The six months when the sun moves toward the north are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 uttar\'e4ya\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or the northern path, and the six months when it moves south are called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dak\'f1i\'eb\'e4yana,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or the southern path. These are mentioned in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (8.24-25). The first day when the sun begins to move north and enter the zodiacal sign of Capricorn is called Makara-sa\'eckr\'e4nti, and the first day when the sun begins to move south and enter the sign of Cancer is called Karka\'f6a-sa\'eckr\'e4
nti. On these two days of the year, one should perform the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7r\'e4ddha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  ceremony.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vi\'f1uva, or Vi\'f1uva-sa\'eckr\'e4nti, means Me\'f1a-sa\'eckr\'e4
nti, or the day on which the sun enters the sign Aries. Tul\'e4-sa\'eckr\'e4nti is the day on which the sun enters the sign Libra. Both of these days occur only once within a year. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 refers to a certain relationship between the sun and moon as they move in the sky. There are twenty-seven different degrees of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yoga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  of which the seventeenth is called Vyat\'e9p\'e4
ta. On the day when this occurs, one should perform the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7r\'e4ddha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  ceremony. A }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tithi,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 or lunar day, consists of the distance between the longitude of the sun and that of the moon. Sometimes a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tithi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 is less than twenty-four hours. When it starts after sunrise on a certain day and ends before the sunrise of the following day, the previous }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tithi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and the following }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tithi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  both "touch" the twenty-four-hour day between the sunrises. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tryaha-spar\'e7a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 or a day touched by some portion of three }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tithis.
