When one comes to the human form of life through natural evolution, one must then take the responsibility for further progress. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (9.25), }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 y\'e4nti deva-vrat\'e4 dev\'e4n:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  one who worships the demigods can be promoted to their planets. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Y\'e4nti mad-y\'e4jino 'pi m\'e4m:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 and if one practices devotional service to the Lord, he goes back home, back to Godhead. In the human form of l
ife, therefore, one is meant to act auspiciously in order to return home, back to Godhead. Devotional service, however, does not depend on material conditions. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Ahaituky apratihat\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
