\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is more powerful than Deity worship. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu set a practical example in that He did not establish any temples or Deities, but He profusely introduced the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa\'eck\'e9rtana}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  movement. Therefore K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness preachers should give more stress to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa\'eck\'e9rtana}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 movement, especially by distributing transcendental literature more and more. This helps the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa\'eck\'e9rtana}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  movement. Whenever there is a possibility to worship the Deity, we may establish
 many centers, but generally we should give more stress to the distribution of transcendental literature, for this will be more effective in converting people to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par It is said in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (11.2.47):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 arc\'e4y\'e4m eva haraye\line p\'fcj\'e4\'e0 ya\'f9 \'e7raddhayehate\line na tad-bhakte\'f1
u c\'e4nye\'f1u\line sa bhakta\'f9 pr\'e4k\'e5ta\'f9 sm\'e5ta\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"A person who is very faithfully engaged in the worship of the Deity in the temple but does not know how to behave toward devotees or people in general is called a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pr\'e4k\'e5ta-bhakta,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kani\'f1\'f6ha-adhik\'e4r\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 " A }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 pr\'e4k\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 devotee, or neophyte devotee, is still on the material platform. He certainly engages in worshiping the Deity, but he cannot appreciate the activities of a pure devotee. It has actually been seen that even an authorized devotee who is 
engaged in the service of the Lord by preaching the mission of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness is sometimes criticized by neophyte devotees. Such neophytes are described by Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
sarva-pr\'e4\'ebi-samm\'e4nan\'e4samarth\'e4n\'e4m avaj\'ef\'e4 spardh\'e4dimat\'e4\'e0 tu bhagavat-pratimaiva p\'e4tram ity \'e4ha.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 For those who cannot properly appreciate the activities of authorized devotees, Deity worship is the only way for spiritual advancement. In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Antya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  7.11) it is clearly said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-\'e7akti vin\'e4 nahe t\'e4ra pravartana:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  without being authorized by K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, one cannot preach the holy name of the Lord throughout the entire world. Nevertheless, a devotee who does so is criticized by neophyte devotees, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 kani\'f1\'f6ha-adhik\'e4r\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 who are on the lower stages of devotional service. For them, Deity worship is strongly recommended.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.14.40
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 40
