 we learn that the Personality of Godhead is the Supreme Person. Every living entity is an individual person, and the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is the Supreme Person. A }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  who is well versed in Vedic knowledge and fully conversant with transcendental matters becomes a representative of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and therefore one should worship such a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4
hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or Vai\'f1\'ebava. A Vai\'f1\'ebava is superior to a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  because whereas a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 knows that he is Brahman, not matter, a Vai\'f1\'ebava knows that he is not only Brahman but also an eternal servant of the Supreme Brahman. Therefore, worship of a Vai\'f1\'ebava is superior to worship of the Deity in the temple. Vi\'e7van\'e4
tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d dharitvena samasta-\'e7\'e4strai\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  in all the scriptures the spiritual master, who is the best of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br
\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the best of the Vai\'f1\'ebavas, is considered to be as good as the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This does not mean, however, that the Vai\'f1\'ebava thinks himself God, for this is blasphemous. Although a }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or Vai\'f1\'eb
ava is worshiped as being as good as the Supreme Personality of Godhead, such a devotee always remains a faithful servant of the Lord and never tries to enjoy the prestige that might accrue to him from being the Supreme Lord's representative.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.14.42
