\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 As admitted by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (18.69), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 na ca tasm\'e4n manu\'f1ye\'f1u ka\'e7cin me priya-k\'e5ttama\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 preach the cult of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness all around the world, and therefore, although they worship K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Lord also recognizes them as worshipable. The relationship is reciprocal. The }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  want to worship K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and similarly K\'e5\'f1\'eba wants to worship the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 In conclusion, therefore, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and Vai\'f1\'ebavas who are engaged in preaching the glories of the Lord must be worshiped by religionists, philosophers and people in general. At the R
\'e4jas\'fcya-yaj\'efa of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira, many hundreds and thousands of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  were present, yet K\'e5\'f1\'eba was selected to be worshiped first. Therefore, K\'e5\'f1
\'eba is always the Supreme Person, but by His causeless mercy He recognizes the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  as dearmost to Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1178\ql \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Seventh Canto, Fourteenth Chapter, of the }{
