\fs28\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdra}{\fs28\insrsid30033 ); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dvi-j\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the twice-born (especially the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 ); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kecit}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash some; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tapa\'f9-ni\'f1\'f6h\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash very much attached to austerities and penances; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 n\'e5pa}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash O King; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 apare}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash others; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sv\'e4dhy\'e4ye}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in studying Vedic literature; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 anye}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash others; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pravacane}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash delivering speeches on Vedic literature; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kecana}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash some; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na-yogayo\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in culturing knowledge and practicing }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid30033 N\'e4rada Muni continued:}{\fs28\insrsid30033  My dear King, some br\'e4hma\'eb
as are very much attached to fruitive activities, some are attached to austerities and penances, and still others study the Vedic literature, whereas some, although very few, cultivate knowledge and practice different yogas, especially bhakti-yoga.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.15.2
