\par itarebhyo yath\'e4rhata\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na-ni\'f1\'f6h\'e4ya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
to the impersonalist or the transcendentalist desiring to merge into the Supreme; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dey\'e4ni}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash to be given in charity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 kavy\'e4ni}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
ingredients offered to the forefathers as oblations; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4nantyam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash liberation from material bondage; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 icchat\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by a person desiring; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 daive}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the ingredients to be offered to the demigods; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ca}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash also; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tat-abh\'e4ve}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
in the absence of such advanced transcendentalists; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sy\'e4t}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash it should be done; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 itarebhya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
to others (namely, those addicted to fruitive activities); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 yath\'e4-arhata\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash comparatively or with discrimination.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
A person desiring liberation for his forefathers or himself should give charity to a br\'e4hma\'eba who adheres to impersonal monism [j\'ef\'e4na-ni\'f1\'f6h\'e4]. In the absence of such an advanced br\'e4hma\'eba, charity may be given to a br\'e4hma\'eb
a addicted to fruitive activities [karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a].
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 There are two processes by which to get free from material bondage. One involves }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and the other involves }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 up\'e4san\'e4-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a.
}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Vai\'f1\'ebavas never want to merge into the existence of the Supreme; rather, they want to be everlastingly servants of the Lord to render loving service unto Him. In this verse the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4
nantyam icchat\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  refer to persons who desire to achieve liberation from material bondage and m
erge into the existence of the Lord. Devotees, however, whose objective is to associate personally with the Lord, have no desire to accept the activities of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  for pure devotional service is above both }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4
na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5721311 \'e4-\'e7\'fcnya\'e0 j\'ef\'e4na-karm\'e4dy-an\'e4v\'e5tam}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 .}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 In pure devotional service there is not even a pinch of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Consequently, when Vai\'f1\'eb
avas distribute charity, they do not need to find a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  performing the activities of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The best example in this regard is provided by Advaita Gosv\'e4m\'e9, who, after performing the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7r\'e4ddha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 ceremony for his father, offered charity to Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura, although it was known to everyone that Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura was born in a Mohammedan family, not a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 family, and was not interested in the activities of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
Charity, therefore, should be given to the first-class transcendentalist, the devotee, because the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'e4stras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  recommend:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mukt\'e4n\'e4m api siddh\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-par\'e4ya\'eba\'f9\line sudur
labha\'f9 pra\'e7\'e4nt\'e4tm\'e4\line ko\'f6i\'f1v api mah\'e4-mune
