\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  for he is situated in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "aha\'e0 brahm\'e4smi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 " position. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4 na \'e7ocati na k\'e4\'eck\'f1ati.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Such a person, who no longer laments or hankers to maintain his body and who can accept all living entities as spirit souls, can then enter the devotion
al service of the Lord. If one does not enter the devotional service of the Lord but artificially considers himself Brahman or N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, not perfectly understanding that the soul and body are different, one certainly falls down (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 patanty adha\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). Such a person again gives importance to the body. There are many }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4s\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 in India who stress the importance of the body. Some of them give special importance to the body of the poor man, accepting him as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  as if N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
