\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e7\'fcdra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Such }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4s\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  are considered the greatest rascals (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
asattam\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). They are shameless because they have not yet understood the difference between the body and the soul and instead have accepted the body of a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  to be a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Brahmanism (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
) consists of the knowledge of Brahman. But actually the body of a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is not Brahman. Similarly, the body is neither rich nor poor. If the body of a poor man were }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  this would mean that the body of a rich man, on the contrary, must be }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 dhan\'e9-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Therefore }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4s\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  who do not know the meaning of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, those who regard the body as Brahman or as N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, are described here as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asattam\'e4
\'f9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the most abominable rascals. Following the bodily concept of life, such }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sanny\'e4s\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
