\par hay\'e4n abh\'e9\'f1\'fcn mana indriye\'e7am
\par vartm\'e4ni m\'e4tr\'e4 dhi\'f1a\'eb\'e4\'e0 ca s\'fcta\'e0
\par sattva\'e0 b\'e5had bandhuram \'e9\'e7a-s\'e5\'f1\'f6am
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e4hu\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash it is said; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7ar\'e9ram}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the body; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ratham}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the chariot; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 indriy\'e4\'ebi}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the senses; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 hay\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the horses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 abh\'e9\'f1\'fcn}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the reins; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 mana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the mind; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 indriya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash of the senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7am}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the master; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vartm\'e4ni}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the destinations; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e4tr\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the sense objects; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dhi\'f1a\'eb\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the intelligence; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ca}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash and; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 s\'fctam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the chariot driver; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sattvam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash consciousness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 b\'e5hat}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash great; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 bandhuram}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash bondage; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e9\'e7a}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 s\'e5\'f1\'f6am}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash created.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
Transcendentalists who are advanced in knowledge compare the body, which is made by the order of the 
Supreme Personality of Godhead, to a chariot. The senses are like the horses; the mind, the master of the senses, is like the reins; the objects of the senses are the destinations; intelligence is the chariot driver; and consciousness, which spreads throu
ghout the body, is the cause of bondage in this material world.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
For a bewildered person in the materialistic way of life, the body, the mind and the senses, which are engaged in sense gratification, are the cause of bondage to repeated birth, death,
 old age and disease. But for one who is advanced in spiritual knowledge, the same body, senses and mind are the cause of liberation. This is confirmed in the }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Ka\'f6ha Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (1.3.3-4,9) as follows:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4na\'e0 rathina\'e0 viddhi\line \'e7ar\'e9ra\'e0 ratham eva ca\line buddhi\'e0
 tu s\'e4rathi\'e0 viddhi\line mana\'f9 pragraham eva ca
\par indriy\'e4\'ebi hay\'e4n \'e4hur\line vi\'f1ay\'e4\'e0s te\'f1u gocar\'e4n
\par so 'dhvana\'f9 p\'e4ram \'e4pnoti\line tad vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9 parama\'e0 padam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
The soul is the occupant of the chariot of the body, of which the driver is the intelligence. The mind is the determination t
o reach the destination, the senses are the horses, and the sense objects are also included in that activity. Thus one can reach the destination, Vi\'f1\'ebu, who is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 parama\'e0 padam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the supreme goal of life. In conditioned life the consciousness in the body is the cause of bondage, but the same consciousness, when transformed into K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, becomes the cause for one's returning home, back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The human body, therefore, may be used in two ways\emdash 
for going to the darkest regions of ignorance or for going forward, back home, back to Godhead. To go back to Godhead, the path is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mahat-sev\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  to accept the self-realized spiritual master. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Mahat-sev\'e4\'e0 dv\'e4ram \'e4hur vimukte\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  For liberation, one should accept the direction of authorized devotees who can actually endow one with perfect knowledge. On the other hand, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tamo-dv\'e4ra\'e0 yo\'f1it\'e4\'e0 sa\'ecgi-sa\'ecgam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  if one wants to go to the darkest regions of material existence, one may continue to associate with persons who are attached to women (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yo\'f1it\'e4\'e0 sa\'ecgi-sa\'ecgam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yo\'f1it}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  means "woman." Persons who are too materialistic are attached to women.
\par It is said, therefore, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4na\'e0 rathina\'e0 viddhi \'e7ar\'e9ra\'e0 ratham eva ca.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The body is just like a chariot or car in which one may go anywhere. One may drive well, or else 
one may drive whimsically, in which case it is quite possible that he may have an accident and fall into a ditch. In other words, if one takes directions from the experienced spiritual master one can go back home, back to Godhead; otherwise, one may retur
n to the cycle of birth and death. Therefore K\'e5\'f1\'eba personally advises:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 a\'e7raddadh\'e4n\'e4\'f9 puru\'f1\'e4\line dharmasy\'e4sya parantapa\line apr\'e4pya m\'e4
\'e0 nivartante\line m\'e5tyu-sa\'e0s\'e4ra-vartmani
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"Those who are not faithful on the path of devotional service cannot attain Me, O conqueror of foes, but return to birth and death in this material world." (Bg. 9.3) The Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, personally gives instructions on how one can return home, back to Godhead, but if one does not care to listen to His instructions, the result w
ill be that one will never go back to Godhead, but will continue life in this miserable condition of repeated birth and death in material existence (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e5tyu-sa\'e0s\'e4ra-vartmani}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The advice of experienced transcendentalists, therefore, is that the body be fully
 engaged for achieving the ultimate goal of life (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sv\'e4rtha-gatim}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
). The real interest or goal of life is to return home, back to Godhead. To enable one to fulfill this purpose, there are so many Vedic literatures, including }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Upani\'f1ads, Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, Mah\'e4bh\'e4rata}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 R\'e4m\'e4ya\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 One should take lessons from these Vedic literatures and learn how to practice }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Then one's life will be perfect. The body is important as long as it has consciousness. Without consciousness, the body i
s merely a lump of matter. Therefore, to return home, back to Godhead, one must change his consciousness from material consciousness to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. One's consciousness is the cause of material bondage, but if this consciousness is purified by }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti-yoga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  one can then understand the falsity of his }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 up\'e4dhi,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  his designations as Indian, American, Hindu, Muslim, Christian and so on. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Sarvop\'e4dhi-vinirmukta\'e0 tat-paratvena nirmalam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 One must forget these designations and use this consciousness only for the service of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore if one takes advantage of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement, his life is certainly successful.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.15.42
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 42
