\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 gari\'f1\'f6ha-cara\'eba}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the lotus feet of the superiors (namely the spiritual master and his predecessors); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 arcanay\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by serving; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 ni\'e7\'e4tam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash sharpened; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na-asim}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the sword or weapon of knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 acyuta-bala\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by the transcendental strength of K\'e5\'f1\'eba; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dadhat}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash holding; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 asta-\'e7atru\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
until the enemy is defeated; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sva-\'e4nanda-tu\'f1\'f6a\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash being fully self-satisfied by transcendental bliss; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 upa\'e7\'e4nta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
the consciousness being cleansed of all material contamination; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 idam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash this body; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vijahy\'e4t}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash one should give up.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
As long as one has to accept a material body, with its different parts and paraphernalia, which are not fully under one's control, one must have the lotus feet of his superiors, namely his spiritual master and the spiritual master's prede
cessors. By their mercy, one can sharpen the sword of knowledge, and with the power of the Supreme Personality of Godhead's mercy one must then conquer the enemies mentioned above. In this way, the devotee should be able to merge into his own transcendent
al bliss, and then he may give up his body and resume his spiritual identity.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (4.9) the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
 punar janma\line naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "One who knows the transcendental 
nature of My appearance and activities does not, upon leaving the body, take his birth again in this material world, but attains My eternal abode, O Arjuna." This is the highest perfection of life, and the human body is meant for this purpose. It is said 
in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (11.20.17):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e5-deham \'e4dya\'e0 sulabha\'e0 sudurlabha\'e0\line plava\'e0 sukalpa\'e0 guru-kar\'eb
adh\'e4ram\line may\'e4nuk\'fclena nabhasvaterita\'e0\line pum\'e4n bhav\'e4bdhi\'e0 na taret sa \'e4tma-h\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 This human form of body is a most valuable boat, and the spiritual master is the captain, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-kar\'ebadh\'e4ram,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  to guide the boat in plying across the ocean of nescience. The instruction of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is a favorable breeze. One must use all these facilities to cross over the ocean of nescience. Since the spiritual master is the captain, one must serve 
the spiritual master very sincerely so that by his mercy one will be able to get the mercy of the Supreme Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 A significant word here is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acyuta-bala\'f9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The spiritual master is certainly very merciful to his disciples, and consequently by satisfying him a devotee gets strength from the Supreme Personality of Godhead. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu therefore says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pras\'e4de p\'e4ya bhakti-lat\'e4-b\'e9ja:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 one must first please the spiritual master, and then one automatically pleases K\'e5\'f1\'eba and ge
ts the strength with which to cross the ocean of nescience. If one seriously desires to return home, back to Godhead, one must therefore become strong enough by pleasing the spiritual master, for thus one gets the weapon with which to conquer the enemy, a
nd one also gets the grace of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Simply getting the weapon of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4na}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 is insufficient. One must sharpen the weapon by serving the spiritual master and adhering to his instructions. Then the candidate will get the mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhea
d. In general warfare one must take help from his chariot and horses in order to conquer his enemy, and after conquering his enemies he may give up the chariot and its paraphernalia. Similarly, as long as one has a human body, one should fully use it to o
btain the highest perfection of life, namely going back home, back to Godhead.
\par The perfection of knowledge is certainly to become transcendentally situated (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4219903 brahma-bh\'fcta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). As the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 (18.54):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4\line na \'e7ocati na k\'e4\'eck\'f1ati\line sama\'f9
 sarve\'f1u bh\'fcte\'f1u\line mad-bhakti\'e0 labhate par\'e4m
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"One who is transcendentally situated at once realizes the Supreme Brahman and becomes fully joyful. He never laments nor desires to have anything; he is equally disposed toward all living 
entities. In that state he attains pure devotional service." Simply by cultivating knowledge as the impersonalists do, one cannot get out of the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 One must attain the platform of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti\line y\'e4v\'e4n ya\'e7 c\'e4smi tattvata\'f9\line tato
 m\'e4\'e0 tattvato j\'ef\'e4tv\'e4\line vi\'e7ate tad-anantaram
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"One can understand the Supreme Personality as He is only by devotional service. And when one is in full consciousness of the Supreme Lord by such devotion, he can enter into the kingdom of God." (Bg. 18.55) Unless
 one has attained the stage of devotional service and the mercy of the spiritual master and K\'e5\'f1\'eba, there is a possibility that one may fall down and again accept a material body. Therefore K\'e5\'f1\'eba stresses in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (4.9):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
 punar janma\line naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"One who knows the transcendental nature of My appearance and activities does not, upon leaving the body, take his birth again in this material world, but attains My eternal abode, O Arjuna."
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tattvata\'f9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 meaning "in reality," is very important. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Tato m\'e4\'e0 tattvato j\'ef\'e4tv\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Unless one understands K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a in truth by the mercy of the spiritual master, one is not free to give up his material body. As it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4ruhya k\'e5cchre\'eba para\'e0 pada\'e0 tata\'f9 patanty adho 'n\'e4d\'e5ta-yu\'f1mad-a\'ecghraya\'f9:}{
\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 if one neglects to serve the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, one cannot become free from the material clutches simply by knowledge. Even if one attains the stage of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
brahma-padam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  merging in Brahman, without }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 he is prone to fall down. One must be very careful in regard to the danger of falling down again into material bondage. The only insurance is to come to the stage of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bhakti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 from which one is sure not to fall. Then one is free from the activities of the material world. In summary, as stated by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, one must get in touch with a bona fide spiritual master coming in the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 parampar\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, for by his mercy and instructions one is able to get strength from K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Thus 
one engages in devotional service and attains the ultimate goal of life, the lotus feet of Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par Significant in this verse are the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4n\'e4sim acyuta-bala\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 J\'ef\'e4n\'e4sim,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  the sword of knowledge, is given by K\'e5
\'f1\'eba, and when one serves the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and K\'e5\'f1\'eba in order to hold the sword of K\'e5\'f1\'eba's instructions, Balar\'e4ma gives one strength. Balar\'e4ma is Nity\'e4nanda. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Vrajendra-nandana yei, \'e7ac\'e9-suta haila sei, balar\'e4ma ha-ila nit\'e4i.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  This }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 bala}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \emdash Balar\'e4ma\emdash comes with \'c7r\'e9
 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, and both of Them are so merciful that in this age of Kali one may very easily take shelter of Their lotus feet. They come especially to deliver the fallen souls of this age. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid6694782 P}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4p\'e9 t\'e4p\'e9 yata chila, hari-n\'e4me uddh\'e4rila.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  Their weapon is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 sa\'eck\'e9rtana, hari-n\'e4ma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 Thus one should accept the sword of knowledge from K\'e5\'f1\'eba and be strong with the mercy of Balar\'e4ma. We are therefore worshiping K\'e5\'f1\'eba-Balar\'e4ma in V\'e5nd\'e4vana. In the }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Mu\'eb\'f2aka Upani\'f1ad}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (3.2.4) it is said:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 n\'e4yam \'e4tm\'e4 bala-h\'e9nena labhyo\line na ca pram\'e4d\'e4t tapaso v\'e4py ali\'ecg
\'e4t\line etair up\'e4yair yatate yas tu vidv\'e4\'e0s\line tasyai\'f1a \'e4tm\'e4 vi\'e7ate brahma-dh\'e4ma
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 One cannot attain the goal of life without the mercy of Balar\'e4ma. \'c7r\'e9 Narottama d\'e4
sa \'d6h\'e4kura therefore says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nit\'e4iyera karu\'eb\'e4 habe, vraje r\'e4dh\'e4-k\'e5\'f1\'eba p\'e4be:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  when one receives the mercy of Balar\'e4ma, Nity\'e4nanda, 
one can attain the lotus feet of R\'e4dh\'e4 and K\'e5\'f1\'eba very easily.
\par }\pard\plain \s320\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 se sambandha n\'e4hi y\'e4ra,     b\'e5th\'e4 janma gela t\'e4ra,\line vidy\'e4-kule hi karibe t
\'e4ra
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 If one has no connection with Nit\'e4i, Balar\'e4
ma, then even though one is a very learned scholar or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or has taken birth in a very respectable family, these assets will not help him. We must therefore conquer the enemies of K\'e5
\'f1\'eba consciousness with the strength received from Balar\'e4ma.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.15.46
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 TEXT 46
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s489\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f75\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 NaaeceTa( Pa[MataMaSaidiNd]YavaiJaSaUTaa\line  NaqTvaeTPaQa& ivzYadSYauzu iNai+aPaiNTa )\line 
Tae dSYav" SahYaSaUTaMaMau& TaMaae_NDae\line  Sa&SaarkU-Pa o\'e5Ma*TYau>aYae i+aPaiNTa )) 46 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 nocet pramattam asad-indriya-v\'e4ji-s\'fct\'e4
\par n\'e9tvotpatha\'e0 vi\'f1aya-dasyu\'f1u nik\'f1ipanti
\par te dasyava\'f9 sahaya-s\'fctam amu\'e0 tamo 'ndhe
\par sa\'e0s\'e4ra-k\'fcpa uru-m\'e5tyu-bhaye k\'f1ipanti
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid30033 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb120\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 nocet}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
if we do not follow the instructions of Acyuta, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and do not take shelter of Balar\'e4ma; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 pramattam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash careless, inattentive; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 asat}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash which are always prone to material consciousness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 indriya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 v\'e4ji}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash acting as the horses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 s
\'fct\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the chariot driver (intelligence); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 n\'e9tv\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash bringing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 utpatham}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash 
to the roadway of material desire; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 vi\'f1aya}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the sense objects; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dasyu\'f1u}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash in the hands of the plunderers; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 
nik\'f1ipanti}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash throw; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 te}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash those; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dasyava\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash plunderers; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash with; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 haya-s\'fctam}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash the horses and chariot driver; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 amum}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash all of them; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 tama\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 
\emdash dark; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 andhe}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash blind; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa\'e0s\'e4ra-k\'fcpe}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash into the well of material existence; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 uru}{
\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash great; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 m\'e5tyu-bhaye}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash fear of death; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 k\'f1ipanti}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash throw.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
Otherwise, if one does not take shelter of Acyuta and Baladeva, then the senses, acting a
s the horses, and the intelligence, acting as the driver, both being prone to material contamination, inattentively bring the body, which acts as the chariot, to the path of sense gratification. When one is thus attracted again by the rogues of vi\'f1aya
\emdash eating, sleeping and mating\emdash the horses and chariot driver are thrown into the blinding dark well of material existence, and one is again put into a dangerous and extremely fearful situation of repeated birth and death.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Without the protection of Gaura-Nit\'e4i\emdash K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Balar\'e4ma\emdash 
one cannot get out of the dark well of ignorance in material existence. This is indicated here by the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 nocet,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 which means that one will always remain in the dark well of material existence. The living entity must get strength from Nit\'e4i-Gaura, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba-Balar\'e4ma. Without the mercy of Nit\'e4
i-Gaura, there is no way to come out of this dark well of ignorance. As stated in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'c4di}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  1.2):
