the beginning of life (the purificatory process of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na,}{\fs28\insrsid30033  performed when the father begets a child by discharging semen into the womb of the mother); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 \'e7ma\'e7
\'e4na-antai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash and at death, when the body is put into a crematorium and burnt to ashes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa\'e0sk\'e4rai\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash by such purificatory processes; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 sa\'e0sk\'e5ta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash purified; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 dvija\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid30033 \emdash a twice-born }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'eba;}{\fs28\insrsid30033  }{
