a [dvija] gains his life by the grace of his parents through the process of purification known as garbh\'e4dh\'e4na. There are also other processes of purification, until the end of life, when the funeral ceremony [antye\'f1\'f6i-kriy\'e4
] is performed. Thus in due course a qualified br\'e4hma\'eba becomes uninterested in materialistic activities and sac
rifices, but he offers the sensual sacrifices, in full knowledge, into the working senses, which are illuminated by the fire of knowledge.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
