\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Prav\'e5tti-m\'e4rga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or the i
nclination to stay in the material world to enjoy varieties of sense gratification, has been explained in the previous verse. Now, in this verse, it is explained that one who has perfect brahminical knowledge rejects the process of elevation to higher pla
nets and accepts }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  in other words, he prepares himself to go back home, back to Godhead. Those who are not }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  but atheists do not know what is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prav\'e5tti-m\'e4rga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 they simply want to obtain pleasure at any cost. Our K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is therefore training devotees to give up the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 prav\'e5tti-m\'e4rga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and accept the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  in order to return home, back to Godhead. This is a little difficult to understand, but it is very easy if one takes to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness serio
usly and tries to understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba. A K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious person can understand that performing }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  according to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  system is a useless waste of time and that merely giving up the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  and accepting the process of speculation is also unfruitful. Therefore Narottama d\'e4
sa \'d6h\'e4kura has sung in his }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid668466 P}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 rema-bhakti-candrik\'e4:
