\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid30033 
Although one may consider the reflection of the sun from a mirror to be false, it has its factual existence. Accordingly, to prove by speculative knowledge that there is no reality would be extremely difficult.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid30033 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
The impersonalists try to prove that the varieties in the vision of the empiric philosopher are false. The impersonalist philosophy, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 vivarta-v\'e4da,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  genera
lly cites the acceptance of a rope to be a snake as an example of this fact. According to this example, the varieties within our vision are false, just as a rope seen to be a snake is false. The Vai\'f1\'eb
avas say, however, that although the idea that the rope 
is a snake is false, the snake is not false; one has experience of a snake in reality, and therefore he knows that although the representation of the rope as a snake is false or illusory, there is a snake in reality. Similarly, this world, which is full o
f varieties, is not false; it is a reflection of the reality in the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha world, the spiritual world.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
The reflection of the sun from a mirror is nothing but light within darkness. Thus although it is not exactly sunlight, without the sunlight the reflec
tion would be impossible. Similarly, the varieties of this world would be impossible unless there were a real prototype in the spiritual world. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9
 philosopher cannot understand this, but a real philosopher must be convinced that light is not possible at all without a background of sunlight. Thus the jugglery of words used by the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9
 philosopher to prove that this material world is false may amaze inexperienced children, but a man with full knowledge knows perfectly well that there cannot be any existence without K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava insists on the platform of somehow or other accepting K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 tasm\'e4t ken\'e4p}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid12063106 y up\'e4yena mana\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'ebe nive\'e7ayet}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ).
\par When we raise our unmixed faith to the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, everything is revealed. K\'e5\'f1\'eba also says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (7.1):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mayy \'e4sakta-man\'e4\'f9 p\'e4rtha\line yoga\'e0 yu\'efjan mad-\'e4\'e7raya\'f9\line asa
\'e0\'e7aya\'e0 samagra\'e0 m\'e4\'e0\line yath\'e4 j\'ef\'e4syasi tac ch\'e5\'ebu
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "Now hear, O son of P\'e5th\'e4 [Arjuna], how by practicing }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  in full consciousness of Me, with mind attached to Me, you can know Me in full, free from doubt." Simply by raising one's staunch faith in K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His instructions, one can understand reality without a doubt (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 asa\'e0\'e7aya\'e0 samagra\'e0 m\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 ). One can understand how K\'e5\'f1\'eba's material and spiritual energies are working and how 
He is present everywhere although everything is not Him. This philosophy of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acintya-bhed\'e4bheda,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  inconceivable oneness and difference, is the perfect philosophy enunciated by the Vai\'f1\'eb
avas. Everything is an emanation from K\'e5\'f1\'eba, but it is not that everythin
g must therefore be worshiped. Speculative knowledge cannot give us reality as it is, but will continue to be nefariously imperfect. So-called scientists try to prove that there is no God and that everything is happening because of the laws of nature, but
 this is imperfect knowledge because nothing can work unless directed by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is explained in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  (9.10) by the Lord Himself:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 may\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9\line s\'fcyate sacar\'e4caram\line hetun\'e4
nena kaunteya\line jagad viparivartate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 "This material nature is working under My direction, O son of Kunt\'e9
, and it is producing all moving and unmoving beings. By its rule this manifestation is created and annihilated again and again." In this regard, \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya gives this note: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 durgha\'f6atv\'e4
d arthatvena parame\'e7vare\'ebaiva kalpitam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  The background of everything is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, V\'e4sudeva. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 V\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  This can be understood by a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mah\'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  who is perfect in knowledge. Such a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 mah\'e4tm\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  is rarely seen.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.15.59
