A forest is certainly a transformation of the earth, but one tree does not depend on another tree; if one is cut down, 
this does not mean that the others are cut down. Therefore, the forest is neither a combination nor a transformation of the trees. The best explanation is given by K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarva\'e0\line jagad avyakta-m\'fcrtin\'e4\line mat-sth\'e4
ni sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni\line na c\'e4ha\'e0 te\'f1v avasthita\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
"By Me, in My unmanifested form, this entire universe is pervaded. All beings are in Me, but I am not in them." (Bg. 9.4) Everything is an expansion of K\'e5\'f1\'eba's energy. As it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 par\'e4sya \'e7
aktir vividhaiva \'e7r\'fcyate: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
the Lord has multi-energies, which are expressed in different ways. The energies are existing, and the Supreme Personality of Godhead also exists simultaneously; because everything is His energy, He is simultaneously one with everything and differe
nt from everything. Thus our speculative theories that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 \'e4tm\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 
 the living force, is a combination of matter, that matter is a transformation of the soul, or that the body is part of the soul are all insubstantial.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 Since all the Lord's energies are simultaneo
usly existing, one must understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead. But although He is everything, He is not present in everything. The Lord must be worshiped in His original form as K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. He can also present Himself in any one of His various expanded 
energies. When we worship the Deity of the Lord in the temple, the Deity appears to be stone or wood. Now, because the Supreme Lord does not have a material body, He is not stone or wood, yet stone and wood are not different from Him. Thus by worshiping s
tone or wood we get no result, but when the stone and wood are represented in the Lord's original form, by worshiping the Deity we get the desired result. This is supported by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu's philosophy, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033 acintya-bhed\'e4bheda,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid30033  which explains how the Lord can present Himself everywhere and anywhere in a form of His energy to accept service from the devotee.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid30033 SB 7.15.60
